            "\n",
            "Cell: 0\n",
            "Matched terms: ['InceptionResnetV1', 'VGGFace2', 'MTCNN', 'alignment']\n",
            "## 3. Research Objective\n",
            "\n",
            "To evaluate the behaviour of embedding-level drift detectors using 512-dimensional face-recognition embeddings extracted with FaceNet pretrained on VGGFace2.\n",
            "## 4. Research Questions\n",
            "- Dataset: Labeled Faces in the Wild (LFW).\n",
            "- Face detector and alignment: MTCNN.\n",
            "- Face-recognition model: InceptionResnetV1.\n",
            "- Pretrained weights: VGGFace2.\n",
            "- Embedding dimension: 512.\n",
            "- Framework: PyTorch and facenet-pytorch.\n",
            "## 7. Experimental Methodology\n",
            "The experiment will use identity-aware data partitioning, face detection and alignment, embedding extraction, independent threshold calibration, control evaluation and controlled drift evaluation.\n",
            "The precise partitioning protocol, environmental transformations, detector configurations and evaluation metrics will be finalised before generating the experimental dataset.\n",
            "\n",
            "Cell: 3\n",
            "Matched terms: ['InceptionResnetV1', 'VGGFace2', 'MTCNN', 'alignment']\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Initialise the MTCNN face detector and pretrained FaceNet recognition model for extracting genuine facial embeddings.\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Import the required FaceNet components.\n",
            "2. Initialise MTCNN for face detection and alignment.\n",
            "3. Load InceptionResnetV1 with VGGFace2 pretrained weights.\n",
            "4. Configure the model for evaluation.\n",
            "5. Verify the expected embedding dimension.\n",
            "### Model Configuration\n",
            "- Face detector: MTCNN\n",
            "- Recognition model: InceptionResnetV1\n",
            "- Pretrained weights: VGGFace2\n",
            "- Expected embedding dimension: 512\n",
            "- Execution device: CPU\n",
            "### Validation Criteria\n",
            "- Successful MTCNN initialisation.\n",
            "- Successful FaceNet model loading.\n",
            "- Confirmation of the 512-dimensional embedding output.\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. MTCNN face detection and alignment were initialised, the pretrained InceptionResnetV1 model with VGGFace2 weights was loaded, and the model was configured for evaluation. The expected 512-dimensional embedding configuration was verified.\n",
            "\n",
            "Cell: 4\n",
            "Matched terms: ['InceptionResnetV1', 'VGGFace2', 'MTCNN']\n",
            "import torch\n",
            "import torchvision\n",
            "from facenet_pytorch import MTCNN, InceptionResnetV1\n",
            "\n",
            "# Configure execution device\n",
            "device = torch.device(\"cpu\")\n",
            "# Initialise MTCNN face detector\n",
            "mtcnn = MTCNN(\n",
            "    image_size=160,\n",
            "    margin=0,\n",
            "    keep_all=False,\n",
            "# Load pretrained FaceNet model\n",
            "facenet = InceptionResnetV1(\n",
            "    pretrained=\"vggface2\"\n",
            ").eval().to(device)\n",
            "# Verify model configuration\n",
            "print(\"MTCNN initialised successfully.\")\n",
            "print(\"FaceNet model initialised successfully.\")\n",
            "print(\"Pretrained weights: VGGFace2\")\n",
            "print(\"Execution device:\", device)\n",
            "print(\"Embedding dimension:\", facenet.last_linear.out_features)\n",
            "\n",
            "Cell: 5\n",
            "Matched terms: ['MTCNN', 'alignment']\n",
            "1. Retrieve a sample face image.\n",
            "2. Load the image using the PIL library.\n",
            "3. Apply MTCNN for face detection and alignment.\n",
            "4. Pass the aligned face through the pretrained FaceNet model.\n",
            "5. Extract the 512-dimensional facial embedding.\n",
            "6. Validate the embedding shape, numerical values and L2 norm.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. The sample face image was downloaded and loaded, MTCNN successfully detected and aligned the face, and the pretrained FaceNet model generated a 512-dimensional embedding. Numerical validation confirmed that all embedding values were finite and the L2 norm was 1.0.\n",
            "\n",
            "Cell: 6\n",
            "Matched terms: ['MTCNN']\n",
            "\n",
            "# Detect and align face\n",
            "face_tensor = mtcnn(image)\n",
            "if face_tensor is None:\n",
            "    raise ValueError(\"No face detected in the sample image.\")\n",
            "\n",
            "Cell: 10\n",
            "Matched terms: ['Resize']\n",
            "lfw_dataset = fetch_lfw_people(\n",
            "    data_home=\"/content/lfw_data\",\n",
            "    resize=1.0,\n",
            "    min_faces_per_person=20,\n",
            "    color=True,\n",
            "    download_if_missing=True\n",
            "\n",
            "Cell: 15\n",
            "Matched terms: ['InceptionResnetV1', 'VGGFace2', 'MTCNN', 'alignment']\n",
            "## Step 8 — Face Alignment and Embedding Extraction\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Extract genuine 512-dimensional facial embeddings from the LFW dataset using the pretrained FaceNet model.\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Process reference, calibration and evaluation images separately.\n",
            "2. Apply MTCNN for face detection and alignment.\n",
            "3. Generate facial embeddings using InceptionResnetV1 pretrained on VGGFace2.\n",
            "4. Preserve the corresponding identity labels and partition assignments.\n",
            "5. Record images for which face detection fails.\n",
            "6. Validate embedding dimensions and numerical integrity.\n",
            "### Embedding Configuration\n",
            "- Recognition model: InceptionResnetV1.\n",
            "- Pretrained weights: VGGFace2.\n",
            "- Input face resolution: 160 × 160.\n",
            "- Embedding dimension: 512.\n",
            "- Normalisation: L2-normalised FaceNet embeddings.\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed after recovery. MTCNN was used to detect and align faces, and the pretrained InceptionResnetV1 model (VGGFace2) generated 512-dimensional, L2-normalised embeddings.\n",
            "Reference partition: 1,460 successful embeddings and 17 failed face detections.\n",
            "Calibration partition: 568 successful embeddings and 10 failed face detections.\n",
            "\n",
            "Cell: 16\n",
            "Matched terms: ['MTCNN']\n",
            "\n",
            "        # Detect and align face\n",
            "        face_tensor = mtcnn(image)\n",
