            "===========================================================================\n",
            "EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 2.6.14: EXACT PIPELINE RECOVERY\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 0\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# Experiment 18: Genuine Face-Recognition Embedding Validation\n",
            "\n",
            "## 1. Research Background\n",
            "\n",
            "Previous experiments evaluated embedding-level drift detection using synthetic distributions and image-derived feature representations. However, generic image features do not necessarily represent the characteristics of genuine face-recognition systems.\n",
            "\n",
            "This experiment extends the existing research by evaluating embedding-level drift detection using a pretrained face-recognition model.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 2. Problem Statement\n",
            "\n",
            "The reliability of statistical drift detectors must be investigated using genuine face-recognition representations rather than relying exclusively on synthetic distributions or generic image features.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 3. Research Objective\n",
            "\n",
            "To evaluate the behaviour of embedding-level drift detectors using 512-dimensional face-recognition embeddings extracted with FaceNet pretrained on VGGFace2.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 4. Research Questions\n",
            "\n",
            "1. Can the existing embedding-level drift detection framework operate on genuine face-recognition embeddings?\n",
            "2. How do controlled environmental changes affect the resulting face embeddings?\n",
            "3. Can statistical detectors distinguish embedding distribution changes from stable operating conditions?\n",
            "4. How reliably can false alarms and detection sensitivity be measured under independent evaluation?\n",
            "\n",
            "## 5. Research Hypotheses\n",
            "\n",
            "**H1:** Controlled changes in face-image acquisition conditions produce measurable changes in FaceNet embedding distributions.\n",
            "\n",
            "**H2:** Embedding-level statistical detectors can identify some of these distribution changes under independently calibrated thresholds.\n",
            "\n",
            "**H3:** Detection performance varies according to the type and magnitude of the environmental change.\n",
            "\n",
            "These hypotheses will be evaluated experimentally and will not be treated as established findings.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 6. Dataset and Model\n",
            "\n",
            "- Dataset: Labeled Faces in the Wild (LFW).\n",
            "- Face detector and alignment: MTCNN.\n",
            "- Face-recognition model: InceptionResnetV1.\n",
            "- Pretrained weights: VGGFace2.\n",
            "- Embedding dimension: 512.\n",
            "- Framework: PyTorch and facenet-pytorch.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 7. Experimental Methodology\n",
            "\n",
            "The experiment will use identity-aware data partitioning, face detection and alignment, embedding extraction, independent threshold calibration, control evaluation and controlled drift evaluation.\n",
            "\n",
            "The precise partitioning protocol, environmental transformations, detector configurations and evaluation metrics will be finalised before generating the experimental dataset.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 8. Evaluation Metrics\n",
            "\n",
            "- False-alarm rate.\n",
            "- Detection rate.\n",
            "- Detection delay.\n",
            "- Precision and recall where appropriate.\n",
            "- Confidence intervals.\n",
            "- Computational performance where applicable.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 9. Reproducibility\n",
            "\n",
            "The experiment will record model configuration, dataset provenance, random seeds, software versions, preprocessing settings and generated result artifacts.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 10. Scientific Scope and Limitations\n",
            "\n",
            "Successful embedding extraction does not establish face-recognition accuracy or reliable drift detection. This experiment evaluates representation-level distribution changes and detector behaviour. It does not independently establish biometric identification performance, fairness, security or deployment readiness.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
