            "CELL INDEX: 15\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 8 — Face Alignment and Embedding Extraction\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Extract genuine 512-dimensional facial embeddings from the LFW dataset using the pretrained FaceNet model.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Process reference, calibration and evaluation images separately.\n",
            "2. Apply MTCNN for face detection and alignment.\n",
            "3. Generate facial embeddings using InceptionResnetV1 pretrained on VGGFace2.\n",
            "4. Preserve the corresponding identity labels and partition assignments.\n",
            "5. Record images for which face detection fails.\n",
            "6. Validate embedding dimensions and numerical integrity.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Embedding Configuration\n",
            "- Recognition model: InceptionResnetV1.\n",
            "- Pretrained weights: VGGFace2.\n",
            "- Input face resolution: 160 × 160.\n",
            "- Embedding dimension: 512.\n",
            "- Normalisation: L2-normalised FaceNet embeddings.\n",
            "- Execution device: CPU.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Validation Criteria\n",
            "- Successful embedding extraction.\n",
            "- Consistent 512-dimensional output.\n",
            "- Finite embedding values.\n",
            "- Recorded face-detection failures.\n",
            "- Preservation of identity and partition information.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Scope\n",
            "This stage generates face-recognition representations. It does not independently measure recognition accuracy or establish drift detection performance.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed after recovery. MTCNN was used to detect and align faces, and the pretrained InceptionResnetV1 model (VGGFace2) generated 512-dimensional, L2-normalised embeddings.\n",
            "\n",
            "Reference partition: 1,460 successful embeddings and 17 failed face detections.\n",
            "Calibration partition: 568 successful embeddings and 10 failed face detections.\n",
            "Evaluation partition: 956 successful embeddings and 12 failed face detections.\n",
            "\n",
            "The initial evaluation extraction was interrupted during CPU-based processing. It was subsequently resumed and completed successfully. Face-detection failures were recorded for each partition.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 16\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['MTCNN(', 'mtcnn(', 'facenet(', 'torch.no_grad', 'embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "import torch\n",
            "from tqdm.auto import tqdm\n",
            "\n",
            "def extract_embeddings(indices, partition_name):\n",
            "    embeddings = []\n",
            "    labels = []\n",
            "    failed_indices = []\n",
            "\n",
            "    for idx in tqdm(indices, desc=f\"Processing {partition_name}\"):\n",
            "\n",
            "        # Convert image to PIL RGB format\n",
            "        image_array = lfw_dataset.images[idx]\n",
            "        image = Image.fromarray(\n",
            "            np.clip(image_array * 255, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "        # Detect and align face\n",
            "        face_tensor = mtcnn(image)\n",
            "\n",
            "        if face_tensor is None:\n",
            "            failed_indices.append(idx)\n",
            "            continue\n",
            "\n",
            "        # Extract FaceNet embedding\n",
            "        face_tensor = face_tensor.unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n",
            "\n",
            "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
            "            embedding = facenet(face_tensor)\n",
            "\n",
            "        embedding_np = embedding.cpu().numpy()[0]\n",
            "\n",
            "        embeddings.append(embedding_np)\n",
            "        labels.append(lfw_dataset.target[idx])\n",
            "\n",
            "    if embeddings:\n",
            "        embeddings = np.asarray(embeddings, dtype=np.float32)\n",
            "        labels = np.asarray(labels)\n",
            "    else:\n",
            "        embeddings = np.empty((0, 512), dtype=np.float32)\n",
            "        labels = np.empty((0,), dtype=int)\n",
            "\n",
            "    print(f\"\\n{partition_name} results:\")\n",
            "    print(\"Successful embeddings:\", len(embeddings))\n",
            "    print(\"Failed face detections:\", len(failed_indices))\n",
            "\n",
            "    return embeddings, labels, failed_indices\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "# Extract embeddings separately\n",
            "reference_embeddings, reference_labels, reference_failures = (\n",
            "    extract_embeddings(reference_indices, \"Reference\")\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "calibration_embeddings, calibration_labels, calibration_failures = (\n",
            "    extract_embeddings(calibration_indices, \"Calibration\")\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "evaluation_embeddings, evaluation_labels, evaluation_failures = (\n",
            "    extract_embeddings(evaluation_indices, \"Evaluation\")\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 17\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "### Execution Issue — Interrupted Evaluation Embedding Extraction\n",
            "\n",
            "**Observed Error:** `KeyboardInterrupt`\n",
            "\n",
            "#### Description\n",
            "The embedding extraction process was manually interrupted during the evaluation partition while the FaceNet model was performing CPU-based inference.\n",
            "\n",
            "#### Results Before Interruption\n",
            "\n",
            "| Partition | Images processed | Successful embeddings | Failed detections |\n",
            "|---|---:|---:|---:|\n",
            "| Reference | 1,477 | 1,460 | 17 |\n",
            "| Calibration | 578 | 568 | 10 |\n",
            "| Evaluation | 367 of 968 | Incomplete | Incomplete |\n",
            "\n",
            "#### Cause\n",
            "The evaluation partition required additional CPU processing time. Execution was interrupted before the partition could be completed.\n",
            "\n",
            "#### Impact\n",
            "- Reference embeddings were successfully extracted.\n",
            "- Calibration embeddings were successfully extracted.\n",
            "- Evaluation embeddings remain incomplete.\n",
            "- Complete three-partition validation cannot yet be performed.\n",
            "\n",
            "#### Corrective Action\n",
            "Resume evaluation embedding extraction without repeating the completed reference and calibration partitions.\n",
            "\n",
            "#### Status\n",
            "**Partially completed — corrective action pending.**\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 18\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# Resume evaluation embedding extraction only\n",
            "\n",
            "evaluation_embeddings, evaluation_labels, evaluation_failures = (\n",
            "    extract_embeddings(evaluation_indices, \"Evaluation\")\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nEvaluation extraction completed.\")\n",
            "print(\"Successful embeddings:\", len(evaluation_embeddings))\n",
            "print(\"Failed face detections:\", len(evaluation_failures))\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 19\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 9 — Embedding Quality and Integrity Validation\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Validate the quality and numerical integrity of the extracted FaceNet embeddings across all three dataset partitions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Verify the dimensions of each embedding matrix.\n",
            "2. Check for NaN and infinite values.\n",
            "3. Calculate the L2 norm of each embedding.\n",
            "4. Verify embedding-label alignment.\n",
            "5. Confirm that all embeddings contain 512 features.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Validation Criteria\n",
            "- Consistent embedding dimensions.\n",
            "- No NaN or infinite values.\n",
            "- L2 norms approximately equal to 1.0.\n",
            "- Matching numbers of embeddings and identity labels.\n",
            "- No empty embedding partitions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. Embedding quality and numerical integrity were validated across all three partitions.\n",
            "\n",
            "Reference: (1,460, 512)\n",
            "Calibration: (568, 512)\n",
            "Evaluation: (956, 512)\n",
            "\n",
            "All embedding matrices contain 512 features. All values are finite, embedding counts match their corresponding identity-label counts, and all L2 norms are approximately 1.0. The minimum and maximum observed norms were 0.9999999 and 1.0000001, respectively.\n",
            "\n",
            "All embedding integrity checks passed.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 20\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "\n",
            "partitions = {\n",
            "    \"Reference\": (reference_embeddings, reference_labels),\n",
            "    \"Calibration\": (calibration_embeddings, calibration_labels),\n",
            "    \"Evaluation\": (evaluation_embeddings, evaluation_labels)\n",
            "}\n",
            "\n",
            "for name, (embeddings, labels) in partitions.items():\n",
            "\n",
            "    norms = np.linalg.norm(embeddings, axis=1)\n",
            "\n",
            "    print(f\"\\n{name} partition\")\n",
            "    print(\"-\" * 40)\n",
            "    print(\"Embedding shape:\", embeddings.shape)\n",
            "    print(\"Label shape:\", labels.shape)\n",
            "    print(\"All values finite:\", np.isfinite(embeddings).all())\n",
            "    print(\"Embedding-label alignment:\", len(embeddings) == len(labels))\n",
            "    print(\"Mean L2 norm:\", norms.mean())\n",
            "    print(\"Minimum L2 norm:\", norms.min())\n",
            "    print(\"Maximum L2 norm:\", norms.max())\n",
            "\n",
            "    assert embeddings.shape[1] == 512\n",
            "    assert len(embeddings) == len(labels)\n",
            "    assert np.isfinite(embeddings).all()\n",
            "    assert np.allclose(norms, 1.0, atol=1e-4)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nAll embedding integrity checks passed.\")\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 21\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 10 — Embedding Storage and Experiment Reproducibility\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Save the extracted FaceNet embeddings, identity labels, partition information and failed detection indices for reproducibility and subsequent analysis.\n",
            "\n",
