            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 15 — Controlled Illumination Drift Experiment\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Evaluate the effect of controlled illumination changes on genuine FaceNet face-recognition embeddings.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Questions\n",
            "1. How does reduced illumination affect embedding representations?\n",
            "2. How does increased illumination affect embedding representations?\n",
            "3. Does illumination change produce measurable embedding-space displacement?\n",
            "4. Can embedding-level drift detectors distinguish transformed embeddings from baseline embeddings?\n",
            "\n",
            "### Experimental Design\n",
            "- Dataset: LFW evaluation partition.\n",
            "- Original images: unmodified evaluation images.\n",
            "- Transformation: controlled brightness adjustment.\n",
            "- Conditions: reduced, unchanged and increased illumination.\n",
            "- Model: InceptionResnetV1 pretrained on VGGFace2.\n",
            "- Embedding dimension: 512.\n",
            "- Comparison: paired original and transformed image embeddings.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Evaluation Metrics\n",
            "- Cosine similarity.\n",
            "- Euclidean embedding displacement.\n",
            "- Distribution-level distance.\n",
            "- Drift detection rate and false alarm rate in subsequent detector evaluation.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Scope\n",
            "This experiment evaluates controlled illumination perturbations. It does not represent naturally occurring temporal drift or establish real-world biometric deployment performance.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. The evaluation partition was inspected, and five original LFW images were visually reviewed. The partition contains 968 image indices, 956 successfully extracted embeddings and 956 corresponding labels. Sample image integrity checks passed, with finite RGB pixel values within the valid [0, 1] range.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 45\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
            "\n",
            "# Verify evaluation partition\n",
            "print(\"EVALUATION PARTITION INSPECTION\")\n",
            "print(\"-\" * 50)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Evaluation image indices:\", len(evaluation_indices))\n",
            "print(\"Evaluation embeddings:\", evaluation_embeddings.shape)\n",
            "print(\"Evaluation labels:\", evaluation_labels.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "# Select five evaluation images for visual inspection\n",
            "sample_indices = evaluation_indices[:5]\n",
            "\n",
            "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 5, figsize=(16, 4))\n",
            "\n",
            "for ax, image_index in zip(axes, sample_indices):\n",
            "\n",
            "    image = lfw_dataset.images[image_index]\n",
            "\n",
            "    ax.imshow(np.clip(image, 0, 1))\n",
            "    ax.set_title(f\"Image {image_index}\")\n",
            "    ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
            "\n",
            "plt.suptitle(\"Original LFW Evaluation Images\")\n",
