            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 15.1 — Controlled Illumination Transformation\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Generate controlled illumination variants from successfully processed evaluation images.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Transformation Conditions\n",
            "- Low illumination: brightness factor 0.5\n",
            "- Original illumination: brightness factor 1.0\n",
            "- High illumination: brightness factor 1.5\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "Apply multiplicative brightness adjustments to the original RGB images. Clip pixel values to the valid [0, 1] range.\n",
            "\n",
            "Only images with successful original FaceNet embedding extraction will be included, preserving paired comparisons.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "These are computationally generated illumination perturbations, not naturally captured lighting conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. Controlled illumination variants were generated for all 956 successfully processed evaluation images using brightness factors of 0.5, 1.0 and 1.5. All three image collections have the expected shape of (956, 125, 94, 3). Numerical integrity checks confirmed finite pixel values within the valid [0, 1] range. These transformations are computationally generated and do not represent naturally captured lighting conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 48\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
            "\n",
            "# Exclude images where original face detection failed\n",
            "successful_evaluation_indices = np.setdiff1d(\n",
            "    evaluation_indices,\n",
            "    evaluation_failures\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Confirm paired dataset size\n",
            "print(\"Successful evaluation images:\",\n",
            "      len(successful_evaluation_indices))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Original evaluation embeddings:\",\n",
            "      len(evaluation_embeddings))\n",
            "\n",
            "assert len(successful_evaluation_indices) == len(evaluation_embeddings)\n",
            "\n",
            "# Define illumination conditions\n",
            "brightness_factors = {\n",
            "    \"Low illumination\": 0.5,\n",
            "    \"Original illumination\": 1.0,\n",
            "    \"High illumination\": 1.5\n",
            "}\n",
            "\n",
            "# Generate transformed images\n",
            "illumination_images = {}\n",
            "\n",
            "for condition, factor in brightness_factors.items():\n",
            "\n",
            "    transformed = []\n",
            "\n",
            "    for image_index in successful_evaluation_indices:\n",
            "\n",
            "        original_image = lfw_dataset.images[image_index]\n",
            "\n",
            "        adjusted_image = np.clip(\n",
            "            original_image * factor,\n",
            "            0.0,\n",
            "            1.0\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "        transformed.append(adjusted_image)\n",
            "\n",
            "    illumination_images[condition] = np.asarray(transformed)\n",
            "\n",
            "    print(\n",
            "        condition,\n",
            "        illumination_images[condition].shape\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "# Visualise one image under all three conditions\n",
            "sample_position = 0\n",
            "\n",
            "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
            "\n",
            "for ax, (condition, images) in zip(\n",
            "    axes, illumination_images.items()\n",
            "):\n",
            "\n",
            "    ax.imshow(images[sample_position])\n",
            "    ax.set_title(condition)\n",
            "    ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
            "\n",
            "plt.suptitle(\"Controlled Illumination Variants\")\n",
            "plt.tight_layout()\n",
            "plt.show()\n",
            "\n",
            "# Validate generated images\n",
            "for condition, images in illumination_images.items():\n",
            "\n",
            "    print(\n",
            "        condition,\n",
            "        \"| Finite:\", np.all(np.isfinite(images)),\n",
            "        \"| Minimum:\", images.min(),\n",
            "        \"| Maximum:\", images.max()\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 49\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 15.2 — FaceNet Embedding Extraction Under Illumination Changes\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Extract 512-dimensional FaceNet embeddings from low- and high-illumination evaluation images.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Reuse the original evaluation embeddings as the baseline.\n",
            "2. Process low-illumination images using MTCNN and FaceNet.\n",
            "3. Process high-illumination images using MTCNN and FaceNet.\n",
            "4. Record face detection failures separately.\n",
            "5. Verify embedding dimensions and numerical integrity.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Experimental Conditions\n",
            "- Original: existing baseline embeddings.\n",
            "- Low illumination: brightness factor 0.5.\n",
            "- High illumination: brightness factor 1.5.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "Face detection may fail on transformed images. The final paired analysis must account for those failures rather than silently discarding them.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. FaceNet embeddings were extracted from low- and high-illumination evaluation images using MTCNN and InceptionResnetV1. The original baseline contained 956 embeddings of 512 dimensions. Low illumination produced 943 valid embeddings with 13 detection failures, while high illumination produced 897 valid embeddings with 59 detection failures. Both transformed embedding collections passed numerical integrity checks, with all values finite. Detection failures were recorded separately for subsequent paired-cohort validation.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 50\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['MTCNN(', 'mtcnn(', 'facenet(', 'torch.no_grad', 'embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "from PIL import Image\n",
            "from tqdm.auto import tqdm\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import torch\n",
            "\n",
            "def extract_transformed_embeddings(images, condition_name):\n",
            "\n",
            "    embeddings = []\n",
            "    successful_positions = []\n",
            "    failed_positions = []\n",
            "\n",
            "    for position, image in enumerate(\n",
            "        tqdm(images, desc=condition_name)\n",
            "    ):\n",
            "\n",
            "        try:\n",
            "            image_uint8 = (\n",
            "                np.clip(image, 0, 1) * 255\n",
            "            ).astype(np.uint8)\n",
            "\n",
            "            pil_image = Image.fromarray(image_uint8)\n",
            "\n",
            "            face_tensor = mtcnn(pil_image)\n",
            "\n",
            "            if face_tensor is None:\n",
            "                failed_positions.append(position)\n",
            "                continue\n",
            "\n",
            "            with torch.no_grad():\n",
            "                embedding = facenet(\n",
            "                    face_tensor.unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n",
            "                )\n",
            "\n",
            "            embedding = embedding.cpu().numpy()[0]\n",
            "\n",
            "            if not np.all(np.isfinite(embedding)):\n",
            "                failed_positions.append(position)\n",
            "                continue\n",
            "\n",
            "            embeddings.append(embedding)\n",
            "            successful_positions.append(position)\n",
            "\n",
            "        except Exception:\n",
            "            failed_positions.append(position)\n",
            "\n",
            "    return (\n",
            "        np.asarray(embeddings),\n",
            "        np.asarray(successful_positions),\n",
            "        np.asarray(failed_positions)\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "# Extract low-illumination embeddings\n",
            "low_embeddings, low_success, low_failures = (\n",
            "    extract_transformed_embeddings(\n",
            "        illumination_images[\"Low illumination\"],\n",
            "        \"Low illumination\"\n",
            "    )\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Extract high-illumination embeddings\n",
            "high_embeddings, high_success, high_failures = (\n",
            "    extract_transformed_embeddings(\n",
            "        illumination_images[\"High illumination\"],\n",
            "        \"High illumination\"\n",
            "    )\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nEMBEDDING EXTRACTION SUMMARY\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Original embeddings:\", evaluation_embeddings.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Low illumination embeddings:\", low_embeddings.shape)\n",
            "print(\"Low illumination failures:\", len(low_failures))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"High illumination embeddings:\", high_embeddings.shape)\n",
            "print(\"High illumination failures:\", len(high_failures))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nNUMERICAL VALIDATION\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Low embeddings finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(low_embeddings)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"High embeddings finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(high_embeddings)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Low successful positions:\", len(low_success))\n",
            "print(\"High successful positions:\", len(high_success))\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 51\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 15.3 — Paired Image and Identity Alignment Validation\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Establish a correctly aligned evaluation cohort across original, low-illumination and high-illumination conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Reconstruct the original successful evaluation image indices while preserving their extraction order.\n",
            "2. Identify images successfully processed under both transformed conditions.\n",
            "3. Match original embeddings with their corresponding transformed embeddings.\n",
            "4. Verify identity-label consistency across all conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Purpose\n",
            "Prevent incorrect image pairing and identity mismatches from contaminating the illumination sensitivity analysis.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. Image-to-embedding alignment and identity-label consistency were validated across original, low-illumination and high-illumination conditions. A common paired cohort of 889 images was established from 956 original, 943 low-illumination and 897 high-illumination successful extractions. All three paired embedding matrices have shape (889, 512). Identity labels were aligned, all embeddings were finite, and the dimensional consistency assertions passed.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 52\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "\n",
            "# Preserve the original extraction order\n",
            "evaluation_failure_set = set(evaluation_failures)\n",
            "\n",
            "ordered_original_indices = np.array([\n",
            "    idx for idx in evaluation_indices\n",
            "    if idx not in evaluation_failure_set\n",
            "])\n",
            "\n",
            "# Verify original image-to-embedding alignment\n",
            "assert len(ordered_original_indices) == len(evaluation_embeddings)\n",
            "\n",
            "original_labels_check = lfw_dataset.target[\n",
            "    ordered_original_indices\n",
            "]\n",
            "\n",
            "assert np.array_equal(\n",
            "    original_labels_check,\n",
            "    evaluation_labels\n",
            "), \"Original image and embedding labels are misaligned.\"\n",
            "\n",
            "# Find positions successful under both transformations\n",
            "common_positions = np.intersect1d(\n",
            "    low_success,\n",
            "    high_success\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Match all three conditions\n",
            "paired_original_embeddings = evaluation_embeddings[\n",
            "    common_positions\n",
            "]\n",
            "\n",
            "paired_low_embeddings = low_embeddings[\n",
            "    np.searchsorted(low_success, common_positions)\n",
            "]\n",
            "\n",
            "paired_high_embeddings = high_embeddings[\n",
            "    np.searchsorted(high_success, common_positions)\n",
            "]\n",
            "\n",
            "# Verify identity consistency\n",
            "paired_labels = evaluation_labels[common_positions]\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"PAIRED COHORT VALIDATION\")\n",
            "print(\"-\" * 50)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Original successful images:\", len(ordered_original_indices))\n",
            "print(\"Low illumination successes:\", len(low_success))\n",
            "print(\"High illumination successes:\", len(high_success))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Images successful in all three conditions:\",\n",
            "      len(common_positions))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nEmbedding shapes:\")\n",
            "print(\"Original:\", paired_original_embeddings.shape)\n",
            "print(\"Low:\", paired_low_embeddings.shape)\n",
            "print(\"High:\", paired_high_embeddings.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nIdentity labels aligned:\",\n",
            "      np.array_equal(\n",
            "          paired_labels,\n",
            "          lfw_dataset.target[\n",
            "              ordered_original_indices[common_positions]\n",
            "          ]\n",
            "      ))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All paired embeddings finite:\",\n",
            "      all(np.all(np.isfinite(x)) for x in [\n",
            "          paired_original_embeddings,\n",
            "          paired_low_embeddings,\n",
            "          paired_high_embeddings\n",
            "      ]))\n",
            "\n",
            "assert paired_original_embeddings.shape == paired_low_embeddings.shape\n",
            "assert paired_original_embeddings.shape == paired_high_embeddings.shape\n",
            "assert paired_original_embeddings.shape[1] == 512\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 53\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 15.4 — Illumination-Induced Embedding Displacement Analysis\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Quantify the changes in FaceNet embedding representations caused by controlled illumination transformations.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "Compare paired original embeddings against their corresponding low- and high-illumination embeddings.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Evaluation Metrics\n",
            "1. Cosine similarity between original and transformed embeddings.\n",
            "2. Euclidean distance between original and transformed embeddings.\n",
            "3. Mean, median and standard deviation of embedding displacement.\n",
            "4. 95th percentile of embedding displacement.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Purpose\n",
            "Determine whether controlled illumination changes produce measurable shifts in genuine face-recognition embedding representations.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "This analysis measures representation changes, not identity recognition accuracy or real-world temporal drift.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. Illumination-induced embedding displacement was calculated for 889 correctly paired evaluation images. Cosine similarity and Euclidean displacement statistics, including mean, median, standard deviation and 95th percentile distance, were computed for low- and high-illumination conditions. The analysis quantifies changes in embedding representations under controlled brightness transformations; it does not establish identity recognition accuracy or real-world temporal drift.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 54\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "\n",
            "def calculate_embedding_displacement(\n",
            "    original_embeddings,\n",
            "    transformed_embeddings,\n",
            "    condition_name\n",
            "):\n",
            "\n",
            "    # Calculate cosine similarity for paired embeddings\n",
            "    cosine_similarities = np.sum(\n",
            "        original_embeddings * transformed_embeddings,\n",
            "        axis=1\n",
            "    ) / (\n",
            "        np.linalg.norm(original_embeddings, axis=1) *\n",
            "        np.linalg.norm(transformed_embeddings, axis=1)\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    # Calculate Euclidean displacement\n",
            "    euclidean_distances = np.linalg.norm(\n",
            "        original_embeddings - transformed_embeddings,\n",
            "        axis=1\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    return {\n",
            "        \"Condition\": condition_name,\n",
            "        \"Mean Cosine Similarity\": np.mean(cosine_similarities),\n",
            "        \"Median Cosine Similarity\": np.median(cosine_similarities),\n",
            "        \"Mean Euclidean Distance\": np.mean(euclidean_distances),\n",
            "        \"Median Euclidean Distance\": np.median(euclidean_distances),\n",
            "        \"Std Euclidean Distance\": np.std(euclidean_distances),\n",
            "        \"95th Percentile Distance\": np.percentile(\n",
            "            euclidean_distances, 95\n",
            "        )\n",
            "    }\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "# Compare original embeddings with transformed embeddings\n",
            "low_results = calculate_embedding_displacement(\n",
            "    paired_original_embeddings,\n",
            "    paired_low_embeddings,\n",
            "    \"Low illumination\"\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "high_results = calculate_embedding_displacement(\n",
            "    paired_original_embeddings,\n",
            "    paired_high_embeddings,\n",
            "    \"High illumination\"\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "illumination_displacement_results = pd.DataFrame([\n",
            "    low_results,\n",
            "    high_results\n",
            "])\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"ILLUMINATION-INDUCED EMBEDDING DISPLACEMENT\")\n",
            "print(\"Paired evaluation images:\", len(common_positions))\n",
            "\n",
            "display(\n",
            "    illumination_displacement_results.round(6)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 55\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 15.5 — Visualisation of Illumination-Induced Embedding Displacement\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Visualise the distribution of Euclidean embedding displacement under low- and high-illumination conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Calculate paired Euclidean distances between original and transformed embeddings.\n",
            "2. Generate comparative histograms.\n",
            "3. Examine distribution spread, central tendency and upper-tail behaviour.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Purpose\n",
            "Identify differences in embedding sensitivity between illumination conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "The visualisation is descriptive and does not independently establish statistical significance or biometric recognition degradation.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. Comparative density histograms were generated for low- and high-illumination Euclidean embedding displacement using 40 bins. Across 889 paired evaluation images, low illumination produced a mean displacement of 0.234665 and a median of 0.222675. High illumination produced a mean displacement of 0.318514 and a median of 0.306734. The descriptive results indicate greater embedding displacement under high illumination. This visualisation alone does not establish statistical significance or biometric recognition degradation.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 56\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "\n",
            "low_distances = np.linalg.norm(\n",
            "    paired_original_embeddings - paired_low_embeddings,\n",
            "    axis=1\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "high_distances = np.linalg.norm(\n",
            "    paired_original_embeddings - paired_high_embeddings,\n",
            "    axis=1\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
            "\n",
            "plt.hist(\n",
            "    low_distances,\n",
            "    bins=40,\n",
            "    alpha=0.6,\n",
            "    density=True,\n",
            "    label=\"Low illumination\"\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "plt.hist(\n",
            "    high_distances,\n",
            "    bins=40,\n",
            "    alpha=0.6,\n",
            "    density=True,\n",
            "    label=\"High illumination\"\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "plt.xlabel(\"Euclidean Embedding Displacement\")\n",
            "plt.ylabel(\"Density\")\n",
            "plt.title(\"FaceNet Embedding Displacement Under Illumination Changes\")\n",
            "plt.legend()\n",
            "plt.grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
            "plt.tight_layout()\n",
            "plt.show()\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"LOW ILLUMINATION\")\n",
            "print(\"Mean:\", np.mean(low_distances))\n",
            "print(\"Median:\", np.median(low_distances))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nHIGH ILLUMINATION\")\n",
            "print(\"Mean:\", np.mean(high_distances))\n",
            "print(\"Median:\", np.median(high_distances))\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 57\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 15.6 — Paired Statistical Significance Testing\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Determine whether embedding displacement differs significantly between low- and high-illumination conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Statistical Method\n",
            "Paired Wilcoxon signed-rank test.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Hypotheses\n",
            "- H0: The paired displacement distributions do not differ systematically between illumination conditions.\n",
            "- H1: The paired displacement distributions differ systematically between illumination conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Additional Measurement\n",
            "Calculate the median paired displacement difference and the proportion of images with greater displacement under high illumination.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "Statistical significance does not establish practical biometric recognition degradation. The analysis is conditional on successful face detection in all three conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. A paired Wilcoxon signed-rank test was conducted to compare low- and high-illumination embedding displacement across 889 paired evaluation images. The test produced a statistic of 52,705 and a p-value of 4.708938 × 10^-80. The median paired displacement difference was 0.075521, and the mean difference was 0.083849. High-illumination displacement was greater for 77.50% of paired images. The null hypothesis was rejected at the 0.05 significance level. Because images are clustered within 13 identities, this image-level result must be interpreted alongside the identity-level analysis. Statistical significance does not establish biometric recognition degradation.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 59\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 15.7 — Identity-Level Statistical Validation\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Determine whether the illumination-induced embedding displacement difference remains consistent across individual identities.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Calculate median low-illumination displacement for each identity.\n",
            "2. Calculate median high-illumination displacement for each identity.\n",
            "3. Calculate the paired median displacement difference for each identity.\n",
            "4. Apply a paired Wilcoxon signed-rank test across identities.\n",
            "5. Report the number of identities showing greater displacement under high illumination.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Purpose\n",
            "Reduce the risk of overstating statistical significance due to multiple correlated images belonging to the same identity.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "The identity-level analysis contains only 13 independent identity groups, limiting statistical power.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. Identity-level displacement statistics were calculated by aggregating paired image-level measurements using median displacement for each identity. The analysis included 13 evaluation identities. A paired Wilcoxon signed-rank test produced a statistic of 3.0 and a p-value of 0.001220703125. High-illumination median displacement was greater for 11 identities and lower for 2 identities. The median identity-level displacement difference was 0.079261. The result indicates a statistically significant identity-level difference, but the analysis remains limited by the small sample of 13 identities and the unequal number of images per identity.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
