            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 16 — Identity-Aware Embedding-Level Drift Detection\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Develop and evaluate embedding-level drift detectors for identifying changes in genuine FaceNet representations under controlled illumination perturbations.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Questions\n",
            "1. Can embedding-level detectors identify illumination-induced representation changes?\n",
            "2. How does detector sensitivity differ between low and high illumination?\n",
            "3. Can the detectors maintain controlled false alarm rates under baseline conditions?\n",
            "4. How does covariance regularisation influence Mahalanobis-based detection?\n",
            "\n",
            "### Experimental Design\n",
            "\n",
            "**Reference population**\n",
            "Original embeddings from the matched evaluation cohort.\n",
            "\n",
            "**Calibration population**\n",
            "Baseline-versus-baseline comparisons constructed using separate image samples and identity-aware sampling.\n",
            "\n",
            "**Evaluation population**\n",
            "Paired original and transformed embeddings under low- and high-illumination conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Detection Methods\n",
            "- Euclidean embedding displacement.\n",
            "- Regularised Mahalanobis distance.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Proposed Configuration\n",
            "- Embedding dimension: 512.\n",
            "- Window size: 20.\n",
            "- Random seed: 202618.\n",
            "- Target false alarm rates: 0.01, 0.05 and 0.10.\n",
            "- Illumination factors: 0.5, 1.0 and 1.5.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Evaluation Metrics\n",
            "- Empirical false alarm rate.\n",
            "- Detection rate.\n",
            "- Detection sensitivity by illumination condition.\n",
            "- Detection performance across identities.\n",
            "- Numerical stability.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitations\n",
            "The experiment uses controlled brightness transformations rather than naturally occurring temporal drift. Detector results will be conditional on the matched evaluation cohort and the chosen calibration protocol.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Methodology defined; implementation pending.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 66\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "\n",
            "# Reproducibility\n",
            "RANDOM_SEED = 202618\n",
            "rng = np.random.default_rng(RANDOM_SEED)\n",
            "\n",
            "# Source data: 889 correctly paired images\n",
            "X_original = paired_original_embeddings\n",
            "X_low = paired_low_embeddings\n",
            "X_high = paired_high_embeddings\n",
            "y = paired_labels\n",
            "\n",
            "# Validate input dimensions\n",
            "assert X_original.shape == X_low.shape == X_high.shape\n",
            "assert len(X_original) == len(y)\n",
            "\n",
            "# Define partition proportions\n",
            "REFERENCE_RATIO = 0.50\n",
            "CALIBRATION_RATIO = 0.25\n",
            "EVALUATION_RATIO = 0.25\n",
            "\n",
            "reference_positions = []\n",
            "calibration_positions = []\n",
            "evaluation_positions = []\n",
            "\n",
            "# Split images separately within each identity\n",
            "for identity in np.unique(y):\n",
            "\n",
            "    identity_positions = np.where(y == identity)[0]\n",
            "\n",
            "    shuffled_positions = rng.permutation(identity_positions)\n",
            "\n",
            "    n = len(shuffled_positions)\n",
            "\n",
            "    reference_count = int(n * REFERENCE_RATIO)\n",
            "    calibration_count = int(n * CALIBRATION_RATIO)\n",
            "\n",
            "    reference_positions.extend(\n",
            "        shuffled_positions[:reference_count]\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    calibration_positions.extend(\n",
            "        shuffled_positions[\n",
            "            reference_count:\n",
            "            reference_count + calibration_count\n",
            "        ]\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    evaluation_positions.extend(\n",
            "        shuffled_positions[\n",
            "            reference_count + calibration_count:\n",
            "        ]\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "# Convert to arrays\n",
            "reference_positions = np.sort(\n",
            "    np.asarray(reference_positions)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "calibration_positions = np.sort(\n",
            "    np.asarray(calibration_positions)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "evaluation_positions = np.sort(\n",
            "    np.asarray(evaluation_positions)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Construct original embedding partitions\n",
            "reference_baseline = X_original[reference_positions]\n",
            "\n",
            "calibration_baseline = X_original[calibration_positions]\n",
            "\n",
            "evaluation_baseline = X_original[evaluation_positions]\n",
            "\n",
            "# Construct corresponding transformed evaluation partitions\n",
            "evaluation_low = X_low[evaluation_positions]\n",
            "\n",
            "evaluation_high = X_high[evaluation_positions]\n",
            "\n",
            "# Identity labels\n",
            "reference_labels = y[reference_positions]\n",
            "\n",
            "calibration_labels = y[calibration_positions]\n",
            "\n",
            "evaluation_labels = y[evaluation_positions]\n",
            "\n",
            "# Validate image-level separation\n",
            "assert len(set(reference_positions) & set(calibration_positions)) == 0\n",
            "assert len(set(reference_positions) & set(evaluation_positions)) == 0\n",
            "assert len(set(calibration_positions) & set(evaluation_positions)) == 0\n",
            "\n",
            "# Validate complete partition coverage\n",
            "all_positions = np.concatenate([\n",
            "    reference_positions,\n",
            "    calibration_positions,\n",
            "    evaluation_positions\n",
            "])\n",
            "\n",
            "assert len(all_positions) == len(X_original)\n",
            "assert len(np.unique(all_positions)) == len(X_original)\n",
            "\n",
            "# Display partition summary\n",
            "partition_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
            "    \"Partition\": [\n",
            "        \"Reference\",\n",
            "        \"Calibration\",\n",
            "        \"Evaluation\"\n",
            "    ],\n",
            "    \"Images\": [\n",
            "        len(reference_positions),\n",
            "        len(calibration_positions),\n",
            "        len(evaluation_positions)\n",
            "    ],\n",
            "    \"Identities\": [\n",
            "        len(np.unique(reference_labels)),\n",
            "        len(np.unique(calibration_labels)),\n",
            "        len(np.unique(evaluation_labels))\n",
            "    ]\n",
            "})\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"IDENTITY-AWARE DATA PARTITIONING\")\n",
            "print(\"-\" * 55)\n",
            "\n",
            "display(partition_summary)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nEMBEDDING SHAPES\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Reference:\", reference_baseline.shape)\n",
            "print(\"Calibration:\", calibration_baseline.shape)\n",
            "print(\"Evaluation baseline:\", evaluation_baseline.shape)\n",
            "print(\"Evaluation low:\", evaluation_low.shape)\n",
            "print(\"Evaluation high:\", evaluation_high.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nVALIDATION\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Reference-calibration overlap:\",\n",
            "      len(set(reference_positions) & set(calibration_positions)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Reference-evaluation overlap:\",\n",
            "      len(set(reference_positions) & set(evaluation_positions)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Calibration-evaluation overlap:\",\n",
            "      len(set(calibration_positions) & set(evaluation_positions)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All identities represented in each partition:\",\n",
            "      all(\n",
            "          len(np.unique(labels)) == len(np.unique(y))\n",
            "          for labels in [\n",
            "              reference_labels,\n",
            "              calibration_labels,\n",
            "              evaluation_labels\n",
            "          ]\n",
            "      ))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All embeddings finite:\",\n",
            "      all(\n",
            "          np.all(np.isfinite(x))\n",
            "          for x in [\n",
            "              reference_baseline,\n",
            "              calibration_baseline,\n",
            "              evaluation_baseline,\n",
            "              evaluation_low,\n",
            "              evaluation_high\n",
            "          ]\n",
            "      ))\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 67\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 16.2 — Reference Distribution Estimation\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Estimate the baseline statistical characteristics of the reference FaceNet embedding population.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Calculate the reference mean embedding vector.\n",
            "2. Calculate the reference covariance matrix.\n",
            "3. Apply covariance regularisation.\n",
            "4. Calculate the covariance condition number.\n",
            "5. Verify numerical stability and embedding integrity.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Purpose\n",
            "Establish a reference distribution for subsequent Euclidean and Mahalanobis drift detection.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "The reference distribution represents the selected 442-image baseline sample from 13 identities, not a universal biometric population.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. The reference distribution was estimated using 442 baseline embeddings across 512 dimensions from 13 evaluation identities. The 512-dimensional mean vector and covariance matrix were calculated, and covariance regularisation was applied with a strength of 0.001. The regularised covariance matrix had a condition number of 140,992.74, with all eigenvalues positive. Numerical validation confirmed that the mean vector, covariance matrix and regularised covariance matrix contained only finite values. The resulting reference distribution provides the baseline statistical representation for subsequent Euclidean and Mahalanobis drift detection. These estimates are specific to the selected reference sample and should not be treated as a universal biometric population model.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 68\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "\n",
            "# Reference distribution\n",
            "reference_mean = np.mean(\n",
            "    reference_baseline,\n",
            "    axis=0\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "reference_covariance = np.cov(\n",
            "    reference_baseline,\n",
            "    rowvar=False\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Covariance regularisation\n",
            "REGULARISATION_STRENGTH = 1e-3\n",
            "\n",
            "base_regularisation = (\n",
            "    np.trace(reference_covariance) /\n",
            "    reference_covariance.shape[0]\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "reference_regularisation = (\n",
            "    REGULARISATION_STRENGTH * base_regularisation\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "reference_regularised_covariance = (\n",
            "    reference_covariance +\n",
            "    reference_regularisation *\n",
            "    np.eye(reference_covariance.shape[0])\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Numerical diagnostics\n",
            "condition_number = np.linalg.cond(\n",
            "    reference_regularised_covariance\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "eigenvalues = np.linalg.eigvalsh(\n",
            "    reference_regularised_covariance\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"REFERENCE DISTRIBUTION STATISTICS\")\n",
            "print(\"-\" * 55)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Reference samples:\", len(reference_baseline))\n",
            "print(\"Embedding dimensions:\", reference_baseline.shape[1])\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Mean vector shape:\", reference_mean.shape)\n",
            "print(\"Covariance matrix shape:\", reference_covariance.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Regularisation strength:\", REGULARISATION_STRENGTH)\n",
            "print(\"Actual regularisation:\", reference_regularisation)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Condition number:\", condition_number)\n",
            "print(\"Minimum eigenvalue:\", eigenvalues.min())\n",
            "print(\"Maximum eigenvalue:\", eigenvalues.max())\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nNUMERICAL VALIDATION\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Mean vector finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(reference_mean)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Covariance finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(reference_covariance)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Regularised covariance finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(reference_regularised_covariance)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All eigenvalues positive:\",\n",
            "      np.all(eigenvalues > 0))\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 69\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 16.3 — Baseline Calibration Window Generation\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Generate calibration windows representing unchanged baseline conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Divide the calibration embeddings into windows of 20 samples.\n",
            "2. Maintain identity-aware sampling.\n",
            "3. Calculate each window's mean embedding vector.\n",
            "4. Measure its displacement from the reference mean.\n",
            "5. Generate calibration scores for Euclidean and Mahalanobis detectors.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Purpose\n",
            "Establish baseline score distributions for threshold calibration and false-alarm control.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "Calibration windows represent the available baseline images and do not simulate naturally occurring temporal sequences\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 70\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "\n",
            "# Configuration\n",
            "RANDOM_SEED = 202618\n",
            "WINDOW_SIZE = 20\n",
            "N_CALIBRATION_WINDOWS = 10\n",
            "\n",
            "rng = np.random.default_rng(RANDOM_SEED)\n",
            "\n",
            "# Group calibration samples by identity\n",
            "calibration_identity_indices = {\n",
            "    identity: np.where(calibration_labels == identity)[0]\n",
            "    for identity in np.unique(calibration_labels)\n",
            "}\n",
            "\n",
            "available_identities = list(calibration_identity_indices.keys())\n",
            "\n",
            "# Verify sufficient identities\n",
            "assert len(available_identities) <= WINDOW_SIZE\n",
            "\n",
            "# Generate calibration windows\n",
            "calibration_windows = []\n",
            "calibration_window_labels = []\n",
            "\n",
            "for window_number in range(N_CALIBRATION_WINDOWS):\n",
            "\n",
            "    selected_positions = []\n",
            "\n",
            "    # First select one image from every identity\n",
            "    for identity in available_identities:\n",
            "\n",
            "        selected_index = rng.choice(\n",
            "            calibration_identity_indices[identity]\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "        selected_positions.append(selected_index)\n",
            "\n",
            "    # Fill remaining positions using identity-balanced sampling\n",
            "    remaining_count = WINDOW_SIZE - len(selected_positions)\n",
            "\n",
            "    for _ in range(remaining_count):\n",
            "\n",
            "        identity = rng.choice(available_identities)\n",
            "\n",
            "        selected_index = rng.choice(\n",
            "            calibration_identity_indices[identity]\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "        selected_positions.append(selected_index)\n",
            "\n",
            "    selected_positions = np.asarray(selected_positions)\n",
            "\n",
            "    # Shuffle positions within the window\n",
            "    rng.shuffle(selected_positions)\n",
            "\n",
            "    window_embeddings = calibration_baseline[selected_positions]\n",
            "    window_labels = calibration_labels[selected_positions]\n",
            "\n",
            "    calibration_windows.append(window_embeddings)\n",
            "    calibration_window_labels.append(window_labels)\n",
            "\n",
            "calibration_windows = np.asarray(calibration_windows)\n",
            "calibration_window_labels = np.asarray(calibration_window_labels)\n",
            "\n",
            "# Calculate window means\n",
            "calibration_window_means = np.mean(\n",
            "    calibration_windows,\n",
            "    axis=1\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Euclidean scores\n",
            "calibration_euclidean_scores = np.linalg.norm(\n",
            "    calibration_window_means - reference_mean,\n",
            "    axis=1\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Mahalanobis scores\n",
            "mean_differences = calibration_window_means - reference_mean\n",
            "\n",
            "solved_differences = np.linalg.solve(\n",
            "    reference_regularised_covariance,\n",
            "    mean_differences.T\n",
            ").T\n",
            "\n",
            "calibration_mahalanobis_scores = np.sqrt(\n",
            "    np.sum(mean_differences * solved_differences, axis=1)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Summary\n",
            "calibration_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
            "    \"Window\": np.arange(1, N_CALIBRATION_WINDOWS + 1),\n",
            "    \"Samples\": [WINDOW_SIZE] * N_CALIBRATION_WINDOWS,\n",
            "    \"Unique Identities\": [\n",
            "        len(np.unique(labels))\n",
            "        for labels in calibration_window_labels\n",
            "    ],\n",
            "    \"Euclidean Score\": calibration_euclidean_scores,\n",
            "    \"Mahalanobis Score\": calibration_mahalanobis_scores\n",
            "})\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"BASELINE CALIBRATION WINDOW SUMMARY\")\n",
            "print(\"-\" * 60)\n",
            "\n",
            "display(calibration_summary.round(6))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nVALIDATION\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Calibration windows shape:\", calibration_windows.shape)\n",
            "print(\"Calibration window means shape:\", calibration_window_means.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All Euclidean scores finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(calibration_euclidean_scores)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All Mahalanobis scores finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(calibration_mahalanobis_scores)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All windows contain 13 identities:\",\n",
            "      np.all(\n",
            "          calibration_summary[\"Unique Identities\"].values == 13\n",
            "      ))\n",
            "\n",
            "assert calibration_windows.shape == (10, 20, 512)\n",
            "assert np.all(np.isfinite(calibration_euclidean_scores))\n",
            "assert np.all(np.isfinite(calibration_mahalanobis_scores))\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 71\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 16.4 — Identity-Balanced Reference Distribution\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Construct a reference distribution that gives equal representation to each evaluation identity.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Calculate the mean embedding for each identity in the reference partition.\n",
            "2. Calculate the global reference mean as the average of the 13 identity means.\n",
            "3. Estimate within-identity covariance to reduce between-identity composition effects.\n",
            "4. Apply covariance regularisation.\n",
            "5. Verify numerical stability.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Purpose\n",
            "Reduce identity-composition bias in the reference distribution used for embedding-level drift detection.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "This approach estimates within-identity variation for the selected 13 identities. It does not establish generalisation to unseen identities.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. An identity-balanced reference distribution was constructed using 13 evaluation identities. Individual identity mean embeddings were calculated and equally weighted to obtain the global reference mean vector. Within-identity residuals were used to estimate the covariance matrix, reducing the influence of between-identity composition differences. Covariance regularisation was applied with a strength of 0.001. The regularised covariance matrix had a condition number of 36,201.96, and all eigenvalues were positive. Numerical validation confirmed that all regularised covariance values were finite. This approach estimates within-identity variation for the selected 13 identities and does not establish generalisation to unseen identities.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 72\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "\n",
            "# Calculate individual identity means\n",
            "reference_identity_means = []\n",
            "\n",
            "for identity in np.unique(reference_labels):\n",
            "\n",
            "    identity_embeddings = reference_baseline[\n",
            "        reference_labels == identity\n",
            "    ]\n",
            "\n",
            "    reference_identity_means.append(\n",
            "        np.mean(identity_embeddings, axis=0)\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "reference_identity_means = np.asarray(\n",
            "    reference_identity_means\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Equal-weight identity-balanced reference mean\n",
            "balanced_reference_mean = np.mean(\n",
            "    reference_identity_means,\n",
            "    axis=0\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Estimate within-identity covariance\n",
            "within_identity_residuals = []\n",
            "\n",
            "for identity in np.unique(reference_labels):\n",
            "\n",
            "    identity_embeddings = reference_baseline[\n",
            "        reference_labels == identity\n",
            "    ]\n",
            "\n",
            "    identity_mean = np.mean(\n",
            "        identity_embeddings,\n",
            "        axis=0\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    within_identity_residuals.append(\n",
            "        identity_embeddings - identity_mean\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "within_identity_residuals = np.vstack(\n",
            "    within_identity_residuals\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "balanced_reference_covariance = np.cov(\n",
            "    within_identity_residuals,\n",
            "    rowvar=False\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Regularise covariance\n",
            "regularisation_strength = 1e-3\n",
            "\n",
            "base_regularisation = (\n",
            "    np.trace(balanced_reference_covariance) / 512\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "balanced_regularisation = (\n",
            "    regularisation_strength * base_regularisation\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "balanced_regularised_covariance = (\n",
            "    balanced_reference_covariance +\n",
            "    balanced_regularisation * np.eye(512)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Numerical diagnostics\n",
            "eigenvalues = np.linalg.eigvalsh(\n",
            "    balanced_regularised_covariance\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "condition_number = np.linalg.cond(\n",
            "    balanced_regularised_covariance\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"IDENTITY-BALANCED REFERENCE DISTRIBUTION\")\n",
            "print(\"-\" * 55)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Number of identities:\",\n",
            "      len(reference_identity_means))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Identity means shape:\",\n",
            "      reference_identity_means.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Balanced reference mean shape:\",\n",
            "      balanced_reference_mean.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Within-identity residuals:\",\n",
            "      within_identity_residuals.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Covariance shape:\",\n",
            "      balanced_reference_covariance.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Actual regularisation:\",\n",
            "      balanced_regularisation)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Condition number:\",\n",
            "      condition_number)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Minimum eigenvalue:\",\n",
            "      eigenvalues.min())\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nVALIDATION\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All values finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(balanced_regularised_covariance)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All eigenvalues positive:\",\n",
            "      np.all(eigenvalues > 0))\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 73\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 16.5 — Identity-Balanced Calibration Score Recalculation\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Recalculate baseline calibration scores using the identity-balanced reference distribution established in Step 16.4.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Calculate the mean embedding vector for each identity within every calibration window.\n",
            "2. Aggregate identity means with equal weighting.\n",
            "3. Calculate Euclidean distance from the identity-balanced reference mean.\n",
            "4. Calculate regularised Mahalanobis distance using the identity-balanced within-identity covariance matrix.\n",
            "5. Validate the resulting calibration scores.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Evaluation Metrics\n",
            "- Identity-balanced Euclidean distance.\n",
            "- Regularised Mahalanobis distance.\n",
            "- Numerical integrity of calibration scores.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Purpose\n",
            "Ensure that reference and calibration statistics use consistent identity-weighting principles, reducing the influence of unequal identity representation.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "The current 10 calibration windows are preliminary. They are insufficient for reliable estimation of low false-alarm thresholds, particularly at a 1% target rate.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. Baseline calibration scores were recalculated using the identity-balanced reference distribution. For each of the 10 calibration windows, identity-specific mean embeddings were calculated and equally weighted to produce a balanced window mean. Euclidean distances were measured against the balanced reference mean, and regularised Mahalanobis distances were calculated using the identity-balanced covariance matrix. All 10 windows represented 13 identities, producing a calibration mean matrix of shape (10, 512). Both Euclidean and Mahalanobis calibration scores passed numerical integrity checks, with all values finite. The resulting scores provide preliminary baseline calibration evidence. The 10-window sample remains insufficient for reliable low false-alarm threshold estimation, particularly at a 1% target rate.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 74\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "\n",
            "# Calculate identity-balanced mean for each calibration window\n",
            "balanced_calibration_window_means = []\n",
            "\n",
            "for window_embeddings, window_labels in zip(\n",
            "    calibration_windows,\n",
            "    calibration_window_labels\n",
            "):\n",
            "\n",
            "    identity_means = []\n",
            "\n",
            "    for identity in np.unique(window_labels):\n",
            "\n",
            "        identity_embeddings = window_embeddings[\n",
            "            window_labels == identity\n",
            "        ]\n",
            "\n",
            "        identity_means.append(\n",
            "            np.mean(identity_embeddings, axis=0)\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "    # Equal weight for all represented identities\n",
            "    balanced_window_mean = np.mean(\n",
            "        identity_means,\n",
            "        axis=0\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    balanced_calibration_window_means.append(\n",
            "        balanced_window_mean\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "balanced_calibration_window_means = np.asarray(\n",
            "    balanced_calibration_window_means\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Calculate Euclidean calibration scores\n",
            "balanced_calibration_euclidean_scores = np.linalg.norm(\n",
            "    balanced_calibration_window_means -\n",
            "    balanced_reference_mean,\n",
            "    axis=1\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Calculate regularised Mahalanobis calibration scores\n",
            "mean_differences = (\n",
            "    balanced_calibration_window_means -\n",
            "    balanced_reference_mean\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "solved_differences = np.linalg.solve(\n",
            "    balanced_regularised_covariance,\n",
            "    mean_differences.T\n",
            ").T\n",
            "\n",
            "balanced_calibration_mahalanobis_scores = np.sqrt(\n",
            "    np.sum(\n",
            "        mean_differences * solved_differences,\n",
            "        axis=1\n",
            "    )\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Create results table\n",
            "balanced_calibration_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
            "    \"Window\": np.arange(\n",
            "        1,\n",
            "        len(calibration_windows) + 1\n",
            "    ),\n",
            "    \"Unique Identities\": [\n",
            "        len(np.unique(labels))\n",
            "        for labels in calibration_window_labels\n",
            "    ],\n",
            "    \"Euclidean Score\": balanced_calibration_euclidean_scores,\n",
            "    \"Mahalanobis Score\": balanced_calibration_mahalanobis_scores\n",
            "})\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"IDENTITY-BALANCED CALIBRATION SCORES\")\n",
            "print(\"-\" * 60)\n",
            "\n",
            "display(balanced_calibration_summary.round(6))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nNUMERICAL VALIDATION\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Calibration window means shape:\",\n",
            "      balanced_calibration_window_means.shape)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All Euclidean scores finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(\n",
            "          balanced_calibration_euclidean_scores\n",
            "      )))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All Mahalanobis scores finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(\n",
            "          balanced_calibration_mahalanobis_scores\n",
            "      )))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"All windows contain 13 identities:\",\n",
            "      np.all(\n",
            "          balanced_calibration_summary[\"Unique Identities\"] == 13\n",
            "      ))\n",
            "\n",
            "assert balanced_calibration_window_means.shape == (10, 512)\n",
            "assert np.all(np.isfinite(balanced_calibration_euclidean_scores))\n",
            "assert np.all(np.isfinite(balanced_calibration_mahalanobis_scores))\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 78\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "\n",
            "RANDOM_SEED = 202618\n",
            "WINDOW_SIZE = 20\n",
            "N_EXPANDED_WINDOWS = 100\n",
            "\n",
            "rng = np.random.default_rng(RANDOM_SEED)\n",
            "\n",
            "identity_groups = {\n",
            "    identity: np.where(calibration_labels == identity)[0]\n",
            "    for identity in np.unique(calibration_labels)\n",
            "}\n",
            "\n",
            "identities = list(identity_groups.keys())\n",
            "\n",
            "expanded_windows = []\n",
            "expanded_labels = []\n",
            "expanded_positions = []\n",
            "\n",
            "for window_number in range(N_EXPANDED_WINDOWS):\n",
            "\n",
            "    selected_positions = []\n",
            "\n",
            "    # One image from each identity\n",
            "    for identity in identities:\n",
            "        selected_positions.append(\n",
            "            rng.choice(identity_groups[identity])\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "    # Fill remaining seven positions\n",
            "    for _ in range(WINDOW_SIZE - len(identities)):\n",
            "        identity = rng.choice(identities)\n",
            "\n",
            "        selected_positions.append(\n",
            "            rng.choice(identity_groups[identity])\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "    selected_positions = np.asarray(selected_positions)\n",
            "\n",
            "    rng.shuffle(selected_positions)\n",
            "\n",
            "    expanded_windows.append(\n",
            "        calibration_baseline[selected_positions]\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    expanded_labels.append(\n",
            "        calibration_labels[selected_positions]\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    expanded_positions.append(selected_positions)\n",
            "\n",
            "expanded_windows = np.asarray(expanded_windows)\n",
            "expanded_labels = np.asarray(expanded_labels)\n",
            "expanded_positions = np.asarray(expanded_positions)\n",
            "\n",
            "# Equal-weight identity means for each window\n",
            "expanded_window_means = []\n",
            "\n",
            "for window, labels in zip(expanded_windows, expanded_labels):\n",
            "\n",
            "    identity_means = []\n",
            "\n",
            "    for identity in identities:\n",
            "\n",
            "        identity_embeddings = window[labels == identity]\n",
            "\n",
            "        identity_means.append(\n",
            "            np.mean(identity_embeddings, axis=0)\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "    expanded_window_means.append(\n",
            "        np.mean(identity_means, axis=0)\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "expanded_window_means = np.asarray(expanded_window_means)\n",
            "\n",
            "# Euclidean scores\n",
            "expanded_euclidean_scores = np.linalg.norm(\n",
            "    expanded_window_means - balanced_reference_mean,\n",
            "    axis=1\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Mahalanobis scores\n",
            "differences = expanded_window_means - balanced_reference_mean\n",
            "\n",
            "solved = np.linalg.solve(\n",
            "    balanced_regularised_covariance,\n",
            "    differences.T\n",
            ").T\n",
            "\n",
            "expanded_mahalanobis_scores = np.sqrt(\n",
            "    np.sum(differences * solved, axis=1)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Image reuse diagnostics\n",
            "unique_images = np.unique(expanded_positions)\n",
            "\n",
            "reuse_counts = np.bincount(\n",
            "    expanded_positions.flatten(),\n",
            "    minlength=len(calibration_baseline)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"EXPANDED CALIBRATION SUMMARY\")\n",
            "print(\"Number of windows:\", len(expanded_windows))\n",
            "print(\"Samples per window:\", WINDOW_SIZE)\n",
            "print(\"Identities per window:\", len(identities))\n",
            "print(\"Unique source images used:\", len(unique_images))\n",
            "print(\"Total calibration images:\", len(calibration_baseline))\n",
            "print(\"Maximum image reuse:\", reuse_counts.max())\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nSCORE VALIDATION\")\n",
            "print(\"Euclidean scores finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(expanded_euclidean_scores)))\n",
            "print(\"Mahalanobis scores finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(expanded_mahalanobis_scores)))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nSCORE STATISTICS\")\n",
            "\n",
            "display(pd.DataFrame({\n",
            "    \"Detector\": [\"Euclidean\", \"Mahalanobis\"],\n",
            "    \"Mean\": [\n",
            "        expanded_euclidean_scores.mean(),\n",
            "        expanded_mahalanobis_scores.mean()\n",
            "    ],\n",
            "    \"Standard Deviation\": [\n",
            "        expanded_euclidean_scores.std(),\n",
            "        expanded_mahalanobis_scores.std()\n",
            "    ],\n",
            "    \"Minimum\": [\n",
            "        expanded_euclidean_scores.min(),\n",
            "        expanded_mahalanobis_scores.min()\n",
            "    ],\n",
            "    \"Maximum\": [\n",
            "        expanded_euclidean_scores.max(),\n",
            "        expanded_mahalanobis_scores.max()\n",
            "    ]\n",
            "}).round(6))\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 84\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "\n",
            "identity_covariances = []\n",
            "\n",
            "for identity in np.unique(reference_labels):\n",
            "\n",
            "    identity_embeddings = reference_baseline[\n",
            "        reference_labels == identity\n",
            "    ]\n",
            "\n",
            "    identity_covariance = np.cov(\n",
            "        identity_embeddings,\n",
            "        rowvar=False,\n",
            "        ddof=1\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    identity_covariances.append(identity_covariance)\n",
            "\n",
            "# Equal weighting across the 13 identities\n",
            "identity_balanced_covariance = np.mean(\n",
            "    identity_covariances,\n",
            "    axis=0\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Diagonal regularisation\n",
            "regularisation_strength = 1e-3\n",
            "\n",
            "covariance_scale = np.trace(\n",
            "    identity_balanced_covariance\n",
            ") / identity_balanced_covariance.shape[0]\n",
            "\n",
            "identity_balanced_regularisation = (\n",
            "    regularisation_strength * covariance_scale\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "identity_balanced_regularised_covariance = (\n",
            "    identity_balanced_covariance\n",
            "    + identity_balanced_regularisation * np.eye(512)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# Numerical diagnostics\n",
            "eigenvalues = np.linalg.eigvalsh(\n",
            "    identity_balanced_regularised_covariance\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "condition_number = np.linalg.cond(\n",
            "    identity_balanced_regularised_covariance\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"IDENTITY-BALANCED COVARIANCE DIAGNOSTICS\")\n",
            "print(\"Number of identity covariance matrices:\",\n",
            "      len(identity_covariances))\n",
            "print(\"Covariance shape:\",\n",
            "      identity_balanced_covariance.shape)\n",
            "print(\"Regularisation strength:\",\n",
            "      regularisation_strength)\n",
            "print(\"Actual regularisation:\",\n",
            "      identity_balanced_regularisation)\n",
            "print(\"Minimum eigenvalue:\", eigenvalues.min())\n",
            "print(\"Maximum eigenvalue:\", eigenvalues.max())\n",
            "print(\"Condition number:\", condition_number)\n",
            "print(\"All eigenvalues positive:\", np.all(eigenvalues > 0))\n",
            "print(\"All covariance values finite:\",\n",
            "      np.all(np.isfinite(identity_balanced_regularised_covariance)))\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 89\n",
            "CELL TYPE: markdown\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 16.13 — Final Detector Configuration\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
