            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 17.1 — Controlled Illumination Detector Scoring\n",
            "\n",
            "### Objective\n",
            "Evaluate the response of the frozen embedding-level detectors under original, low-illumination, and high-illumination conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Methodology\n",
            "1. Calculate identity-balanced window means for each illumination condition.\n",
            "2. Calculate Euclidean distances from the frozen reference mean.\n",
            "3. Calculate Mahalanobis distances using the frozen identity-balanced covariance.\n",
            "4. Compare detector scores across the three conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Evaluation Conditions\n",
            "- Original illumination\n",
            "- Low illumination (brightness factor 0.5)\n",
            "- High illumination (brightness factor 1.5)\n",
            "\n",
            "### Research Purpose\n",
            "Determine whether controlled illumination changes produce measurable shifts in the embedding-level detector scores.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "The evaluation contains 13 identities and 229 images. Results represent controlled synthetic illumination changes, not real-world environmental drift or biometric recognition accuracy.\n",
            "\n",
            "### Status\n",
            "Successfully completed. The frozen Euclidean and Mahalanobis detectors were evaluated under original, low-illumination and high-illumination conditions using the identity-balanced reference statistics.\n",
            "\n",
            "The original condition produced a mean Euclidean score of 0.053114 and a mean Mahalanobis score of 0.797920.\n",
            "\n",
            "The low-illumination condition (brightness factor 0.5) produced a mean Euclidean score of 0.094771 and a mean Mahalanobis score of 1.735851.\n",
            "\n",
            "The high-illumination condition (brightness factor 1.5) produced a mean Euclidean score of 0.082996 and a mean Mahalanobis score of 1.871540.\n",
            "\n",
            "Numerical validation confirmed that all detector scores were finite.\n",
            "\n",
            "These results show measurable changes in embedding-level detector scores under the controlled illumination conditions. They do not establish real-world biometric recognition accuracy, environmental robustness or deployment readiness. The evaluation is limited to 13 identities and 229 images.\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 92\n",
            "CELL TYPE: code\n",
            "MATCHED TERMS: ['embedding']\n",
            "---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "\n",
            "# Calculate identity-balanced evaluation means\n",
            "def calculate_identity_balanced_mean(embeddings, labels):\n",
            "\n",
            "    identity_means = []\n",
            "\n",
            "    for identity in np.unique(labels):\n",
            "\n",
            "        identity_embeddings = embeddings[labels == identity]\n",
            "\n",
            "        identity_means.append(\n",
            "            np.mean(identity_embeddings, axis=0)\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "    return np.mean(identity_means, axis=0)\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "# Calculate evaluation means for each condition\n",
            "evaluation_condition_means = {\n",
            "    \"Original\": calculate_identity_balanced_mean(\n",
            "        evaluation_baseline, evaluation_labels\n",
            "    ),\n",
            "    \"Low illumination\": calculate_identity_balanced_mean(\n",
            "        evaluation_low, evaluation_labels\n",
            "    ),\n",
            "    \"High illumination\": calculate_identity_balanced_mean(\n",
            "        evaluation_high, evaluation_labels\n",
            "    )\n",
            "}\n",
            "\n",
            "# Calculate detector scores\n",
            "evaluation_detector_results = []\n",
            "\n",
            "for condition, embedding_mean in evaluation_condition_means.items():\n",
            "\n",
            "    difference = embedding_mean - balanced_reference_mean\n",
            "\n",
            "    euclidean_score = np.linalg.norm(difference)\n",
            "\n",
            "    solved_difference = np.linalg.solve(\n",
            "        identity_balanced_regularised_covariance,\n",
            "        difference\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    mahalanobis_score = np.sqrt(\n",
            "        difference @ solved_difference\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    evaluation_detector_results.append({\n",
            "        \"Condition\": condition,\n",
            "        \"Euclidean\": euclidean_score,\n",
            "        \"Mahalanobis\": mahalanobis_score\n",
            "    })\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "evaluation_detector_df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
            "    evaluation_detector_results\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"CONTROLLED ILLUMINATION DETECTOR RESULTS\")\n",
            "display(evaluation_detector_df.round(6))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nNUMERICAL VALIDATION\")\n",
            "print(\n",
            "    \"All scores finite:\",\n",
            "    np.all(np.isfinite(\n",
            "        evaluation_detector_df[[\"Euclidean\", \"Mahalanobis\"]].values\n",
            "    ))\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "===========================================================================\n",
            "CELL INDEX: 95\n",
