      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.1.6: Consolidated Methodological Risk Register\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "Consolidate the methodological findings from the completed Step 3.1 review.\n",
        "\n",
        "The register must distinguish:\n",
        "1. Verified methodological properties.\n",
        "2. Known limitations that must be disclosed.\n",
        "3. Unresolved decisions requiring attention before manuscript submission.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Scope\n",
        "This is a documentation and review step.\n",
        "\n",
        "It must not:\n",
        "- Modify experimental data.\n",
        "- Recalculate or replace statistical results.\n",
        "- Change the frozen protocol.\n",
        "- Introduce unsupported scientific claims.\n",
        "- Treat embedding displacement as recognition accuracy.\n",
        "- Treat descriptive analysis as a calibrated real-time detector.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Output\n",
        "Save a structured JSON risk register and verify that it can be reloaded."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Kx1-baI4vMVQ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "import json\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\")\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = BASE / \"step_3_1\"\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "OUTPUT_FILE = (\n",
        "    OUTPUT_DIR /\n",
        "    \"experiment20_step316_methodological_risk_register.json\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "risks = [\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M01\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Dataset provenance\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"The actual acquisition listing matches the acquired CroppedYale.zip record.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Step 3.1.5.2 supplementary acquisition-source reconciliation audit\",\n",
        "            \"Matching acquisition info-hash and archive size\",\n",
        "            \"Matching source archive SHA256\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"verified_with_limitation\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"Official Yale checksum authentication and independent torrent-piece verification were not performed.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Describe the community-hosted Academic Torrents acquisition and disclose the provenance limitation.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M02\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Dataset scope\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"The acquired dataset is the cropped frontal-pose subset, not the complete multi-pose Extended Yale B dataset.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Frozen dataset README\",\n",
        "            \"Dataset acquisition and cohort audits\",\n",
        "            \"38 identities and P00 pose\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"verified_scope_limitation\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"The findings cannot be generalized to all poses or the complete Extended Yale B dataset.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Use the precise cropped frontal-pose subset description throughout.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M03\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Repeated observations\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"Evaluation observations are identity-condition matched captures under different illumination conditions.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Common illumination condition manifest\",\n",
        "            \"38 identities\",\n",
        "            \"57 common conditions\",\n",
        "            \"2,166 common-condition observations\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"verified_design_limitation\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"Different captures are not exact source-image perturbations.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Avoid describing the observations as exact image-level pairs.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M04\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Preprocessing reproducibility\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"Images were converted from grayscale to RGB, resized to 160x160, and converted using ToTensor.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Freeze manifest\",\n",
        "            \"Embedding generation configuration\",\n",
        "            \"Preprocessing consistency audit\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"partially_documented\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"Resize interpolation and some software/model execution details remain insufficiently documented.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Recover these details from the original execution environment if possible; otherwise disclose them as unavailable.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M05\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Model validation\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"The same pretrained VGGFace2 InceptionResnetV1 FaceNet backbone was used.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Freeze manifest\",\n",
        "            \"Embedding metadata\",\n",
        "            \"Model configuration\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"verified_design_limitation\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"The external dataset does not constitute independent model validation.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Describe this as external dataset evaluation using the same pretrained model.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M06\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Statistical inference\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"Repeated-measures Friedman and Wilcoxon analyses were reproduced.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Step 3.1.3 independent statistical reproduction\",\n",
        "            \"38 identities\",\n",
        "            \"All six pairwise comparisons reproduced\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"reproduced_with_reporting_decision\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"Holm correction was applied separately to the three comparisons for each metric; the protocol does not explicitly define the correction family.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Justify the two metric-wise families or recompute using one six-comparison family. Do not silently change the correction.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M07\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Descriptive analysis\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"Euclidean displacement and cosine distance quantify embedding changes relative to the reference condition.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Frozen descriptive analysis protocol\",\n",
        "            \"Step 2.7.2 displacement analysis\",\n",
        "            \"Step 2.7.3 group statistics\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"verified_scope_limitation\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"These metrics do not establish identity recognition accuracy, detector accuracy, or operational robustness.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Interpret results as embedding displacement only.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M08\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Detector calibration\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"The selected analysis is descriptive and does not use calibrated detection thresholds.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Step 2.7.1 protocol\",\n",
        "            \"No threshold calibration\",\n",
        "            \"No false-alarm evaluation\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"verified_scope_limitation\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"No operational false-alarm control or real-time detection performance can be claimed.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Do not present this experiment as a validated real-time drift detector.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M09\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Lighting geometry\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"Illumination groups represent angular deviation of light direction.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Lighting geometry grouping audit\",\n",
        "            \"Near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular groups\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"verified_interpretation_constraint\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"The groups do not directly measure illumination intensity.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Use light-direction geometry terminology rather than intensity categories.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M10\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Hemisphere analysis\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"Frontal and beyond-frontal conditions were compared descriptively and statistically.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Step 2.7.5 hemisphere analysis\",\n",
        "            \"45 frontal evaluation conditions\",\n",
        "            \"11 beyond-frontal evaluation conditions\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"exploratory_limitation\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"Unequal condition counts and confounding with angular geometry limit interpretation.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Present hemisphere findings as exploratory, not as an isolated causal effect.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M11\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Reference representation\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"One reference embedding per identity was used.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Reference condition A+000E+00\",\n",
        "            \"38 reference embeddings\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"verified_design_limitation\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"One reference embedding per identity does not support reliable identity-conditioned covariance estimation.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Do not claim identity-conditioned Mahalanobis calibration or covariance modelling.\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"id\": \"M12\",\n",
        "        \"area\": \"Cohort selection\",\n",
        "        \"finding\": \"The analysis uses 38 identities sharing 57 illumination conditions.\",\n",
        "        \"evidence\": [\n",
        "            \"Common illumination condition manifest\",\n",
        "            \"2,128 evaluation observations after reference exclusion\"\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"classification\": \"verified_scope_limitation\",\n",
        "        \"limitation\": \"Seven identities are incomplete in the broader dataset, and only common conditions enter the main evaluation.\",\n",
        "        \"manuscript_action\": \"Explain the common-condition cohort selection and avoid implying complete condition coverage.\"\n",
        "    }\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "register = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": 20,\n",
        "    \"step\": \"3.1.6\",\n",
        "    \"title\": \"Consolidated Methodological Risk Register\",\n",
        "    \"timestamp_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"source_review_steps\": [\n",
        "        \"3.1.1\",\n",
        "        \"3.1.2\",\n",
        "        \"3.1.3\",\n",
        "        \"3.1.4\",\n",
        "        \"3.1.5\",\n",
        "        \"3.1.5.1\",\n",
        "        \"3.1.5.2\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"risk_count\": len(risks),\n",
        "    \"classification_counts\": {},\n",
        "    \"risks\": risks,\n",
        "    \"overall_assessment\": (\n",
        "        \"The experiment has a reproducible descriptive analysis and a \"\n",
        "        \"documented cohort, but important scope, provenance, preprocessing, \"\n",
        "        \"and inferential limitations must be explicitly handled in the manuscript.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "for item in risks:\n",
        "    category = item[\"classification\"]\n",
        "    register[\"classification_counts\"][category] = (\n",
        "        register[\"classification_counts\"].get(category, 0) + 1\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "with OUTPUT_FILE.open(\"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "    json.dump(register, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "with OUTPUT_FILE.open(\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "    verified = json.load(f)\n",
        "\n",
        "assert len(verified[\"risks\"]) == 12\n",
        "assert len({r[\"id\"] for r in verified[\"risks\"]}) == 12\n",
        "assert all(\n",
        "    r[\"finding\"] and r[\"limitation\"] and r[\"manuscript_action\"]\n",
        "    for r in verified[\"risks\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 100)\n",
        "print(\"EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.1.6\")\n",
        "print(\"CONSOLIDATED METHODOLOGICAL RISK REGISTER\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 100)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Risk entries:\", verified[\"risk_count\"])\n",
        "print(\"\\nClassification counts:\")\n",
        "for key, value in verified[\"classification_counts\"].items():\n",
        "    print(f\"{key}: {value}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nValidation:\")\n",
        "print(\"Unique risk IDs:\", \"PASS\")\n",
        "print(\"Required fields:\", \"PASS\")\n",
        "print(\"JSON reload:\", \"PASS\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nOverall assessment:\")\n",
        "print(verified[\"overall_assessment\"])\n",
