      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.2.2\n",
        "## Closest Prior Studies and Methodological Comparison\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "Compare the closest identified studies with the actual\n",
        "methodology of Experiment 20.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Main findings\n",
        "- Yale B illumination evaluation is well established.\n",
        "- Angular illumination grouping is established.\n",
        "- Identity-specific illumination subspaces have been studied.\n",
        "- Illumination-invariant handcrafted and transport-based\n",
        "  representations already exist.\n",
        "- Modern deep face-verification robustness under low light\n",
        "  has also been investigated.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Potential distinction\n",
        "Experiment 20 uses a fixed pretrained InceptionResnetV1\n",
        "FaceNet representation and evaluates paired identity-level\n",
        "embedding displacement from a common reference capture\n",
        "across three illumination-direction groups.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Novelty status\n",
        "POTENTIALLY_DISTINCT_EMPIRICAL_DESIGN_NOT_ESTABLISHED.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Main limitations\n",
        "- One reference embedding per identity.\n",
        "- No identity-conditioned covariance estimation.\n",
        "- No independent model validation.\n",
        "- No recognition accuracy or verification-performance evaluation.\n",
        "- No calibrated drift detector."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "F9S8TTLbzplI"
      }
    },
