    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.2.3\n",
        "## Deep Face Embedding and Illumination Prior-Art Assessment\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "Evaluate the closest prior work involving:\n",
        "1. FaceNet and Extended Yale B.\n",
        "2. Illumination-direction grouping.\n",
        "3. Within-identity pairwise distances.\n",
        "4. Embedding-space attribute geometry.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Newly verified prior work\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Siddique et al. (2025):\n",
        "   FaceNet features, Extended Yale B, illumination subsets,\n",
        "   probabilistic illumination enhancement and SVM recognition.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Eight Local Directional Patterns (2014):\n",
        "   Yale B illumination subsets and within-subject /\n",
        "   between-subject pairwise L2 distance analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Leroy et al. (2025):\n",
        "   Geometric analysis of face-recognition embedding spaces\n",
        "   and image attributes, including illumination.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Experiment 20 distinction\n",
        "A fixed pretrained InceptionResnetV1 representation is used\n",
        "to calculate displacement from a common reference capture\n",
        "for each identity across three illumination-direction groups.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Novelty conclusion\n",
        "The broad research problem and several methodological\n",
        "components are established prior art.\n",
        "\n",
        "The precise combination of the Experiment 20 protocol\n",
        "remains potentially distinctive but has not been established\n",
        "as novel.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Research limitations\n",
        "- One reference capture per identity.\n",
        "- Distinct captures rather than exact source-image perturbations.\n",
        "- One pretrained embedding architecture.\n",
        "- No recognition-performance evaluation.\n",
        "- No calibrated drift detector.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Next action\n",
        "Assess whether the present experimental design supports\n",
        "a standalone empirical paper and identify the minimum\n",
        "additional experiments needed to strengthen it."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "h-SSqxMX0c8r"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
