      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.2.12\n",
        "## Landmark-Alignment Route Feasibility Assessment\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "Identify a possible alternative to MTCNN for landmark detection\n",
        "on the frozen Cropped Extended Yale B image cohort.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Candidate: MediaPipe Face Landmarker\n",
        "\n",
        "Official documentation:\n",
        "https://developers.google.com/edge/mediapipe/solutions/vision/face_landmarker\n",
        "\n",
        "Documented capabilities:\n",
        "- Processes still images.\n",
        "- Returns 478 facial landmarks.\n",
        "- Provides normalized landmark coordinates.\n",
        "- Supports Python image-mode inference.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Potential application\n",
        "A five-point alignment transform may be derived from selected\n",
        "landmarks representing:\n",
        "- Left eye\n",
        "- Right eye\n",
        "- Nose\n",
        "- Left mouth corner\n",
        "- Right mouth corner\n",
        "\n",
        "The selected landmark indices and target coordinates must be\n",
        "documented and validated before use.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Unresolved questions\n",
        "1. Can MediaPipe detect faces reliably in the grayscale Yale B images?\n",
        "2. Does detection coverage remain stable across illumination conditions?\n",
        "3. Are the selected landmarks anatomically plausible under strong shadows?\n",
        "4. Can a consistent five-point alignment transform be derived?\n",
        "5. Does alignment introduce condition-dependent crop failures or distortions?\n",
        "\n",
        "### Important methodological restriction\n",
        "Do not assume that MediaPipe alignment is equivalent to the\n",
        "alignment pipelines used by AdaFace or MagFace.\n",
        "\n",
        "A successful landmark detection is not proof of successful alignment.\n",
        "Alignment must be visually inspected and quantitatively audited.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Decision\n",
        "MediaPipe is retained as an experimental alignment candidate.\n",
        "It is not yet approved for the additional-model evaluation.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Restrictions\n",
        "- No package installation.\n",
        "- No model download.\n",
        "- No inference.\n",
        "- No changes to frozen images or FaceNet embeddings."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FGFKO1o36AFF"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
