      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.2\n",
        "## Research Gap and Related-Work Positioning\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. Established Research\n",
        "\n",
        "Previous research has investigated:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Illumination variation and face-recognition performance\n",
        "   on Yale B and related datasets.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Illumination compensation and normalization using\n",
        "   frequency-domain and spatial-domain methods.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Identity-specific illumination subspaces and geometric\n",
        "   relationships between face-image sets.\n",
        "\n",
        "4. The influence of image attributes on deep face-recognition\n",
        "   embedding geometry.\n",
        "\n",
        "5. Modern face-verification performance under low-light\n",
        "   degradation and illumination-aware enhancement.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Research Gap\n",
        "\n",
        "Existing literature establishes that illumination variation\n",
        "affects face images, recognition systems, and learned\n",
        "representation spaces.\n",
        "\n",
        "The present study addresses a narrower empirical question:\n",
        "\n",
        "How does a fixed pretrained FaceNet model represent\n",
        "reference-relative embedding displacement across illumination\n",
        "geometry conditions when evaluated at the individual-identity\n",
        "level using a common reference capture for each identity?\n",
        "\n",
        "The investigation examines:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Reference-relative Euclidean displacement.\n",
        "- Reference-relative cosine distance.\n",
        "- Near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular illumination groups.\n",
        "- Differences across identities using repeated-measures analysis.\n",
        "- Exploratory frontal versus beyond-frontal comparisons.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. Research-Gap Boundary\n",
        "\n",
        "This study does not establish that reference-relative embedding\n",
        "displacement is a previously unexplored concept.\n",
        "\n",
        "It does not establish that no previous study has used Yale B,\n",
        "FaceNet, angular illumination groups, or identity-level\n",
        "distance measurements.\n",
        "\n",
        "Its potential contribution lies in the particular combination\n",
        "of:\n",
        "\n",
        "- A fixed pretrained FaceNet representation.\n",
        "- A common reference capture per identity.\n",
        "- Reference-relative embedding displacement.\n",
        "- Three illumination geometry groups.\n",
        "- Identity-level descriptive and repeated-measures analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "The distinctiveness of this combination remains an empirical\n",
        "positioning claim, not an established claim of first discovery.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Important Dataset Qualification\n",
        "\n",
        "The evaluation images are different captures under different\n",
        "illumination conditions.\n",
        "\n",
        "They are not exact pixel-level transformations of the same\n",
        "source image.\n",
        "\n",
        "Consequently, the measured displacement may reflect\n",
        "illumination together with other capture-related differences.\n",
        "\n",
        "The study therefore describes displacement across illumination\n",
        "conditions rather than claiming that illumination alone caused\n",
        "the entire displacement.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5. Research Contribution Positioning\n",
        "\n",
        "The manuscript presents a focused empirical characterisation\n",
        "of reference-relative FaceNet embedding displacement across\n",
        "illumination geometry conditions.\n",
        "\n",
        "It contributes descriptive measurements, identity-level\n",
        "comparisons, and statistical evidence within the evaluated\n",
        "Cropped Extended Yale B cohort.\n",
        "\n",
        "It does not propose a new recognition architecture,\n",
        "illumination-normalisation method, or operational drift detector.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 6. Status\n",
        "\n",
        "Research-gap formulation drafted.\n",
        "Novelty remains qualified and requires further literature review."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qjR85z3E8uey"
      }
    },
