    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.3\n",
        "## Research Contributions and Hypothesis Formulation\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. Final Proposed Research Contributions\n",
        "\n",
        "C1 — Identity-Level Empirical Characterisation\n",
        "\n",
        "An empirical characterisation of reference-relative FaceNet\n",
        "embedding displacement across illumination geometry conditions\n",
        "using 38 identities from the Cropped Extended Yale B dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "C2 — Dual-Distance Measurement\n",
        "\n",
        "A comparative examination of Euclidean embedding displacement\n",
        "and cosine distance relative to a common reference capture\n",
        "for each identity.\n",
        "\n",
        "C3 — Repeated-Measures Statistical Evidence\n",
        "\n",
        "An identity-level statistical comparison of near-frontal,\n",
        "oblique, and large-angular illumination groups using\n",
        "Friedman and pairwise Wilcoxon signed-rank tests.\n",
        "\n",
        "C4 — Hemisphere-Based Exploratory Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "An exploratory comparison of frontal and beyond-frontal\n",
        "illumination conditions, accounting for unequal condition\n",
        "counts and geometric confounding.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Retrospective Research Hypotheses\n",
        "\n",
        "IMPORTANT:\n",
        "These hypotheses are formulated during manuscript development,\n",
        "after the experimental analysis was completed. They are not\n",
        "preregistered or prospective hypotheses.\n",
        "\n",
        "H1 — Illumination Geometry Ordering\n",
        "\n",
        "Reference-relative embedding displacement differs across\n",
        "near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular illumination groups.\n",
        "\n",
        "Expected ordering:\n",
        "Near-frontal < Oblique < Large-angular.\n",
        "\n",
        "Evaluated separately using Euclidean displacement\n",
        "and cosine distance.\n",
        "\n",
        "H2 — Identity-Level Consistency\n",
        "\n",
        "The ordering of displacement across illumination groups\n",
        "is consistent across the evaluated identities.\n",
        "\n",
        "Evidence is assessed using identity-level repeated-measures\n",
        "comparisons and the observed direction of pairwise differences.\n",
        "\n",
        "H3 — Hemisphere Comparison\n",
        "\n",
        "Beyond-frontal illumination conditions exhibit greater\n",
        "reference-relative embedding displacement than frontal\n",
        "illumination conditions.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is an exploratory hypothesis because the two groups\n",
        "contain unequal numbers of illumination conditions and\n",
        "are confounded with angular geometry.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. Statistical Evidence Already Available\n",
        "\n",
        "H1:\n",
        "- Friedman repeated-measures tests were significant for\n",
        "  both Euclidean displacement and cosine distance.\n",
        "- All three pairwise comparisons were significant after\n",
        "  Holm correction across the six comparisons.\n",
        "\n",
        "H2:\n",
        "- All 38 identities showed the same direction of difference\n",
        "  for each pairwise illumination-group comparison.\n",
        "- Kendall's W was 1.0 for both metrics.\n",
        "\n",
        "H3:\n",
        "- Beyond-frontal mean displacement was higher for both metrics.\n",
        "- The comparison was exploratory and subject to\n",
        "  unequal-condition and geometric-confounding limitations.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Interpretation Restrictions\n",
        "\n",
        "Statistical significance does not establish:\n",
        "- Recognition accuracy.\n",
        "- Biometric verification reliability.\n",
        "- Causal isolation of illumination effects.\n",
        "- Operational drift detection.\n",
        "- Generalisation to other face-recognition architectures.\n",
        "\n",
        "Kendall's W = 1.0 indicates perfectly consistent group ordering\n",
        "in the evaluated identities; it does not indicate perfect\n",
        "recognition or detector performance.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5. Hypothesis Classification\n",
        "\n",
        "H1: Retrospective, directional empirical hypothesis.\n",
        "H2: Retrospective, identity-consistency hypothesis.\n",
        "H3: Retrospective, exploratory hemisphere hypothesis.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 6. Status\n",
        "\n",
        "Research contributions and retrospective hypotheses documented."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ScEW43fP88Ic"
      }
    },
