    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Abstract\n",
        "\n",
        "Illumination variation remains a significant challenge for face-recognition systems, potentially altering the representations produced by deep neural networks. This study empirically examines reference-relative face embedding displacement across illumination geometry conditions using a fixed pretrained FaceNet architecture. Experiments were conducted on the Cropped Extended Yale B dataset, comprising 38 identities and 2,414 images. A common reference capture was established for each identity, and 2,128 evaluation observations across 56 non-reference illumination conditions were analysed using 512-dimensional embeddings. Euclidean displacement and cosine distance were calculated relative to the corresponding identity reference. Illumination conditions were grouped into near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular categories.\n",
        "\n",
        "Both distance measures exhibited progressively greater displacement across the three illumination groups. Mean Euclidean displacement increased from 0.402 in near-frontal conditions to 0.709 in oblique conditions and 1.118 in large-angular conditions. Corresponding mean cosine distances increased from 0.087 to 0.262 and 0.649. Friedman tests indicated significant differences across groups for both metrics (χ² = 76.0, p = 3.14 × 10⁻¹⁷, Kendall's W = 1.0). All six pairwise comparisons remained significant following Holm correction. An exploratory hemisphere comparison also showed greater mean displacement under beyond-frontal conditions.\n",
        "\n",
        "These findings characterise reference-relative embedding displacement within the evaluated dataset and model. However, the analysis uses different captures rather than exact transformations of identical source images, limiting causal attribution to illumination alone. The results do not establish recognition accuracy, operational drift detection, or generalisation across architectures."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "IGHNzHRj9Lu5"
      }
    },
