        "\n",
        "Deep face-recognition models represent facial images through learned feature embeddings. Changes in facial appearance may therefore be accompanied by changes in embedding-space position. However, the magnitude and consistency of such changes depend on the model, the input images, and the conditions under which the representations are evaluated. An observed embedding displacement should consequently be interpreted as a change in representation rather than direct evidence of incorrect identity recognition.\n",
