        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.7\n",
        "## Introduction Consolidation and Consistency Audit\n",
        "\n",
        "### Purpose\n",
        "\n",
        "This step combines the five previously drafted introduction sections into one manuscript-ready working draft.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Sections to consolidate\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Background: Face Recognition and Deep Face Embeddings.\n",
        "2. Illumination Variation and Its Effect on Facial Representations.\n",
        "3. Research Gap and Motivation.\n",
        "4. Research Questions and Objectives.\n",
        "5. Study Contributions and Scope.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Consistency requirements\n",
        "\n",
        "- Preserve the established research questions and objectives.\n",
        "- Use consistent terminology for reference-relative embedding displacement.\n",
        "- Distinguish Euclidean displacement from cosine distance.\n",
        "- Distinguish the total image count from common-condition and evaluation counts.\n",
        "- Describe illumination groups as angular geometry categories.\n",
        "- Preserve the distinction between primary and exploratory analyses.\n",
        "- Disclose that the hypotheses were formulated retrospectively.\n",
        "- Avoid unsupported novelty, causality, recognition-accuracy, and generalisation claims.\n",
        "- Identify citations that still require bibliographic verification.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Deliverables\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Consolidated introduction in Markdown.\n",
        "2. Consolidated introduction in JSON.\n",
        "3. Introduction consistency audit.\n",
        "4. Word-count and section-count verification.\n",
        "\n",
        "The consolidated draft remains subject to citation verification and final editorial review."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HDlqMSZnAv0H"
      }
