        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.8\n",
        "## Citation Verification and Claim-to-Source Audit\n",
        "\n",
        "### Verified References\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Moses, Y., Adini, Y., and Ullman, S. (1994).\n",
        "   \"Face Recognition: The Problem of Compensating for Changes in Illumination Direction.\"\n",
        "   In: Computer Vision — ECCV 1994, pp. 286–296.\n",
        "   DOI: 10.1007/3-540-57956-7_33.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Beveridge, J. R., Draper, B. A., Chang, J.-M., Kirby, M., Kley, H., and Peterson, C. (2009).\n",
        "   \"Principal Angles Separate Subject Illumination Spaces in YDB and CMU-PIE.\"\n",
        "   IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence, 31(2), 351–363.\n",
        "   DOI: 10.1109/TPAMI.2008.200.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Han, H., Shan, S., Chen, X., and Gao, W. (2013).\n",
        "   \"A Comparative Study on Illumination Preprocessing in Face Recognition.\"\n",
        "   Pattern Recognition, 46(6), 1691–1699.\n",
        "   DOI: 10.1016/j.patcog.2012.11.022.\n",
        "\n",
        "4. Ochoa-Villegas, M. A., Nolazco-Flores, J. A., Barron-Cano, O., and Kakadiaris, I. A. (2015).\n",
        "   \"Addressing the Illumination Challenge in Two-Dimensional Face Recognition: A Survey.\"\n",
        "   IET Computer Vision, 9(6), 978–992.\n",
        "   DOI: 10.1049/iet-cvi.2014.0086.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Claim-to-Source Assessment\n",
        "\n",
        "- Moses et al. (1994): supports illumination-direction effects and within-person image variation.\n",
        "- Beveridge et al. (2009): supports subject-specific illumination subspaces and principal-angle analysis using Yale B and CMU-PIE.\n",
        "- Han et al. (2013): supports comparative evaluation of illumination preprocessing methods.\n",
        "- Ochoa-Villegas et al. (2015): supports the broader historical review of illumination challenges and approaches.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Required Editorial Corrections\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Do not describe Beveridge et al. as validating the exact three angular groups used in this experiment.\n",
        "2. Do not use these four references alone to substantiate the precise angular grouping thresholds.\n",
        "3. Retain the distinction between the 1994 ECCV conference paper by Moses et al. and the separate 1997 TPAMI publication with a similar title.\n",
        "4. Verify any additional source used to support the specific angular grouping methodology.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Verification Status\n",
        "\n",
        "Bibliographic details: verified.\n",
        "General claim support: verified.\n",
        "Exact angular-grouping claim: additional source required.\n",
        "Novelty established: no."
      ],
