      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.8.1\n",
        "## Verification of Angular Illumination Grouping in Prior Research\n",
        "\n",
        "### Source\n",
        "\n",
        "Ochoa-Villegas, M. A., Nolazco-Flores, J. A., Barron-Cano, O., and Kakadiaris, I. A. (2015).\n",
        "\n",
        "\"Addressing the Illumination Challenge in Two-Dimensional Face Recognition: A Survey.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "IET Computer Vision, 9(6), 978–992.\n",
        "\n",
        "DOI: 10.1049/iet-cvi.2014.0086\n",
        "\n",
        "### Verified literature finding\n",
        "\n",
        "The survey describes Yale Face Database B experiments that divide illumination conditions into five subsets according to the angle between the light-source direction and camera axis:\n",
        "\n",
        "- S1: 0°–12°\n",
        "- S2: 13°–25°\n",
        "- S3: 26°–50°\n",
        "- S4: 51°–77°\n",
        "- S5: greater than 78°\n",
        "\n",
        "### Relationship to Experiment 20\n",
        "\n",
        "This source establishes precedent for analysing Yale B illumination conditions using angular groupings.\n",
        "\n",
        "Experiment 20 uses three different groups:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Near-frontal: theta ≤ 30°.\n",
        "- Oblique: 30° < theta ≤ 60°.\n",
        "- Large angular deviation: theta > 60°.\n",
        "\n",
        "These thresholds are not identical to the five subsets described in the survey.\n",
        "\n",
        "The survey supports the general use of angular illumination grouping, but does not independently validate the exact three-group thresholds or the angular formula used in Experiment 20.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Decision\n",
        "\n",
        "The general angular-grouping precedent is supported by prior literature.\n",
        "\n",
        "The exact three-group classification remains a study-specific analytical design.\n",
        "\n",
        "Novelty is not established."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zATe5hPWDq9L"
      }
    },
