        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.8.2\n",
        "## Consolidated Introduction: Citation Integration\n",
        "\n",
        "### Required revision\n",
        "\n",
        "Update Section 1.2 to include the established precedent for angular illumination grouping in Yale B research.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Citation integration\n",
        "\n",
        "Ochoa-Villegas et al. (2015) describe Yale Face Database B illumination subsets classified according to the angle between the light-source direction and camera axis.\n",
        "\n",
        "The reported five subsets are:\n",
        "\n",
        "- 0°–12°\n",
        "- 13°–25°\n",
        "- 26°–50°\n",
        "- 51°–77°\n",
        "- Above 77°\n",
        "\n",
        "Experiment 20 uses a different three-group classification:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Near-frontal: θ ≤ 30°.\n",
        "- Oblique: 30° < θ ≤ 60°.\n",
        "- Large angular deviation: θ > 60°.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Editorial requirement\n",
        "\n",
        "Present the published five-subset classification as prior research and the three-group classification as the analytical design adopted in Experiment 20.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not imply that the published study validates the exact thresholds used in this experiment.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Deliverables\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Updated consolidated introduction.\n",
        "2. Updated citation inventory.\n",
        "3. Citation integration audit.\n",
        "4. JSON and Markdown reload verification."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "F6mZBpKGEXD9"
      }
    },
