        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.9.1\n",
        "## Methodology: Research Design and Experimental Overview\n",
        "\n",
        "This subsection establishes the research design, analytical framework, evaluation population, and scope of the experiment.\n",
        "\n",
        "The manuscript will describe the work as a descriptive empirical investigation of reference-relative face-embedding displacement across illumination geometry conditions. The text must distinguish the experimental observations from operational drift detection, biometric recognition performance, and causal claims about illumination."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "JTXVuD2aJaHW"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import re\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\")\n",
        "STEP_DIR = BASE / \"step_3_3\"\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = STEP_DIR / \"step_3391\"\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Methodology subsection draft\n",
        "section_title = \"3.1 Research Design and Experimental Overview\"\n",
        "\n",
        "section_text = \"\"\"\n",
        "Experiment 20 employed a descriptive empirical design to examine reference-relative displacement in deep face-recognition embeddings across illumination geometry conditions. The analysis focused on the extent to which the embedding representation of an identity's facial image differed from that identity's embedding under a designated reference illumination condition. Rather than developing or evaluating an operational drift-detection algorithm, the experiment characterised these differences using two distance measures: Euclidean displacement and cosine distance.\n",
        "\n",
        "The evaluation used the Cropped Extended Yale B dataset, comprising 2,414 standard-illumination images from 38 identities. A common-condition selection procedure identified 57 illumination conditions represented across all 38 identities, yielding 2,166 identity-condition observations. One observation per identity corresponded to the designated reference condition, A+000E+00. These 38 reference observations were used to establish the identity-specific reference embeddings. After excluding the reference condition, the primary evaluation comprised 2,128 non-reference observations across 56 illumination conditions.\n",
        "\n",
        "The primary unit of observation was an identity-condition pair, while identity served as the repeated-measures unit for group-level statistical comparisons. This structure allowed displacement measurements from the same 38 identities to be examined across near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular-deviation illumination groups. The observations represent identity-condition-matched captures under different illumination conditions; they are not pairs produced by applying controlled transformations to identical source images.\n",
        "\n",
        "The analysis was conducted using 512-dimensional embeddings generated by a fixed pretrained InceptionResnetV1 model with VGGFace2 weights. Each evaluation embedding was compared with the corresponding identity's reference embedding. Euclidean displacement and cosine distance were then summarised across illumination geometry groups and examined using identity-level repeated-measures statistical procedures.\n",
        "\n",
        "The study was intentionally restricted to descriptive embedding-space analysis. It did not estimate calibrated detection thresholds, operational false-alarm rates, or recognition accuracy. It also did not evaluate an independent face-recognition architecture. Consequently, the results characterise reference-relative embedding displacement within the selected dataset, preprocessing procedure, and pretrained model; they do not establish that illumination alone caused the observed differences or that the findings generalise to other recognition systems.\n",
        "\"\"\".strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Core facts to be checked against the frozen protocol.\n",
        "expected_facts = {\n",
        "    \"dataset\": \"Cropped Extended Yale B\",\n",
        "    \"source_images\": 2414,\n",
        "    \"identities\": 38,\n",
        "    \"common_conditions\": 57,\n",
        "    \"common_condition_observations\": 2166,\n",
        "    \"reference_condition\": \"A+000E+00\",\n",
        "    \"reference_observations\": 38,\n",
        "    \"evaluation_conditions\": 56,\n",
        "    \"evaluation_observations\": 2128,\n",
        "    \"embedding_dimension\": 512,\n",
        "    \"model\": \"InceptionResnetV1\",\n",
        "    \"pretrained_weights\": \"VGGFace2\",\n",
        "    \"analysis_type\": \"descriptive empirical analysis\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "checks = {\n",
        "    \"descriptive_empirical_design_stated\":\n",
        "        \"descriptive empirical design\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"dataset_name_stated\":\n",
        "        expected_facts[\"dataset\"] in section_text,\n",
        "    \"2414_source_images_stated\":\n",
        "        \"2,414\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"38_identities_stated\":\n",
        "        \"38 identities\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"2166_common_observations_stated\":\n",
        "        \"2,166\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"57_common_conditions_stated\":\n",
        "        \"57 illumination conditions\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"reference_condition_stated\":\n",
        "        expected_facts[\"reference_condition\"] in section_text,\n",
        "    \"2128_evaluation_observations_stated\":\n",
        "        \"2,128\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"56_evaluation_conditions_stated\":\n",
        "        \"56 illumination conditions\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"repeated_measures_unit_identified\":\n",
        "        \"identity served as the repeated-measures unit\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"different_capture_limitation_stated\":\n",
        "        \"not pairs produced by applying controlled transformations\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"embedding_dimension_stated\":\n",
        "        \"512-dimensional embeddings\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"model_and_weights_stated\":\n",
        "        \"InceptionResnetV1 model with VGGFace2 weights\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"euclidean_and_cosine_metrics_stated\":\n",
        "        \"Euclidean displacement and cosine distance\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"no_operational_detection_claim\":\n",
        "        \"operational false-alarm rates\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"no_recognition_accuracy_claim\":\n",
        "        \"recognition accuracy\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"no_independent_architecture_claim\":\n",
        "        \"independent face-recognition architecture\" in section_text\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "word_count = len(re.findall(r\"\\b[\\w'-]+\\b\", section_text))\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_content = f\"# {section_title}\\n\\n{section_text}\\n\"\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_methodology_3_1_research_design.md\"\n",
        "json_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_step3391_research_design.json\"\n",
        "audit_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_step3391_research_design_audit.json\"\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_path.write_text(markdown_content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "\n",
        "record = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": \"Experiment 20\",\n",
        "    \"phase\": \"3.3\",\n",
        "    \"step\": \"3.3.9.1\",\n",
        "    \"subsection\": section_title,\n",
        "    \"created_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"research_design\": \"Descriptive empirical analysis\",\n",
        "    \"draft_text\": section_text,\n",
        "    \"verified_protocol_facts\": expected_facts,\n",
        "    \"word_count\": word_count,\n",
        "    \"checks\": checks,\n",
        "    \"passed_checks\": sum(checks.values()),\n",
        "    \"total_checks\": len(checks),\n",
        "    \"failed_checks\": [\n",
        "        name for name, passed in checks.items() if not passed\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"status\": (\n",
        "        \"DRAFT_CONSISTENCY_CHECK_PASSED\"\n",
        "        if all(checks.values())\n",
        "        else \"DRAFT_REQUIRES_REVIEW\"\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"limitations_preserved\": [\n",
        "        \"Different captures across illumination conditions, not exact source-image transformations\",\n",
        "        \"Descriptive embedding displacement, not operational drift detection\",\n",
        "        \"No recognition-accuracy evaluation\",\n",
        "        \"No independent architecture evaluation\",\n",
        "        \"No causal attribution to illumination alone\"\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "json_path.write_text(\n",
        "    json.dumps(record, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False),\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "audit = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": \"Experiment 20\",\n",
        "    \"step\": \"3.3.9.1\",\n",
        "    \"created_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"word_count\": word_count,\n",
        "    \"checks\": checks,\n",
        "    \"passed_checks\": sum(checks.values()),\n",
        "    \"total_checks\": len(checks),\n",
        "    \"failed_checks\": record[\"failed_checks\"],\n",
        "    \"status\": record[\"status\"],\n",
        "    \"files\": {\n",
        "        \"markdown\": str(markdown_path),\n",
        "        \"json\": str(json_path)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "audit_path.write_text(\n",
        "    json.dumps(audit, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False),\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Reload and verify saved artifacts.\n",
        "reloaded_markdown = markdown_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "reloaded_record = json.loads(json_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n",
        "reloaded_audit = json.loads(audit_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "assert reloaded_markdown == markdown_content\n",
        "assert reloaded_record == record\n",
        "assert reloaded_audit == audit\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 88)\n",
        "print(\"EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.3.9.1\")\n",
        "print(\"RESEARCH DESIGN AND EXPERIMENTAL OVERVIEW\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 88)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nWord count:\", word_count)\n",
        "print(\"\\nConsistency checks:\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for name, passed in checks.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"{name}: {'PASS' if passed else 'FAIL'}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\nPassed: {record['passed_checks']} / {record['total_checks']}\")\n",
        "print(\"Failed:\", len(record[\"failed_checks\"]))\n",
        "print(\"Status:\", record[\"status\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nMarkdown reload: PASS\")\n",
        "print(\"JSON reload: PASS\")\n",
        "print(\"Audit reload: PASS\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nSaved files:\")\n",
        "print(markdown_path)\n",
        "print(json_path)\n",
        "print(audit_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 88)\n",
        "print(\"DRAFT TEXT\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 88)\n",
        "print(markdown_content)\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 88)"
      ],
