      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.9.3\n",
        "## Methodology: Subject Selection and Illumination-Condition Coverage\n",
        "\n",
        "This subsection describes the identity cohort, common-condition selection, reference-condition assignment, and construction of the evaluation observations.\n",
        "\n",
        "The analysis included 38 identities. Although the standard-illumination dataset contained 64 distinct conditions, only 57 were represented for every identity. The common-condition subset was therefore used to maintain complete identity coverage.\n",
        "\n",
        "The reference condition, A+000E+00, contributed one reference observation per identity. The remaining 56 conditions formed the evaluation set. The resulting design contained 38 reference observations and 2,128 non-reference evaluation observations.\n",
        "\n",
        "The three illumination geometry groups were assigned using the frozen condition manifest. The groups describe the angular deviation of the light-source direction and should not be interpreted as measured illumination intensity."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "wDb16jB0J13a"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import re\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\")\n",
        "STEP_DIR = BASE / \"step_3_3\"\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = STEP_DIR / \"step_3393\"\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "section_title = \"3.3 Subject Selection and Illumination-Condition Coverage\"\n",
        "\n",
        "section_text = \"\"\"\n",
        "The subject cohort comprised 38 identities represented in the Cropped Extended Yale B frontal-pose illumination subset. The standard-illumination image collection contained 64 distinct illumination conditions across the cohort; however, not every condition was available for every identity. Seven identities had incomplete condition coverage. To preserve a consistent identity set across the primary condition-based comparisons, the analysis retained only conditions represented for all 38 identities.\n",
        "\n",
        "This complete-case condition selection produced 57 common illumination conditions and 2,166 identity-condition observations, corresponding to 38 observations for each condition. The selection was based on shared condition availability rather than on embedding displacement values or statistical outcomes. Conditions not represented across all 38 identities were excluded from analyses requiring complete identity-condition coverage.\n",
        "\n",
        "The condition A+000E+00 was designated as the reference condition. One reference observation was available for each of the 38 identities, providing an identity-specific reference embedding. The reference observations were retained for calculating reference-relative distances but excluded from the non-reference evaluation set. Consequently, the primary evaluation comprised the remaining 56 common conditions and 2,128 identity-condition observations.\n",
        "\n",
        "The 56 non-reference conditions were assigned to three illumination geometry groups using the frozen condition-grouping manifest: near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular-deviation. The corresponding evaluation counts were 17, 11, and 28 conditions, respectively, representing 646, 418, and 1,064 observations. The reference condition belonged to the near-frontal group but was excluded from these evaluation counts.\n",
        "\n",
        "The geometry groups represent the angular deviation of the illumination direction relative to the camera axis, as defined by the study's condition-grouping procedure. They do not represent directly measured illumination intensity. The same 38 identities were represented in each of the three evaluation groups, enabling identity-level repeated-measures comparisons. The resulting observations are identity-condition-matched captures under different lighting conditions, not exact image-level pairs generated from a single source image.\n",
        "\"\"\".strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "facts = {\n",
        "    \"identity_count\": 38,\n",
        "    \"standard_illumination_condition_count\": 64,\n",
        "    \"incomplete_identity_count\": 7,\n",
        "    \"common_condition_count\": 57,\n",
        "    \"common_condition_observation_count\": 2166,\n",
        "    \"observations_per_common_condition\": 38,\n",
        "    \"reference_condition\": \"A+000E+00\",\n",
        "    \"reference_observation_count\": 38,\n",
        "    \"evaluation_condition_count\": 56,\n",
        "    \"evaluation_observation_count\": 2128,\n",
        "    \"evaluation_groups\": {\n",
        "        \"near_frontal\": {\n",
        "            \"conditions\": 17,\n",
        "            \"observations\": 646\n",
        "        },\n",
        "        \"oblique\": {\n",
        "            \"conditions\": 11,\n",
        "            \"observations\": 418\n",
        "        },\n",
        "        \"large_angular_deviation\": {\n",
        "            \"conditions\": 28,\n",
        "            \"observations\": 1064\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"grouping_interpretation\": \"Angular deviation of illumination direction, not measured intensity\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "checks = {\n",
        "    \"38_identity_cohort_stated\":\n",
        "        \"38 identities\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"64_total_conditions_stated\":\n",
        "        \"64 distinct illumination conditions\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"seven_incomplete_identities_stated\":\n",
        "        \"Seven identities\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"57_common_conditions_stated\":\n",
        "        \"57 common illumination conditions\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"2166_common_observations_stated\":\n",
        "        \"2,166 identity-condition observations\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"complete_case_selection_explained\":\n",
        "        \"represented for all 38 identities\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"reference_condition_correct\":\n",
        "        \"A+000E+00\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"38_reference_observations_stated\":\n",
        "        \"38 reference observations\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"56_evaluation_conditions_stated\":\n",
        "        \"56 common conditions\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"2128_evaluation_observations_stated\":\n",
        "        \"2,128 identity-condition observations\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"three_geometry_groups_named\": all(\n",
        "        group in section_text\n",
        "        for group in [\n",
        "            \"near-frontal\",\n",
        "            \"oblique\",\n",
        "            \"large-angular-deviation\"\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"group_condition_and_observation_counts_stated\": all(\n",
        "        value in section_text\n",
        "        for value in [\n",
        "            \"17, 11, and 28 conditions\",\n",
        "            \"646, 418, and 1,064 observations\"\n",
