      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.9.5\n",
        "## Methodology: Face-Image Preprocessing\n",
        "\n",
        "This subsection documents the image preprocessing procedure applied before embedding extraction.\n",
        "\n",
        "The description must reflect the frozen Stage 2 preprocessing record. It must not imply that MTCNN detection or facial alignment was performed. The distinction between implicit torchvision resize defaults and explicitly configured parameters must also be preserved."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cMPbVH9IKVQb"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import re\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\")\n",
        "STEP_DIR = BASE / \"step_3_3\"\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = STEP_DIR / \"step_3395\"\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "section_title = \"3.4 Face-Image Preprocessing\"\n",
        "\n",
        "section_text = \"\"\"\n",
        "The Cropped Extended Yale B images were supplied as grayscale PGM files. Before embedding extraction, each image was converted to an RGB representation by replicating its grayscale channel across the three colour channels. The resulting images were resized directly to 160 × 160 pixels and converted to tensors using torchvision.transforms.ToTensor().\n",
        "\n",
        "Face detection and facial alignment were not applied during this preprocessing stage. An initial MTCNN compatibility test detected only one face in twelve tested Yale B images. Consequently, the experiment used direct image resizing rather than MTCNN-based detection and alignment. This decision was consistent with the cropped-image format of the selected dataset, but it means that the preprocessing procedure should not be described as a face-detection or landmark-alignment pipeline.\n",
        "\n",
        "The original resize operation did not explicitly specify interpolation or antialiasing arguments. The recorded torchvision version was 0.29.1+cpu, for which the applicable Resize defaults were bilinear interpolation and antialiasing enabled. These settings are therefore documented as library defaults rather than as manually specified experimental parameters.\n",
        "\n",
        "This preprocessing procedure differs from the MTCNN-based preprocessing used in Experiment 18. Accordingly, results obtained from the two experimental stages should not be treated as directly interchangeable without accounting for their different image-processing procedures.\n",
        "\"\"\".strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "facts = {\n",
        "    \"input_format\": \"PGM\",\n",
        "    \"input_image_type\": \"grayscale\",\n",
        "    \"grayscale_to_rgb\": \"replicate grayscale channel across three channels\",\n",
        "    \"resize_dimensions\": [160, 160],\n",
        "    \"tensor_conversion\": \"torchvision.transforms.ToTensor()\",\n",
        "    \"face_detection_used\": False,\n",
        "    \"face_alignment_used\": False,\n",
        "    \"mtcnn_compatibility_test\": {\n",
        "        \"detected_faces\": 1,\n",
        "        \"tested_images\": 12\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"torchvision_version\": \"0.29.1+cpu\",\n",
        "    \"resize_interpolation_default\": \"bilinear\",\n",
        "    \"resize_antialias_default\": True,\n",
        "    \"resize_arguments_explicitly_configured\": False,\n",
        "    \"difference_from_experiment_18\": \"Experiment 18 used MTCNN-based preprocessing\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "checks = {\n",
        "    \"pgm_grayscale_input_documented\":\n",
        "        \"grayscale PGM files\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"channel_replication_documented\":\n",
        "        \"replicating its grayscale channel across the three colour channels\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"resize_dimensions_correct\":\n",
        "        \"160 × 160 pixels\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"tensor_conversion_documented\":\n",
        "        \"torchvision.transforms.ToTensor()\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"no_face_detection_claimed\":\n",
        "        \"Face detection and facial alignment were not applied\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"mtcnn_test_result_correct\":\n",
        "        \"only one face in twelve tested\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"direct_resize_reason_documented\":\n",
        "        \"direct image resizing rather than MTCNN-based detection and alignment\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"implicit_resize_defaults_distinguished\":\n",
        "        \"did not explicitly specify interpolation or antialiasing arguments\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"bilinear_default_documented\":\n",
        "        \"bilinear interpolation\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"antialias_default_documented\":\n",
        "        \"antialiasing enabled\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"torchvision_version_documented\":\n",
        "        \"0.29.1+cpu\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"difference_from_experiment18_documented\":\n",
        "        \"differs from the MTCNN-based preprocessing used in Experiment 18\" in section_text\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "word_count = len(re.findall(r\"\\b[\\w'-]+\\b\", section_text))\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_content = f\"# {section_title}\\n\\n{section_text}\\n\"\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_methodology_3_4_face_preprocessing.md\"\n",
        "json_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_step3395_face_preprocessing.json\"\n",
        "audit_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_step3395_face_preprocessing_audit.json\"\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_path.write_text(markdown_content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "\n",
        "record = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": \"Experiment 20\",\n",
        "    \"phase\": \"3.3\",\n",
        "    \"step\": \"3.3.9.5\",\n",
        "    \"subsection\": section_title,\n",
        "    \"created_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"draft_text\": section_text,\n",
        "    \"verified_preprocessing_facts\": facts,\n",
        "    \"word_count\": word_count,\n",
        "    \"checks\": checks,\n",
        "    \"passed_checks\": sum(checks.values()),\n",
        "    \"total_checks\": len(checks),\n",
        "    \"failed_checks\": [\n",
        "        name for name, passed in checks.items() if not passed\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"status\": (\n",
        "        \"DRAFT_CONSISTENCY_CHECK_PASSED\"\n",
        "        if all(checks.values())\n",
        "        else \"DRAFT_REQUIRES_REVIEW\"\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"methodological_limitations\": [\n",
        "        \"No MTCNN face detection was applied.\",\n",
        "        \"No facial alignment was applied.\",\n",
        "        \"Resize interpolation and antialiasing were implicit library defaults.\",\n",
        "        \"Preprocessing differs from Experiment 18.\"\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "json_path.write_text(\n",
        "    json.dumps(record, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False),\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "audit = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": \"Experiment 20\",\n",
        "    \"step\": \"3.3.9.5\",\n",
        "    \"created_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"word_count\": word_count,\n",
        "    \"checks\": checks,\n",
        "    \"passed_checks\": sum(checks.values()),\n",
        "    \"total_checks\": len(checks),\n",
        "    \"failed_checks\": record[\"failed_checks\"],\n",
        "    \"status\": record[\"status\"],\n",
        "    \"files\": {\n",
        "        \"markdown\": str(markdown_path),\n",
        "        \"json\": str(json_path)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "audit_path.write_text(\n",
        "    json.dumps(audit, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False),\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Reload and verify all saved artifacts.\n",
        "assert markdown_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == markdown_content\n",
        "assert json.loads(json_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")) == record\n",
        "assert json.loads(audit_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")) == audit\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 88)\n",
        "print(\"EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.3.9.5\")\n",
        "print(\"FACE-IMAGE PREPROCESSING\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 88)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nWord count:\", word_count)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nConsistency checks:\")\n",
        "for name, passed in checks.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"{name}: {'PASS' if passed else 'FAIL'}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\nPassed: {record['passed_checks']} / {record['total_checks']}\")\n",
        "print(\"Failed:\", len(record[\"failed_checks\"]))\n",
        "print(\"Status:\", record[\"status\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nMarkdown reload: PASS\")\n",
        "print(\"JSON reload: PASS\")\n",
        "print(\"Audit reload: PASS\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nSaved files:\")\n",
        "print(markdown_path)\n",
        "print(json_path)\n",
        "print(audit_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 88)\n",
        "print(\"DRAFT TEXT\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 88)\n",
        "print(markdown_content)\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 88)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
