        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.9.6\n",
        "## Methodology: FaceNet Architecture and Embedding Extraction\n",
        "\n",
        "This subsection documents the pretrained face-recognition architecture and embedding extraction procedure used in Stage 2. The description must distinguish the model architecture and pretrained training source from the unavailable exact weight-file checksum."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "oqPaf2MrK-g_"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import re\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\")\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = BASE / \"step_3_3\" / \"step_3396\"\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "section_title = \"3.5 FaceNet Architecture and Embedding Extraction\"\n",
        "\n",
        "section_text = \"\"\"\n",
        "Face embeddings were generated using the InceptionResnetV1 architecture implemented in facenet-pytorch, with pretrained weights associated with the VGGFace2 training dataset. The model was used as a fixed pretrained feature extractor rather than being fine-tuned on the Cropped Extended Yale B images. The same model configuration was applied throughout the Stage 2 embedding extraction procedure.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model produced a 512-dimensional embedding for each preprocessed image. Embedding extraction was performed with the model in evaluation mode, and gradient computation was disabled. These settings were used to obtain feature representations without updating model parameters during inference. The extracted embeddings were L2-normalised, providing the representations used in the subsequent reference-relative distance calculations.\n",
        "\n",
        "The recorded software environment included Python 3.13.18, PyTorch 2.14.1+cpu, torchvision 0.29.1+cpu, and facenet-pytorch 2.6.0. The embedding-generation procedure used the pretrained InceptionResnetV1 model configured for VGGFace2 weights.\n",
        "\n",
        "Although the model architecture, pretrained training source, software versions, output dimensionality, and inference settings were recorded, the exact pretrained weight-file identity and its SHA256 checksum were not preserved. Consequently, the model configuration is documented at the architecture and pretrained-source level, but exact weight-file reproducibility cannot be independently established from the retained records.\n",
        "\n",
        "The resulting embeddings were retained with row-aligned image and identity metadata, including filenames, subject identifiers, illumination azimuths, elevations, and condition labels. These records enabled each non-reference embedding to be associated with the corresponding identity-specific reference representation during the displacement analysis.\n",
        "\"\"\".strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "facts = {\n",
        "    \"architecture\": \"InceptionResnetV1\",\n",
        "    \"implementation\": \"facenet-pytorch\",\n",
        "    \"facenet_pytorch_version\": \"2.6.0\",\n",
        "    \"pretrained_source\": \"VGGFace2\",\n",
        "    \"fine_tuning_on_yaleb\": False,\n",
        "    \"embedding_dimension\": 512,\n",
        "    \"model_evaluation_mode\": True,\n",
        "    \"gradient_computation_disabled\": True,\n",
        "    \"l2_normalisation\": True,\n",
        "    \"python_version\": \"3.13.18\",\n",
        "    \"pytorch_version\": \"2.14.1+cpu\",\n",
        "    \"torchvision_version\": \"0.29.1+cpu\",\n",
        "    \"exact_weight_file_identity_preserved\": False,\n",
        "    \"exact_weight_file_sha256_preserved\": False,\n",
        "    \"metadata_arrays\": [\n",
        "        \"filenames\",\n",
        "        \"subjects\",\n",
        "        \"subject_numbers\",\n",
        "        \"azimuths\",\n",
        "        \"elevations\",\n",
        "        \"conditions\"\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "checks = {\n",
        "    \"architecture_correct\":\n",
        "        \"InceptionResnetV1\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"implementation_correct\":\n",
        "        \"facenet-pytorch\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"pretrained_source_correct\":\n",
        "        \"VGGFace2\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"fixed_feature_extractor_documented\":\n",
        "        \"rather than being fine-tuned\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"embedding_dimension_correct\":\n",
        "        \"512-dimensional embedding\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"evaluation_mode_documented\":\n",
        "        \"evaluation mode\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"gradients_disabled_documented\":\n",
        "        \"gradient computation was disabled\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"l2_normalisation_documented\":\n",
        "        \"L2-normalised\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"python_version_correct\":\n",
        "        \"Python 3.13.18\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"pytorch_version_correct\":\n",
        "        \"PyTorch 2.14.1+cpu\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"torchvision_version_correct\":\n",
        "        \"torchvision 0.29.1+cpu\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"facenet_version_correct\":\n",
        "        \"facenet-pytorch 2.6.0\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"missing_weight_hash_disclosed\":\n",
        "        \"SHA256 checksum were not preserved\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"no_exact_weight_reproducibility_claim\":\n",
        "        \"cannot be independently established\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"row_aligned_metadata_documented\":\n",
        "        \"row-aligned image and identity metadata\" in section_text\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "word_count = len(re.findall(r\"\\b[\\w'-]+\\b\", section_text))\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_content = f\"# {section_title}\\n\\n{section_text}\\n\"\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_methodology_3_5_facenet_embedding_extraction.md\"\n",
        "json_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_step3396_facenet_embedding_extraction.json\"\n",
        "audit_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_step3396_facenet_embedding_extraction_audit.json\"\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_path.write_text(markdown_content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "\n",
        "record = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": \"Experiment 20\",\n",
        "    \"phase\": \"3.3\",\n",
        "    \"step\": \"3.3.9.6\",\n",
        "    \"subsection\": section_title,\n",
        "    \"created_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"draft_text\": section_text,\n",
        "    \"verified_model_facts\": facts,\n",
        "    \"word_count\": word_count,\n",
        "    \"checks\": checks,\n",
        "    \"passed_checks\": sum(checks.values()),\n",
        "    \"total_checks\": len(checks),\n",
        "    \"failed_checks\": [\n",
        "        name for name, passed in checks.items() if not passed\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"status\": (\n",
        "        \"DRAFT_CONSISTENCY_CHECK_PASSED\"\n",
        "        if all(checks.values())\n",
        "        else \"DRAFT_REQUIRES_REVIEW\"\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"reproducibility_limitation\": (\n",
        "        \"Exact pretrained weight-file identity and SHA256 checksum \"\n",
        "        \"were not preserved.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "json_path.write_text(\n",
        "    json.dumps(record, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False),\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "audit = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": \"Experiment 20\",\n",
        "    \"step\": \"3.3.9.6\",\n",
        "    \"created_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"word_count\": word_count,\n",
        "    \"checks\": checks,\n",
        "    \"passed_checks\": sum(checks.values()),\n",
        "    \"total_checks\": len(checks),\n",
        "    \"failed_checks\": record[\"failed_checks\"],\n",
        "    \"status\": record[\"status\"],\n",
        "    \"files\": {\n",
        "        \"markdown\": str(markdown_path),\n",
        "        \"json\": str(json_path)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "audit_path.write_text(\n",
        "    json.dumps(audit, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False),\n",
