        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.9.8\n",
        "## Methodology: Illumination Geometry Classification\n",
        "\n",
        "This subsection documents the angular geometry calculation and the three illumination groups used in the Stage 2 analysis. The classification describes the direction of illumination relative to the camera-facing orientation. It does not represent illumination intensity or exposure level."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ea-6uPZjLmDx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import re\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\")\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = BASE / \"step_3_3\" / \"step_3398\"\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "section_title = \"3.7 Illumination Geometry Classification\"\n",
        "\n",
        "section_text = \"\"\"\n",
        "Illumination conditions were grouped according to the angular deviation of the light source from the camera-facing direction. The angular deviation, denoted by θ, was calculated from the recorded illumination azimuth and elevation angles using θ = cos⁻¹(cos(elevation) × cos(azimuth)). The angular values were expressed in degrees for interpretation and grouping.\n",
        "\n",
        "Three study-specific illumination geometry groups were defined. Near-frontal conditions comprised observations with θ ≤ 30°. Oblique conditions comprised observations with 30° < θ ≤ 60°. Large-angular conditions comprised observations with θ > 60°. These mutually exclusive intervals assigned each evaluated illumination condition to one geometry group.\n",
        "\n",
        "Across the 56 non-reference evaluation conditions, 17 conditions were classified as near-frontal, 11 as oblique, and 28 as large-angular. Across the 38 identities, these groups contained 646, 418, and 1,064 evaluation observations, respectively. All three groups therefore included observations from the same 38 identities, supporting the repeated-measures comparisons conducted at the identity level.\n",
        "\n",
        "The groups represent the angular geometry of the illumination direction rather than its intensity. They should not be interpreted as brightness levels, exposure categories, or measurements of lighting power. The three angular boundaries were selected for this study and are not presented as universal or standard illumination categories. Previous face-recognition research has used angular subsets to examine illumination variation, but the thresholds and grouping scheme used here are study-specific.\n",
        "\"\"\".strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "facts = {\n",
        "    \"angular_deviation_symbol\": \"theta\",\n",
        "    \"angular_deviation_formula\": \"acos(cos(elevation) * cos(azimuth))\",\n",
        "    \"angle_unit\": \"degrees\",\n",
        "    \"groups\": {\n",
        "        \"near_frontal\": {\n",
        "            \"rule\": \"theta <= 30 degrees\",\n",
        "            \"conditions\": 17,\n",
        "            \"observations\": 646\n",
        "        },\n",
        "        \"oblique\": {\n",
        "            \"rule\": \"30 degrees < theta <= 60 degrees\",\n",
        "            \"conditions\": 11,\n",
        "            \"observations\": 418\n",
        "        },\n",
        "        \"large_angular\": {\n",
        "            \"rule\": \"theta > 60 degrees\",\n",
        "            \"conditions\": 28,\n",
        "            \"observations\": 1064\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"evaluation_conditions\": 56,\n",
        "    \"evaluation_observations\": 2128,\n",
        "    \"identities\": 38,\n",
        "    \"all_groups_include_same_identities\": True,\n",
        "    \"groups_measure\": \"illumination direction geometry\",\n",
        "    \"groups_do_not_measure\": \"illumination intensity\",\n",
        "    \"thresholds_are_study_specific\": True\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "checks = {\n",
        "    \"angular_formula_documented\":\n",
        "        \"cos⁻¹(cos(elevation) × cos(azimuth))\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"angle_unit_documented\":\n",
        "        \"expressed in degrees\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"near_frontal_threshold_correct\":\n",
        "        \"θ ≤ 30°\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"oblique_threshold_correct\":\n",
        "        \"30° < θ ≤ 60°\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"large_angular_threshold_correct\":\n",
        "        \"θ > 60°\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"near_frontal_counts_correct\":\n",
        "        \"17 conditions\" in section_text and \"646\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"oblique_counts_correct\":\n",
        "        \"11 as oblique\" in section_text and \"418\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"large_angular_counts_correct\":\n",
        "        \"28 as large-angular\" in section_text and \"1,064\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"all_38_identities_documented\":\n",
        "        \"same 38 identities\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"geometry_not_intensity_distinction\":\n",
        "        \"rather than its intensity\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"not_universal_categories\":\n",
        "        \"not presented as universal or standard illumination categories\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"study_specific_thresholds\":\n",
        "        \"thresholds and grouping scheme used here are study-specific\" in section_text\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "word_count = len(re.findall(r\"\\b[\\w'-]+\\b\", section_text))\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_content = f\"# {section_title}\\n\\n{section_text}\\n\"\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_methodology_3_7_illumination_geometry.md\"\n",
        "json_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_step3398_illumination_geometry.json\"\n",
        "audit_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_step3398_illumination_geometry_audit.json\"\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_path.write_text(markdown_content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "\n",
        "record = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": \"Experiment 20\",\n",
        "    \"phase\": \"3.3\",\n",
        "    \"step\": \"3.3.9.8\",\n",
        "    \"subsection\": section_title,\n",
        "    \"created_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"draft_text\": section_text,\n",
        "    \"verified_geometry_facts\": facts,\n",
        "    \"word_count\": word_count,\n",
        "    \"checks\": checks,\n",
