      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Step 3.3.9.9\n",
        "## Methodology: Statistical Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "This subsection documents the identity-level aggregation, repeated-measures tests, pairwise comparisons, multiple-comparison correction, confidence intervals, and effect-size reporting used in the Stage 2 analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "The statistical description must reflect the completed analysis. It must not introduce unrecorded software, bootstrap settings, or prospective hypothesis registration."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "h0DGiy6zL362"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import re\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\")\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = BASE / \"step_3_3\" / \"step_3399\"\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "section_title = \"3.8 Statistical Analysis\"\n",
        "\n",
        "section_text = \"\"\"\n",
        "Statistical comparisons were conducted using identity-level summaries of the reference-relative distances. For each identity, the mean Euclidean displacement and mean cosine distance were calculated separately within the near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular illumination geometry groups. This aggregation provided three repeated measurements for each metric from each of the 38 identities.\n",
        "\n",
        "Differences across the three illumination geometry groups were evaluated using the Friedman test, a non-parametric repeated-measures procedure. The test was applied separately to Euclidean displacement and cosine distance. Kendall's coefficient of concordance (W) was reported as the corresponding effect-size measure.\n",
        "\n",
        "Pairwise differences between illumination geometry groups were examined using Wilcoxon signed-rank tests on the paired identity-level summaries. Three pairwise comparisons were conducted for each distance metric: near-frontal versus oblique, near-frontal versus large-angular, and oblique versus large-angular. Holm's step-down procedure was applied across the combined family of six pairwise tests, comprising the three Euclidean comparisons and the three cosine comparisons, to account for multiple testing.\n",
        "\n",
        "Bootstrap confidence intervals were also calculated for the identity-level mean differences in the pairwise comparisons. The identity served as the resampling unit, preserving the paired structure of the repeated-measures observations. The reported intervals were 95% confidence intervals.\n",
        "\n",
        "An exploratory comparison between frontal and beyond-frontal illumination conditions was additionally conducted using identity-level summaries. This comparison was interpreted cautiously because the two hemispheric categories contained unequal numbers of illumination conditions and observations and were associated with differences in angular geometry.\n",
        "\n",
        "The research hypotheses were formulated retrospectively after the experimental results had been examined. They were not preregistered and should therefore be interpreted as hypotheses used to organise the analysis rather than as prospectively specified tests. Statistical significance was assessed using the corrected pairwise p-values, while effect sizes and confidence intervals were considered alongside the test results.\n",
        "\"\"\".strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "facts = {\n",
        "    \"identity_count\": 38,\n",
        "    \"aggregation_unit\": \"identity\",\n",
        "    \"repeated_measures_groups\": [\n",
        "        \"near-frontal\",\n",
        "        \"oblique\",\n",
        "        \"large-angular\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"metrics\": [\n",
        "        \"Euclidean displacement\",\n",
        "        \"Cosine distance\"\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"omnibus_test\": \"Friedman test\",\n",
        "    \"omnibus_test_type\": \"non-parametric repeated-measures test\",\n",
        "    \"effect_size\": \"Kendall's W\",\n",
        "    \"pairwise_test\": \"Wilcoxon signed-rank test\",\n",
        "    \"pairwise_comparisons_per_metric\": 3,\n",
        "    \"total_pairwise_comparisons\": 6,\n",
        "    \"multiple_comparison_correction\": \"Holm step-down procedure\",\n",
        "    \"correction_family\": \"one combined family of six tests across both metrics\",\n",
        "    \"confidence_interval_method\": \"bootstrap\",\n",
        "    \"confidence_interval_level\": 0.95,\n",
        "    \"bootstrap_resampling_unit\": \"identity\",\n",
        "    \"hemisphere_comparison\": \"exploratory\",\n",
        "    \"hypotheses_preregistered\": False,\n",
        "    \"hypotheses_formulated\": \"retrospectively after results were examined\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "checks = {\n",
        "    \"identity_level_aggregation_documented\":\n",
        "        \"identity-level summaries\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"38_identities_documented\":\n",
        "        \"38 identities\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"three_repeated_measure_groups_documented\":\n",
        "        all(group in section_text for group in [\n",
        "            \"near-frontal\", \"oblique\", \"large-angular\"\n",
        "        ]),\n",
        "    \"both_metrics_documented\":\n",
        "        \"Euclidean displacement\" in section_text and\n",
        "        \"cosine distance\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"friedman_test_documented\":\n",
        "        \"Friedman test\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"kendall_w_documented\":\n",
        "        \"Kendall's coefficient of concordance (W)\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"wilcoxon_test_documented\":\n",
        "        \"Wilcoxon signed-rank tests\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"three_pairwise_comparisons_documented\":\n",
        "        \"Three pairwise comparisons\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"combined_six_test_holm_family_documented\":\n",
        "        \"combined family of six pairwise tests\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"holm_correction_documented\":\n",
        "        \"Holm's step-down procedure\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"bootstrap_confidence_intervals_documented\":\n",
        "        \"Bootstrap confidence intervals\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"identity_resampling_unit_documented\":\n",
        "        \"identity served as the resampling unit\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"confidence_level_correct\":\n",
        "        \"95% confidence intervals\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"hemisphere_analysis_exploratory\":\n",
        "        \"exploratory comparison\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"unequal_hemisphere_counts_limitation\":\n",
        "        \"unequal numbers of illumination conditions and observations\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"retrospective_hypotheses_disclosed\":\n",
        "        \"formulated retrospectively\" in section_text,\n",
        "    \"not_preregistered_disclosed\":\n",
        "        \"They were not preregistered\" in section_text\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "word_count = len(re.findall(r\"\\b[\\w'-]+\\b\", section_text))\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_content = f\"# {section_title}\\n\\n{section_text}\\n\"\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_methodology_3_8_statistical_analysis.md\"\n",
        "json_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_step3399_statistical_analysis.json\"\n",
        "audit_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"experiment20_step3399_statistical_analysis_audit.json\"\n",
        "\n",
        "markdown_path.write_text(markdown_content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "\n",
        "record = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": \"Experiment 20\",\n",
        "    \"phase\": \"3.3\",\n",
