    ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"else:\\\\n    print(\\\\\\\"Required functions and configuration are available.\\\\\\\")\\\\n    print(\\\\\\\"Embedding dimension:\\\\\\\", CONFIG[\\\\\\\"embedding_dimension\\\\\\\"])\\\\n    print(\\\\\\\"Random seed:\\\\\\\", CONFIG[\\\\\\\"random_seed\\\\\\\"])\\\\n    print(\\\\\\\"Detectors:\\\\\\\", CONFIG[\\\\\\\"detectors\\\\\\\"])\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 87,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"alignment\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"\\\\nprint(\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nIndex-order check completed.\\\\\\\")\\\\nprint(\\\\\\\"Note: hashes alone cannot establish alignment unless we also have\\\\\\\"\\\\n      \\\\\\\" matching source-image hashes from the original embedding run.\\\\\\\")\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 90,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"alignment\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"    \\\\\\\"Identity mismatch detected; do not generate transformed embeddings.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nprint(\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nIdentity alignment check passed.\\\\\\\")\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 97,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"alignment\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"- The fresh identities come from the same dataset, not an external dataset.\\\\n- Matching identity labels verifies the selected identity mapping but does not\\\\n  independently prove exact image-level alignment for identities with multiple images.\\\\n- No biometric recognition accuracy, demographic fairness, bias mitigation, or\\\\n  deployment-readiness claim is supported.\\\\n- The detector's threshold and CUSUM settings are provisional and do not guarantee\\\"\\n\",\"        }\\n\",\"      ]\\n\",\"    },\\n\",\"    {\\n\",\"      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Colab Notebooks/Experiment_17_Target_Condition_Recalibration.ipynb\\\",\\n\",\"      \\\"experiment18_reference\\\": false,\\n\",\"      \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 1,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"embedding_dimension\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"    \\\\\\\"random_seed\\\\\\\": 202617,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"n_seeds\\\\\\\": 20,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"embedding_dimension\\\\\\\": 64,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"window_size\\\\\\\": 20,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"reference_samples\\\\\\\": 1000,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"source_calibration_windows\\\\\\\": 200,\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 2,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"embedding_dimension\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"# Experiment 17 — Step 3: Define and Validate Covariance Conditions\\\\n\\\\nD = CONFIG[\\\\\\\"embedding_dimension\\\\\\\"]\\\\nrho = CONFIG[\\\\\\\"correlation_strength\\\\\\\"]\\\\ncovariances = {\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 22,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"alignment\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"- Aggregated scenario count.\\\\n- Finite values and valid rate ranges.\\\\n- One-to-one alignment between control and drift evaluation records.\\\\n\\\\n### Expected Result\\\\nAll programmed integrity checks should pass. Passing these checks confirms data consistency and numerical integrity, but does not by itself establish scientific validity or real-world applicability.\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 28,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"alignment\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"## Integrity Checks\\\\n\\\\nThe programmed integrity audit passed **15 out of 15 checks**. These checks cover expected record counts, numerical finiteness, valid rate ranges, and alignment of control and drift evaluation records.\\\\nPassing these checks establishes basic numerical and data-structure consistency. It does not establish scientific validity by itself.\\\"\\n\",\"        }\\n\",\"      ]\\n\",\"    },\\n\",\"    {\\n\",\"      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Colab Notebooks/(Master)11_Illumination_Drift_Detection.ipynb\\\",\\n\",\"      \\\"experiment18_reference\\\": false,\\n\",\"      \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 3,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"Resize\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"lfw = fetch_lfw_people(\\\\n    min_faces_per_person=20,\\\\n    resize=0.5,\\\\n    color=True,\\\\n    download_if_missing=True\\\\n)\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 6,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"Resize\\\",\\n\",\"            \\\"Normalize\\\",\\n\",\"            \\\"ToTensor\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"    print(\\\\\\\"Re-initializing missing dataset and illumination transformations...\\\\\\\")\\\\n    from sklearn.datasets import fetch_lfw_people\\\\n    lfw = fetch_lfw_people(min_faces_per_person=20, resize=0.5, color=True, download_if_missing=True)\\\\n    images = lfw.images\\\\n    labels = lfw.target\\\\n    identity_names = lfw.target_names\\\\nmodel.eval()\\\\n\\\\n# LFW images are small; resize consistently to the model's expected input size.\\\\npreprocess = transforms.Compose([\\\\n    transforms.ToPILImage(),\\\\n    transforms.Resize((224, 224)),\\\\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\\\\n    transforms.Normalize(\\\\n        mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406],\\\\n        std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225]\\\\n    )\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 7,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"embedding_dimension\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"        \\\\\\\"condition\\\\\\\": condition,\\\\n        \\\\\\\"num_images\\\\\\\": len(distances),\\\\n        \\\\\\\"embedding_dimension\\\\\\\": changed_embeddings.shape[1],\\\\n        \\\\\\\"mean_l2_distance\\\\\\\": float(distances.mean()),\\\\n        \\\\\\\"median_l2_distance\\\\\\\": float(np.median(distances)),\\\\n        \\\\\\\"std_l2_distance\\\\\\\": float(distances.std()),\\\\n    \\\\\\\"num_identities\\\\\\\": int(len(identity_names)),\\\\n    \\\\\\\"embedding_model\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ImageNet-pretrained ResNet-18, classification head removed\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"embedding_dimension\\\\\\\": 512,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"illumination_factors\\\\\\\": illumination_conditions,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"seed\\\\\\\": SEED,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"device\\\\\\\": str(device),\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 25,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"Resize\\\",\\n\",\"            \\\"Normalize\\\",\\n\",\"            \\\"ToTensor\\\",\\n\",\"            \\\"embedding_dimension\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"        \\\\\\\"num_identities\\\\\\\": 62,\\\\n        \\\\\\\"embedding_model\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ImageNet-pretrained ResNet-18, classification head removed\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"embedding_dimension\\\\\\\": 512,\\\\n        \\\\\\\"seed\\\\\\\": 42,\\\\n        \\\\\\\"device\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"cpu\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n    \\\\\\\"weights_requested\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"torchvision.models.ResNet18_Weights.DEFAULT\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"classification_head\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"nn.Identity()\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"embedding_dimension\\\\\\\": 512,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"input_resize\\\\\\\": [224, 224],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"input_transform\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"ToPILImage -> Resize -> ToTensor -> Normalize\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"normalization_mean\\\\\\\": [0.485, 0.456, 0.406],\\\\n    \\\\\\\"normalization_std\\\\\\\": [0.229, 0.224, 0.225],\\\\n}\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 80,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"Resize\\\",\\n\",\"            \\\"Normalize\\\",\\n\",\"            \\\"ToTensor\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"lfw = fetch_lfw_people(\\\\n    min_faces_per_person=20,\\\\n    resize=0.5,\\\\n    color=True,\\\\n    download_if_missing=True\\\\n)\\\\npreprocess = transforms.Compose([\\\\n    transforms.ToPILImage(),\\\\n    transforms.Resize((224, 224)),\\\\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\\\\n    transforms.Normalize(\\\\n        mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406],\\\\n        std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225]\\\\n    )\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 81,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"embedding_dimension\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"    \\\\\\\"images\\\\\\\": 3023,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"identities\\\\\\\": 62,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"embedding_dimension\\\\\\\": 512,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"illumination_factors\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Dim\\\\\\\": 0.60,\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Original\\\\\\\": 1.00,\\\"\\n\",\"        },\\n\",\"        {\\n\",\"          \\\"cell_index\\\": 95,\\n\",\"          \\\"matched_terms\\\": [\\n\",\"            \\\"embedding_dimension\\\"\\n\",\"          ],\\n\",\"          \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"        \\\\\\\"condition\\\\\\\": condition,\\\\n        \\\\\\\"num_images\\\\\\\": len(changed_embeddings),\\\\n        \\\\\\\"embedding_dimension\\\\\\\": changed_embeddings.shape[1],\\\\n        \\\\\\\"mean_l2_distance\\\\\\\": float(np.mean(distances)),\\\\n        \\\\\\\"median_l2_distance\\\\\\\": float(np.median(distances)),\\\\n        \\\\\\\"std_l2_distance\\\\\\\": float(np.std(distances)),\\\\n        row[\\\\\\\"num_images_recorded\\\\\\\"] == row[\\\\\\\"num_images_regenerated\\\\\\\"],\\\\n        \\\\\\\"| Dimens