      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "## Step 3.3.10.2 — Corrected Frozen-Table and Holm-Correction Audit\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "This step verifies the integrity of the frozen Experiment 20 result tables and independently examines the multiple-comparison correction applied to the six pairwise comparisons across the Euclidean and cosine distance outcomes.\n",
        "\n",
        "The purpose is to distinguish the original frozen statistical results from the subsequent methodological decision to apply one Holm correction family across all six comparisons.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Verification procedure\n",
        "\n",
        "The audit performs the following checks:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Frozen-table integrity:** Verifies the presence and expected row counts of the seven primary CSV result tables.\n",
        "2. **Pairwise comparison inspection:** Loads the six frozen pairwise comparisons and checks the required statistical fields.\n",
        "3. **Independent Holm recomputation:** Recalculates Holm-adjusted p-values using one combined family of six comparisons.\n",
        "4. **Correction-method comparison:** Determines whether the original frozen CSV reflects one six-test family or separate metric-wise correction families.\n",
        "5. **Statistical significance:** Checks whether all six comparisons remain significant at the 0.05 significance level following the combined correction.\n",
        "6. **Audit declaration:** Reads the original repeated-measures audit to identify the correction method documented in the frozen experimental record.\n",
        "7. **Audit preservation:** Saves a separate verification record containing table metadata, SHA256 hashes, correction results, and the final audit status.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Important methodological distinction\n",
        "\n",
        "The original frozen pairwise comparison table is preserved without modification. Its existing Holm-adjusted p-values are not silently replaced.\n",
        "\n",
        "The combined six-test Holm correction is calculated separately for manuscript reporting. This correction treats the six comparisons across both distance metrics as one multiple-testing family.\n",
        "\n",
        "The distinction between the original frozen results and the subsequent manuscript-level correction is retained for traceability and reproducibility.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Scope and limitations\n",
        "\n",
        "This step verifies table integrity and the consistency of the multiple-comparison correction. It does not independently reproduce the underlying embedding extraction, distance calculations, Friedman tests, or bootstrap confidence intervals.\n",
        "\n",
        "Statistical significance does not establish biometric recognition accuracy, operational drift-detection performance, or deployment readiness.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Expected output\n",
        "\n",
        "The audit produces:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Frozen-table row-count and SHA256 verification.\n",
        "- Six pairwise comparison records.\n",
        "- Independently recomputed six-test Holm-adjusted p-values.\n",
        "- Identification of the correction method used in the original frozen results.\n",
        "- A separate JSON audit record.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Output file:** `experiment20_step33102_corrected_results_audit.json`\n",
        "\n",
        "**Preservation rule:** Original frozen experimental results must remain unchanged.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "EMzBkaxbwH4_"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.3.10.2\n",
        "# CORRECTED FROZEN-TABLE AND HOLM-CORRECTION AUDIT\n",
        "# INSPECTION ONLY — DO NOT MODIFY FROZEN RESULTS\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import hashlib\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "\n",
        "ROOT = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\")\n",
        "FREEZE = ROOT / \"step_2_7\" / \"final_freeze\"\n",
        "\n",
        "OUT = ROOT / \"step_3_3\" / \"step_33102\"\n",
        "OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "AUDIT_PATH = OUT / \"experiment20_step33102_corrected_results_audit.json\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 75)\n",
        "print(\"EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.3.10.2\")\n",
        "print(\"CORRECTED FROZEN-TABLE AND HOLM-CORRECTION AUDIT\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 75)\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 1. VERIFY ACTUAL FROZEN CSV FILENAMES AND ROW COUNTS\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "expected_rows = {\n",
        "    \"experiment20_reference_evaluation_displacement.csv\": 2128,\n",
        "    \"experiment20_illumination_group_descriptive_statistics.csv\": 6,\n",
        "    \"experiment20_identity_level_group_means.csv\": 114,\n",
        "    \"experiment20_paired_comparison_results.csv\": 6,\n",
        "    \"experiment20_identity_level_hemisphere_means.csv\": 76,\n",
        "    \"experiment20_hemisphere_comparison_results.csv\": 2,\n",
        "    \"experiment20_repeated_measures_test_results.csv\": 2\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "table_checks = {}\n",
        "table_metadata = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[1] FROZEN CSV ROW-COUNT VERIFICATION\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for filename, expected in expected_rows.items():\n",
        "\n",
        "    path = FREEZE / filename\n",
        "\n",
        "    if not path.is_file():\n",
        "        table_checks[filename] = False\n",
        "        print(f\"{filename}: NOT FOUND\")\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "\n",
        "    df = pd.read_csv(path)\n",
        "    actual = len(df)\n",
        "\n",
        "    passed = actual == expected\n",
        "\n",
        "    table_checks[filename] = passed\n",
        "\n",
        "    table_metadata[filename] = {\n",
        "        \"expected_rows\": expected,\n",
        "        \"actual_rows\": actual,\n",
        "        \"columns\": list(df.columns),\n",
        "        \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        f\"{filename}: \"\n",
        "        f\"expected={expected}, actual={actual}, \"\n",
        "        f\"{'PASS' if passed else 'FAIL'}\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 2. LOAD SIX PAIRWISE COMPARISONS\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "pairwise_path = FREEZE / \"experiment20_paired_comparison_results.csv\"\n",
        "\n",
        "if not pairwise_path.is_file():\n",
        "    raise FileNotFoundError(pairwise_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "pairwise = pd.read_csv(pairwise_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "required_columns = [\n",
        "    \"metric\",\n",
        "    \"group_a\",\n",
        "    \"group_b\",\n",
        "    \"raw_p_value\",\n",
        "    \"holm_adjusted_p_value\",\n",
        "    \"significant_after_holm_0_05\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "missing_columns = [\n",
        "    col for col in required_columns\n",
        "    if col not in pairwise.columns\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "if missing_columns:\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        f\"Missing pairwise columns: {missing_columns}\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "if len(pairwise) != 6:\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        f\"Expected six pairwise comparisons, found {len(pairwise)}\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[2] FROZEN PAIRWISE COMPARISON VALUES\")\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    pairwise[\n",
        "        [\n",
        "            \"metric\",\n",
        "            \"group_a\",\n",
        "            \"group_b\",\n",
        "            \"raw_p_value\",\n",
        "            \"holm_adjusted_p_value\",\n",
        "            \"significant_after_holm_0_05\"\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    ].to_string(index=False)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 3. RECOMPUTE HOLM ADJUSTMENT ACROSS ONE FAMILY OF SIX\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "def holm_adjust(p_values):\n",
        "\n",
        "    p_values = [float(p) for p in p_values]\n",
        "    m = len(p_values)\n",
        "\n",
        "    order = sorted(\n",
        "        range(m),\n",
        "        key=lambda i: p_values[i]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    adjusted = [None] * m\n",
        "    running_max = 0.0\n",
        "\n",
        "    for rank, original_index in enumerate(order):\n",
        "\n",
        "        multiplier = m - rank\n",
        "        candidate = multiplier * p_values[original_index]\n",
        "\n",
        "        running_max = max(running_max, candidate)\n",
        "\n",
        "        adjusted[original_index] = min(1.0, running_max)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return adjusted\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "raw_p_values = pairwise[\"raw_p_value\"].astype(float).tolist()\n",
        "\n",
        "six_test_holm = holm_adjust(raw_p_values)\n",
        "\n",
        "pairwise[\"recomputed_six_test_holm_p\"] = six_test_holm\n",
        "\n",
        "pairwise[\"six_test_significant_at_005\"] = [\n",
        "    p < 0.05 for p in six_test_holm\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[3] SIX-TEST HOLM RECOMPUTATION\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for i, row in pairwise.iterrows():\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        f\"{row['metric']} | \"\n",
        "        f\"{row['group_a']} vs {row['group_b']} | \"\n",
        "        f\"raw p={row['raw_p_value']:.12g} | \"\n",
        "        f\"frozen adjusted p={row['holm_adjusted_p_value']:.12g} | \"\n",
        "        f\"six-test adjusted p={row['recomputed_six_test_holm_p']:.12g}\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 4. IDENTIFY THE CORRECTION USED IN THE FROZEN CSV\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "frozen_adjusted = pairwise[\n",
        "    \"holm_adjusted_p_value\"\n",
        "].astype(float).tolist()\n",
        "\n",
        "six_test_adjusted = pairwise[\n",
        "    \"recomputed_six_test_holm_p\"\n",
        "].astype(float).tolist()\n",
        "\n",
        "frozen_matches_six_test = all(\n",
        "    abs(a - b) <= 1e-15\n",
        "    for a, b in zip(frozen_adjusted, six_test_adjusted)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "metric_family_matches = True\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric, subset in pairwise.groupby(\"metric\"):\n",
        "\n",
        "    expected_metric_adjusted = holm_adjust(\n",
        "        subset[\"raw_p_value\"].astype(float).tolist()\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    actual_metric_adjusted = (\n",
        "        subset[\"holm_adjusted_p_value\"].astype(float).tolist()\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    if not all(\n",
        "        abs(a - b) <= 1e-15\n",
        "        for a, b in zip(\n",
        "            actual_metric_adjusted,\n",
        "            expected_metric_adjusted\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    ):\n",
        "        metric_family_matches = False\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[4] FROZEN CORRECTION METHOD\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    \"Frozen CSV matches one six-test family:\",\n",
        "    frozen_matches_six_test\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    \"Frozen CSV matches separate metric-wise families:\",\n",
        "    metric_family_matches\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 5. VERIFY SIGNIFICANCE UNDER SIX-TEST CORRECTION\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "six_test_all_significant = all(\n",
        "    p < 0.05 for p in six_test_adjusted\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[5] SIX-TEST SIGNIFICANCE\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    \"All six comparisons significant after six-test Holm:\",\n",
        "    six_test_all_significant\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    \"Six-test Holm-adjusted p-value range:\",\n",
        "    min(six_test_adjusted),\n",
        "    \"to\",\n",
        "    max(six_test_adjusted)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 6. CHECK REPEATED-MEASURES AUDIT DECLARATION\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "repeated_audit_path = (\n",
        "    FREEZE / \"experiment20_step274_repeated_measures_audit.json\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(repeated_audit_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "    repeated_audit = json.load(f)\n",
        "\n",
        "declared_method = repeated_audit.get(\n",
        "    \"multiple_comparison_correction\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[6] REPEATED-MEASURES AUDIT DECLARATION\")\n",
        "print(\"Declared correction:\", declared_method)\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 7. SAVE AUDIT WITHOUT MODIFYING FROZEN FILES\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "audit = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": 20,\n",
        "    \"step\": \"3.3.10.2\",\n",
        "    \"timestamp_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"frozen_table_checks\": table_checks,\n",
        "    \"frozen_table_metadata\": table_metadata,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"pairwise_comparison_count\": len(pairwise),\n",
        "    \"frozen_correction_declaration\": declared_method,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"frozen_csv_matches_six_test_family\": frozen_matches_six_test,\n",
        "    \"frozen_csv_matches_metric_wise_families\": metric_family_matches,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"six_test_holm_adjusted_p_values\": six_test_adjusted,\n",
        "    \"all_six_significant_after_six_test_holm\": six_test_all_significant,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"interpretation\": (\n",
        "        \"The frozen pairwise CSV and repeated-measures audit \"\n",
        "        \"must be distinguished from the later six-test Holm \"\n",
        "        \"correction decision. This audit does not overwrite \"\n",
        "        \"or alter the frozen experimental outputs.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "audit[\"status\"] = (\n",
        "    \"TABLES_VERIFIED_CORRECTION_DISCREPANCY_DOCUMENTED\"\n",
        "    if all(table_checks.values())\n",
        "    and metric_family_matches\n",
        "    and not frozen_matches_six_test\n",
        "    and six_test_all_significant\n",
        "    else \"REQUIRES_REVIEW\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(AUDIT_PATH, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "    json.dump(audit, f, indent=4)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[7] FINAL AUDIT\")\n",
        "print(\"CSV tables verified:\", sum(table_checks.values()), \"/\", len(table_checks))\n",
        "print(\"Missing or incorrect tables:\", sum(not x for x in table_checks.values()))\n",
        "print(\"Metric-wise correction reproduced:\", metric_family_matches)\n",
        "print(\"Six-test correction reproduced:\", not frozen_matches_six_test)\n",
        "print(\"All six remain significant:\", six_test_all_significant)\n",
        "print(\"Status:\", audit[\"status\"])\n",
        "print(\"Audit saved:\", AUDIT_PATH)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 75)\n",
        "print(\"STEP 3.3.10.2 COMPLETED\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 75)"
      ],
