        "\n",
        "## Step 3.3.10.3 — Manuscript Six-Test Holm Correction Artifact\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "This step generates a separate manuscript-ready statistical results table by applying the Holm–Bonferroni multiple-comparison correction across one combined family of six pairwise comparisons.\n",
        "\n",
        "The six comparisons comprise three illumination-group comparisons for each of the two distance metrics: Euclidean displacement and cosine distance.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Methodology\n",
        "\n",
        "The procedure uses the original frozen pairwise comparison CSV as its input and performs the following operations:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Source validation:** Loads the original frozen pairwise comparison table and verifies that it contains exactly six comparisons with valid raw p-values.\n",
        "2. **Combined correction:** Recalculates Holm-adjusted p-values across all six comparisons as one correction family.\n",
        "3. **Significance assessment:** Evaluates each corrected p-value against the significance threshold of 0.05.\n",
        "4. **Traceability:** Retains the original metric-wise Holm-adjusted p-values alongside the newly calculated six-test adjusted values.\n",
        "5. **Manuscript reporting:** Creates a separate field identifying the adjusted p-values intended for manuscript reporting.\n",
        "6. **Integrity verification:** Reopens the generated CSV, checks its row count and significance results, and calculates SHA256 hashes for the source and output files.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Multiple-comparison correction decision\n",
        "\n",
        "The original frozen results applied Holm correction separately within each distance metric. The subsequent methodological decision adopts one combined correction family containing all six pairwise comparisons across both metrics.\n",
        "\n",
        "These are distinct correction procedures and must not be conflated.\n",
        "\n",
        "The original frozen results are retained unchanged. The newly generated six-test Holm-adjusted p-values are used for the manuscript's inferential reporting.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Expected output\n",
        "\n",
        "This step produces two separate artifacts:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `experiment20_manuscript_six_test_holm_results.csv` — manuscript-level pairwise comparison table containing both original and combined-family adjusted p-values.\n",
        "- `experiment20_step33103_holm_correction_record.json` — correction methodology, source and output hashes, significance status, and provenance record.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Interpretation and limitations\n",
        "\n",
        "The combined Holm correction controls the family-wise error rate across the six specified pairwise tests under the chosen correction family.\n",
        "\n",
        "Statistical significance following correction does not establish practical significance, biometric recognition accuracy, or generalisation beyond the evaluated identities, dataset, and pretrained model.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Preservation rule:** The original frozen pairwise comparison CSV must not be modified. The manuscript correction is stored as a separate artifact.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "kNjdnqxvwV-b"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.3.10.3\n",
        "# MANUSCRIPT SIX-TEST HOLM CORRECTION ARTIFACT\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import hashlib\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "\n",
        "ROOT = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\")\n",
        "FREEZE = ROOT / \"step_2_7\" / \"final_freeze\"\n",
        "OUT = ROOT / \"step_3_3\" / \"step_33103\"\n",
        "OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "SOURCE = FREEZE / \"experiment20_paired_comparison_results.csv\"\n",
        "\n",
        "CSV_OUT = OUT / \"experiment20_manuscript_six_test_holm_results.csv\"\n",
        "JSON_OUT = OUT / \"experiment20_step33103_holm_correction_record.json\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 75)\n",
        "print(\"EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.3.10.3\")\n",
        "print(\"MANUSCRIPT SIX-TEST HOLM CORRECTION ARTIFACT\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 75)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load the original frozen results without modifying them.\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(SOURCE)\n",
        "\n",
        "if len(df) != 6:\n",
        "    raise ValueError(f\"Expected 6 comparisons, found {len(df)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if df[\"raw_p_value\"].isna().any():\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\"Missing raw p-values detected.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Recompute Holm adjustment across one family of six.\n",
        "p_values = df[\"raw_p_value\"].astype(float).tolist()\n",
        "m = len(p_values)\n",
        "\n",
        "order = sorted(range(m), key=lambda i: p_values[i])\n",
        "\n",
        "adjusted = [None] * m\n",
        "running_max = 0.0\n",
        "\n",
        "for rank, original_index in enumerate(order):\n",
        "    candidate = (m - rank) * p_values[original_index]\n",
        "    running_max = max(running_max, candidate)\n",
        "    adjusted[original_index] = min(1.0, running_max)\n",
        "\n",
        "df[\"six_test_holm_adjusted_p_value\"] = adjusted\n",
        "df[\"six_test_family_size\"] = m\n",
        "df[\"six_test_significant_at_0_05\"] = [\n",
        "    p < 0.05 for p in adjusted\n",
        "]\n",
        "df[\"correction_scope\"] = \"One family of six pairwise tests\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Retain original frozen adjusted values for traceability.\n",
        "df[\"original_metric_wise_holm_adjusted_p_value\"] = (\n",
        "    df[\"holm_adjusted_p_value\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Explicitly distinguish manuscript values from frozen values.\n",
        "df[\"manuscript_adjusted_p_value\"] = (\n",
        "    df[\"six_test_holm_adjusted_p_value\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Save separate manuscript artifact.\n",
        "df.to_csv(CSV_OUT, index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Verify output.\n",
        "check = pd.read_csv(CSV_OUT)\n",
        "\n",
        "if len(check) != 6:\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\"Output row-count verification failed.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if not all(check[\"six_test_significant_at_0_05\"]):\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\"Not all six comparisons are significant.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "source_hash = hashlib.sha256(SOURCE.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n",
        "output_hash = hashlib.sha256(CSV_OUT.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n",
        "\n",
        "record = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": 20,\n",
        "    \"step\": \"3.3.10.3\",\n",
        "    \"created_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"source_file\": str(SOURCE),\n",
        "    \"source_sha256\": source_hash,\n",
        "    \"output_csv\": str(CSV_OUT),\n",
        "    \"output_csv_sha256\": output_hash,\n",
        "    \"number_of_tests\": 6,\n",
        "    \"correction_method\": \"Holm-Bonferroni\",\n",
        "    \"correction_family\": \"One combined family of six pairwise comparisons\",\n",
        "    \"original_frozen_correction\": (\n",
        "        \"Holm correction separately within each metric\"\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"manuscript_correction\": (\n",
        "        \"Holm correction across all six comparisons\"\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"six_test_adjusted_p_values\": adjusted,\n",
        "    \"all_six_significant_at_0_05\": True,\n",
        "    \"original_frozen_file_modified\": False,\n",
        "    \"status\": \"MANUSCRIPT_CORRECTION_ARTIFACT_CREATED\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(JSON_OUT, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "    json.dump(record, f, indent=4)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[1] CORRECTED MANUSCRIPT TABLE\")\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    check[\n",
        "        [\n",
        "            \"metric\",\n",
        "            \"group_a\",\n",
        "            \"group_b\",\n",
        "            \"raw_p_value\",\n",
        "            \"original_metric_wise_holm_adjusted_p_value\",\n",
        "            \"manuscript_adjusted_p_value\",\n",
        "            \"six_test_significant_at_0_05\"\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    ].to_string(index=False)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[2] INTEGRITY\")\n",
        "print(\"Source SHA256:\", source_hash)\n",
        "print(\"Output SHA256:\", output_hash)\n",
        "print(\"Frozen source modified: False\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n[3] FINAL STATUS\")\n",
        "print(\"Comparisons:\", len(check))\n",
        "print(\"All six significant:\", all(check[\"six_test_significant_at_0_05\"]))\n",
        "print(\"Status:\", record[\"status\"])\n",
        "print(\"CSV:\", CSV_OUT)\n",
        "print(\"JSON:\", JSON_OUT)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 75)\n",
        "print(\"STEP 3.3.10.3 COMPLETED\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 75)"
      ],
