        "\n",
        "## Step 3.3.10.7 — Results-Section Cross-Validation and Consistency Audit\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "This step performs a consolidated consistency audit of the Experiment 20 results before preparation of the manuscript Results section.\n",
        "\n",
        "It examines whether the overall descriptive statistics, illumination-group results, identity-level repeated-measures findings, combined six-test Holm correction, and exploratory hemisphere comparisons are consistent across the frozen experimental tables and previously completed verification records.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Verification procedure\n",
        "\n",
        "The audit performs the following checks:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Source integrity:** Confirms the presence of the required frozen CSV files and previously completed verification records.\n",
        "2. **Overall descriptive statistics:** Cross-checks the total evaluation sample size and overall Euclidean and cosine distance statistics.\n",
        "3. **Illumination-group consistency:** Verifies the observation counts, identity coverage, and progressive ordering of the three illumination geometry groups.\n",
        "4. **Repeated-measures consistency:** Checks the Friedman statistics, p-values, Kendall's W, and six pairwise comparisons.\n",
        "5. **Multiple-comparison correction:** Confirms that the manuscript uses the combined six-test Holm correction rather than the original metric-wise correction values.\n",
        "6. **Bootstrap consistency:** Checks the repeated-measures bootstrap configuration and the hemisphere bootstrap configuration separately.\n",
        "7. **Hemisphere-analysis consistency:** Verifies the identity coverage, condition counts, mean differences, confidence intervals, and Holm-adjusted p-values.\n",
        "8. **Audit-record consistency:** Confirms that the previously completed Steps 3.3.10.4, 3.3.10.5, and 3.3.10.6 report successful verification.\n",
        "9. **Provenance preservation:** Records SHA256 hashes of the source tables and audit records without modifying the original files.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "The purpose is to establish that the numerical findings intended for manuscript reporting are traceable to the frozen experimental outputs and are consistent across the completed verification stages.\n",
        "\n",
        "This audit does not independently reproduce the entire embedding extraction pipeline or establish external scientific validity.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Scope limitations\n",
        "\n",
        "The evaluation remains restricted to 38 identities, the Cropped Extended Yale B dataset, and one fixed pretrained FaceNet model.\n",
        "\n",
        "The three illumination geometry groups and the exploratory hemisphere comparison describe observed reference-relative embedding displacement. Differences cannot be attributed exclusively to illumination because different image captures were evaluated rather than exact transformations of identical source images.\n",
        "\n",
        "The Euclidean and cosine distance outcomes are mathematically related and must not be presented as independent validation experiments.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Expected output\n",
        "\n",
        "`experiment20_step33107_results_consistency_audit.json`\n",
        "\n",
        "The record contains source-file hashes, cross-validation checks, verified result summaries, discrepancies, and the final audit status.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Preservation rule:** All frozen experimental results and previously completed audit records must remain unchanged.\n"
      ],
