        "\n",
        "# Step 3.3.10.8 — Manuscript Results Section Drafting and Evidence Integration\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "Draft the Results section of the Experiment 20 manuscript using only the verified and cross-validated experimental results from Step 3.3.10.7.\n",
        "\n",
        "The purpose is to convert the verified numerical findings into a clear, academically structured Results section without modifying the original experimental outputs.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Required subsections\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Evaluation Cohort and Analysis Coverage\n",
        "2. Overall Reference-Relative Embedding Displacement\n",
        "3. Displacement Across Illumination Geometry Groups\n",
        "4. Identity-Level Repeated-Measures Analysis\n",
        "5. Exploratory Frontal and Beyond-Frontal Comparison\n",
        "6. Summary of Findings\n",
        "\n",
        "## Evidence and reporting requirements\n",
        "\n",
        "- Use the frozen experimental tables and the verified six-test Holm correction artifact.\n",
        "- Report 2,414 standard-illumination images, 38 identities, 2,166 observations across 57 common conditions, and 2,128 non-reference evaluation observations across 56 conditions accurately.\n",
        "- Report the three illumination groups using their verified observation and condition counts.\n",
        "- Report Friedman statistics, pairwise comparisons, confidence intervals, and corrected p-values exactly as verified.\n",
        "- Use one combined family of six pairwise comparisons for manuscript-level Holm correction.\n",
        "- Preserve the exploratory status of the hemisphere comparison.\n",
        "- Do not generate new statistical tests or alter frozen results.\n",
        "- Do not claim recognition accuracy, fairness, operational drift-detection performance, or cross-architecture generalisation.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Scientific interpretation restrictions\n",
        "\n",
        "- Treat the findings as descriptive evidence of reference-relative embedding displacement.\n",
        "- Do not attribute all observed displacement exclusively to illumination because the evaluation uses different image captures rather than exact transformations of identical source images.\n",
        "- Do not interpret Kendall's W as detector accuracy.\n",
        "- Recognise that Euclidean displacement and cosine distance are mathematically related for L2-normalised embeddings.\n",
        "- Do not claim that the study establishes research novelty.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Expected outputs\n",
        "\n",
        "- A complete first-draft Results section in Markdown.\n",
        "- A JSON evidence and drafting record.\n",
        "- Source-file hashes and output integrity checks.\n",
        "- Confirmation that original frozen experimental files remain unchanged.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Completion condition:** The draft must be generated, reloaded successfully, and checked against the verified evidence before proceeding to editorial review.\n"
      ],
