      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "# Step 3.3.11 — Discussion Section Development\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "Develop the Discussion section of the Experiment 20 manuscript using the verified Results section, established methodological decisions, and the literature already incorporated into the Introduction.\n",
        "\n",
        "The Discussion must interpret the experimental findings, relate them to previous illumination research, explain their implications, and critically evaluate the study's limitations.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Required subsections\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Principal Findings\n",
        "2. Interpretation of Illumination Geometry and Embedding Displacement\n",
        "3. Identity-Level Consistency and Statistical Evidence\n",
        "4. Relationship to Previous Illumination Research\n",
        "5. Implications for Face-Embedding Evaluation\n",
        "6. Limitations\n",
        "7. Future Research Directions\n",
        "8. Overall Discussion\n",
        "\n",
        "## Evidence requirements\n",
        "\n",
        "- Use the verified numerical results from Step 3.3.10.8.\n",
        "- Preserve the combined six-test Holm correction.\n",
        "- Interpret Kendall's W as agreement in ranking across identities, not recognition accuracy.\n",
        "- Recognise the mathematical relationship between Euclidean displacement and cosine distance for L2-normalised embeddings.\n",
        "- Use the existing literature references: Moses et al. (1994), Beveridge et al. (2009), Han et al. (2013), and Ochoa-Villegas et al. (2015).\n",
        "- Distinguish previous research findings from the findings of Experiment 20.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Limitations that must be addressed\n",
        "\n",
        "- Evaluation uses different image captures, not exact transformations of identical source images.\n",
        "- One reference capture per identity.\n",
        "- One pretrained FaceNet architecture.\n",
        "- Cropped frontal-pose Extended Yale B subset.\n",
        "- Community-hosted dataset acquisition provenance.\n",
        "- No recognition accuracy or verification-performance evaluation.\n",
        "- No calibrated drift-detection thresholds or operational false-alarm analysis.\n",
        "- No independent architecture validation.\n",
        "- Hemisphere analysis is exploratory and confounded with angular geometry.\n",
        "- Illumination geometry groups do not represent illumination intensity.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Writing restrictions\n",
        "\n",
        "- Do not claim that illumination alone caused all observed displacement.\n",
        "- Do not claim established research novelty.\n",
        "- Do not claim fairness, bias mitigation, robustness, or deployment readiness.\n",
        "- Do not interpret descriptive displacement as biometric recognition failure.\n",
        "- Do not describe retrospective hypotheses as preregistered.\n",
        "- Do not introduce unsupported literature claims or invented citations.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Expected outputs\n",
        "\n",
        "- A complete Discussion section in Markdown.\n",
        "- A JSON evidence and drafting record.\n",
        "- Source-file hashes and output integrity checks.\n",
        "- Confirmation that the existing Results and frozen experimental files remain unchanged.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Completion condition:** The Discussion draft must be generated from verified evidence, reloaded successfully, and checked for scientific interpretation and consistency before editorial approval.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "_LYGToKg4JIR"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.3.11\n",
        "# DISCUSSION SECTION — COMPLETE CORRECTED VERSION\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Purpose:\n",
        "# 1. Load the generated Discussion draft.\n",
        "# 2. Correct the identity-level sample-size interpretation.\n",
        "# 3. Preserve all other Discussion content.\n",
        "# 4. Update the Markdown and JSON records.\n",
        "# 5. Verify file integrity and source preservation.\n",
        "#\n",
        "# No experimental results or frozen source files are modified.\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import hashlib\n",
        "\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 1. DEFINE FILE PATHS\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "ROOT = Path(\n",
        "    \"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "STEP3 = ROOT / \"step_3_3\"\n",
        "\n",
        "OUT = STEP3 / \"step_3311\"\n",
        "\n",
        "DISCUSSION_MD = (\n",
        "    OUT / \"experiment20_discussion_section_draft_v1.md\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "DISCUSSION_JSON = (\n",
        "    OUT / \"experiment20_step3311_discussion_record.json\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "RESULTS_MD = (\n",
        "    STEP3\n",
        "    / \"step_33108\"\n",
        "    / \"experiment20_results_section_draft_v1.md\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "RESULTS_JSON = (\n",
        "    STEP3\n",
        "    / \"step_33108\"\n",
        "    / \"experiment20_step33108_results_draft_record.json\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 2. CHECK REQUIRED FILES\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "required_files = [\n",
        "    DISCUSSION_MD,\n",
        "    DISCUSSION_JSON,\n",
        "    RESULTS_MD,\n",
        "    RESULTS_JSON\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "for path in required_files:\n",
        "\n",
        "    if not path.is_file():\n",
        "\n",
        "        raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
        "            f\"Required file not found: {path}\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
        "print(\"EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.3.11\")\n",
        "print(\"DISCUSSION CORRECTION AND INTEGRITY VERIFICATION\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 3. LOAD EXISTING DISCUSSION AND RESULTS RECORDS\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "discussion_text = DISCUSSION_MD.read_text(\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(\n",
        "    DISCUSSION_JSON,\n",
        "    \"r\",\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ") as f:\n",
        "\n",
        "    discussion_record = json.load(f)\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(\n",
        "    RESULTS_JSON,\n",
        "    \"r\",\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ") as f:\n",
        "\n",
        "    results_record = json.load(f)\n",
        "\n",
        "if discussion_record.get(\"status\") != (\n",
        "    \"DISCUSSION_SECTION_DRAFT_GENERATED\"\n",
        "):\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        \"Existing Discussion record has an unexpected status.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "if results_record.get(\"status\") != (\n",
        "    \"RESULTS_SECTION_DRAFT_GENERATED\"\n",
        "):\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        \"Results record has an unexpected status.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 4. DEFINE ORIGINAL AND CORRECTED PARAGRAPHS\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "old_paragraph = (\n",
        "    \"However, the statistical evidence should be interpreted \"\n",
        "    \"within the study design. The repeated-measures analysis \"\n",
        "    \"uses identity-level group means, whereas the observation-\"\n",
        "    \"level descriptive statistics contain different numbers \"\n",
        "    \"of captures across the three groups. The group sample \"\n",
        "    \"sizes therefore should not be interpreted as equal \"\n",
        "    \"numbers of independent identity-level observations.\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "corrected_paragraph = (\n",
        "    \"However, the statistical evidence should be interpreted \"\n",
        "    \"within the study design. The descriptive statistics are \"\n",
        "    \"based on unequal numbers of image observations across \"\n",
        "    \"the three illumination groups (646 near-frontal, \"\n",
        "    \"418 oblique, and 1,064 large-angular-deviation \"\n",
        "    \"observations). In contrast, the repeated-measures \"\n",
        "    \"analysis uses identity-level group means from the same \"\n",
        "    \"38 identities across all three groups. The inferential \"\n",
        "    \"sample therefore consists of 38 matched identities, \"\n",
        "    \"rather than the total number of image observations. \"\n",
        "    \"This distinction is important when interpreting the \"\n",
        "    \"descriptive and inferential results.\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 5. VERIFY THE TARGET PARAGRAPH\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "if old_paragraph not in discussion_text:\n",
        "\n",
        "    if corrected_paragraph in discussion_text:\n",
        "\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\n",
        "            \"The correction already exists. \"\n",
        "            \"No replacement was necessary.\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        \"The expected original paragraph was not found. \"\n",
        "        \"The Discussion file has not been modified.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "if discussion_text.count(old_paragraph) != 1:\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        \"The original paragraph occurs more than once. \"\n",
        "        \"Manual review is required.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 6. APPLY THE COMPLETE PARAGRAPH REPLACEMENT\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "corrected_discussion = discussion_text.replace(\n",
        "    old_paragraph,\n",
        "    corrected_paragraph,\n",
        "    1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "if old_paragraph in corrected_discussion:\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
        "        \"Original paragraph remains after correction.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "if corrected_discussion.count(corrected_paragraph) != 1:\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
        "        \"Corrected paragraph validation failed.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 7. VERIFY SECTION 5.3 CONTEXT\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "section_start = corrected_discussion.find(\n",
        "    \"## 5.3 Identity-level consistency\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "section_end = corrected_discussion.find(\n",
        "    \"## 5.4 Relationship to previous illumination research\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "if section_start == -1 or section_end == -1:\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        \"Section 5.3 boundaries could not be verified.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "section_53 = corrected_discussion[\n",
        "    section_start:section_end\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "required_statements = [\n",
        "    \"646 near-frontal\",\n",
        "    \"418 oblique\",\n",
        "    \"1,064 large-angular-deviation\",\n",
        "    \"same 38 identities\",\n",
        "    \"38 matched identities\",\n",
        "    \"total number of image observations\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "for statement in required_statements:\n",
        "\n",
        "    if statement not in section_53:\n",
        "\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\n",
        "            f\"Section 5.3 is missing: {statement}\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 8. VERIFY ALL EIGHT DISCUSSION SECTIONS\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "required_headings = [\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"## 5.1 Principal findings\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"## 5.2 Interpretation of illumination geometry \"\n",
        "    \"and embedding displacement\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"## 5.3 Identity-level consistency and statistical evidence\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"## 5.4 Relationship to previous illumination research\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"## 5.5 Implications for face-embedding evaluation\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"## 5.6 Limitations\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"## 5.7 Future research directions\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"## 5.8 Overall discussion\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "for heading in required_headings:\n",
        "\n",
        "    if heading not in corrected_discussion:\n",
        "\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\n",
        "            f\"Required heading missing: {heading}\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 9. VERIFY LITERATURE REFERENCES\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "required_citations = [\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Moses et al. (1994)\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Beveridge et al. (2009)\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Han et al. (2013)\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Ochoa-Villegas et al. (2015)\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "for citation in required_citations:\n",
        "\n",
        "    if citation not in corrected_discussion:\n",
        "\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\n",
        "            f\"Required citation missing: {citation}\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 10. VERIFY SCIENTIFIC INTERPRETATION\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "scientific_checks = {\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Kendall's W interpretation\":\n",
        "        \"complete agreement in the ranking\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Euclidean and cosine relationship\":\n",
        "        \"squared Euclidean distance equals twice \"\n",
        "        \"the cosine distance\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Causal limitation\":\n",
        "        \"do not isolate a causal illumination effect\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Recognition limitation\":\n",
        "        \"does not establish whether a face-recognition \"\n",
        "        \"system accepts or rejects an identity correctly\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Drift-detection limitation\":\n",
        "        \"does not implement or validate an operational \"\n",
        "        \"drift detection system\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Architecture limitation\":\n",
        "        \"one fixed pretrained InceptionResnetV1\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Dataset provenance limitation\":\n",
        "        \"community-hosted Academic Torrents listing\",\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"Hemisphere limitation\":\n",
        "        \"does not isolate an independent hemisphere effect\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "for check_name, phrase in scientific_checks.items():\n",
        "\n",
        "    if phrase.lower() not in corrected_discussion.lower():\n",
        "\n",
        "        raise ValueError(\n",
        "            f\"Scientific interpretation check failed: \"\n",
        "            f\"{check_name}\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 11. PRESERVE RESULTS SOURCE HASHES\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "results_markdown_hash_before = hashlib.sha256(\n",
        "    RESULTS_MD.read_bytes()\n",
        ").hexdigest()\n",
        "\n",
        "results_json_hash_before = hashlib.sha256(\n",
        "    RESULTS_JSON.read_bytes()\n",
        ").hexdigest()\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 12. SAVE CORRECTED DISCUSSION\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "DISCUSSION_MD.write_text(\n",
        "    corrected_discussion,\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 13. UPDATE DISCUSSION JSON RECORD\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "corrected_markdown_hash = hashlib.sha256(\n",
        "    DISCUSSION_MD.read_bytes()\n",
        ").hexdigest()\n",
        "\n",
        "discussion_record[\"draft_word_count\"] = len(\n",
        "    corrected_discussion.split()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "discussion_record[\"markdown_sha256\"] = (\n",
        "    corrected_markdown_hash\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "discussion_record[\"status\"] = (\n",
        "    \"DISCUSSION_SECTION_DRAFT_CORRECTED\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "discussion_record[\"last_updated_utc\"] = (\n",
        "    datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "discussion_record[\"editorial_corrections\"] = [\n",
        "\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"section\": \"5.3 Identity-level consistency \"\n",
        "                   \"and statistical evidence\",\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"issue\": (\n",
        "            \"The previous paragraph could confuse unequal \"\n",
        "            \"image-observation counts with identity-level \"\n",
        "            \"sample sizes.\"\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"correction\": (\n",
        "            \"Explicitly distinguishes the 2,128 image \"\n",
        "            \"observations and unequal illumination-group \"\n",
        "            \"observation counts from the 38 matched identities \"\n",
        "            \"used in repeated-measures inference.\"\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"verified_identity_sample_size\": 38,\n",
        "\n",
        "        \"verified_observation_counts\": {\n",
        "\n",
        "            \"near_frontal\": 646,\n",
        "\n",
        "            \"oblique\": 418,\n",
        "\n",
        "            \"large_angular_deviation\": 1064\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "discussion_record[\"integrity_verification\"] = {\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"corrected_paragraph_found\": True,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"original_paragraph_removed\": True,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"all_eight_sections_verified\": True,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"all_four_existing_citations_verified\": True,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"scientific_interpretation_checks_passed\": True,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"results_markdown_modified\": False,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"results_json_modified\": False,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"frozen_experimental_files_modified\": False\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(\n",
        "    DISCUSSION_JSON,\n",
        "    \"w\",\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ") as f:\n",
        "\n",
        "    json.dump(\n",
        "        discussion_record,\n",
        "        f,\n",
        "        indent=2,\n",
        "        allow_nan=False\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 14. RELOAD AND VERIFY DISCUSSION FILES\n",
        "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "reloaded_markdown = DISCUSSION_MD.read_text(\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(\n",
        "    DISCUSSION_JSON,\n",
        "    \"r\",\n",
        "    encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
        ") as f:\n",
        "\n",
        "    reloaded_record = json.load(f)\n",
        "\n",
        "if reloaded_markdown != corrected_discussion:\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
        "        \"Markdown reload verification failed.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "if reloaded_record[\"status\"] != (\n",
        "    \"DISCUSSION_SECTION_DRAFT_CORRECTED\"\n",
        "):\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
        "        \"JSON status verification failed.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "reloaded_hash = hashlib.sha256(\n",
        "    DISCUSSION_MD.read_bytes()\n",
        ").hexdigest()\n",
        "\n",
        "if reloaded_hash != reloaded_record[\"markdown_sha256\"]:\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
