      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "## Step 3.3.14 — Identification of Outstanding Review Checks\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "This step examines the six Step 3.3.13 audit JSON reports to identify the specific checks that require manual scientific or editorial review.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Procedure\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Load all available audit JSON files from the Step 3.3.13 output directory.\n",
        "2. Inspect recorded check statuses and their associated details.\n",
        "3. Identify review-required, unresolved, warning, or pending records.\n",
        "4. Print the complete details of each identified record.\n",
        "5. Save a consolidated JSON report for subsequent review.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Data Integrity\n",
        "\n",
        "This is a read-only inspection of the existing audit reports. The original manuscript, frozen figures, experimental CSV files, and numerical results must remain unchanged.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Expected Output\n",
        "\n",
        "A consolidated report identifying outstanding review records, their source audit files, and their recorded details.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Completion Criteria\n",
        "\n",
        "The inspection must finish successfully, and the resulting report must be saved. Absence of automatically detected review records must not be interpreted as proof that all scientific checks have passed.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zTyyRO7B_2hb"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import json\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE = Path(\n",
        "    \"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results/step_3_3/step_3313\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "if not BASE.exists():\n",
        "    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Audit directory not found: {BASE}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "audit_files = sorted(BASE.glob(\"*audit.json\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "if not audit_files:\n",
        "    raise FileNotFoundError(\"No audit JSON files found.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "REVIEW_TERMS = {\n",
        "    \"review\", \"requires_review\", \"manual_review\",\n",
        "    \"needs_review\", \"pending\", \"warning\", \"unresolved\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "STATUS_KEYS = {\n",
        "    \"status\", \"result\", \"outcome\", \"verdict\",\n",
        "    \"assessment\", \"audit_status\", \"check_status\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "findings = []\n",
        "\n",
        "def inspect_json(obj, file_name, path=\"$\"):\n",
        "    if isinstance(obj, dict):\n",
        "        statuses = {\n",
        "            str(k).lower(): str(v).strip().lower()\n",
        "            for k, v in obj.items()\n",
        "            if str(k).lower() in STATUS_KEYS\n",
        "        }\n",
        "\n",
        "        review_statuses = {\n",
        "            k: v for k, v in statuses.items()\n",
        "            if any(term in v for term in REVIEW_TERMS)\n",
        "        }\n",
        "\n",
        "        if review_statuses:\n",
        "            findings.append({\n",
        "                \"file\": file_name,\n",
        "                \"path\": path,\n",
        "                \"status\": review_statuses,\n",
        "                \"record\": obj\n",
        "            })\n",
        "\n",
        "        for key, value in obj.items():\n",
        "            inspect_json(value, file_name, f\"{path}.{key}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    elif isinstance(obj, list):\n",
        "        for index, value in enumerate(obj):\n",
        "            inspect_json(value, file_name, f\"{path}[{index}]\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 90)\n",
        "print(\"EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.3.13 OUTSTANDING REVIEW CHECKS\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 90)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\nAudit files discovered: {len(audit_files)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for file_path in audit_files:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nLoading: {file_path.name}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    with file_path.open(\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "        data = json.load(f)\n",
        "\n",
        "    inspect_json(data, file_path.name)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 90)\n",
        "print(f\"REVIEW-STATUS RECORDS FOUND: {len(findings)}\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 90)\n",
        "\n",
        "if findings:\n",
        "    for number, item in enumerate(findings, start=1):\n",
        "        print(f\"\\nRECORD {number}\")\n",
        "        print(\"-\" * 70)\n",
        "        print(\"File:\", item[\"file\"])\n",
        "        print(\"JSON location:\", item[\"path\"])\n",
        "        print(\"Status:\", json.dumps(item[\"status\"], indent=2))\n",
        "        print(\"Full record:\")\n",
        "        print(json.dumps(item[\"record\"], indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        \"No review-status records were identified using the recognised \"\n",
        "        \"status fields. This does not prove that all checks passed.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "summary_path = BASE / \"experiment20_step3314_outstanding_review_checks.json\"\n",
        "\n",
        "output = {\n",
