        "\n",
        "## Step 3.3.16 — Verification of the Holm Multiple-Comparison Family\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "Determine whether the six pairwise comparisons were corrected using one family of six tests or two separate families of three tests.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Background\n",
        "\n",
        "The documented analysis decision specifies one Holm correction family containing all six pairwise comparisons across the Euclidean and cosine outcomes.\n",
        "\n",
        "The frozen paired-comparison CSV reports adjusted p-values that appear consistent with separate three-test correction families. This requires direct verification.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Procedure\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Load the frozen paired-comparison CSV.\n",
        "2. Extract all six raw p-values.\n",
        "3. Independently calculate Holm-adjusted p-values for one family of six.\n",
        "4. Independently calculate Holm-adjusted p-values separately for each metric, using three comparisons per metric.\n",
        "5. Compare both calculations with the frozen adjusted p-values.\n",
        "6. Record the discrepancy without modifying the source CSV.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Data Integrity\n",
        "\n",
        "No experimental data, statistical results, manuscript text, or frozen files will be modified.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Expected Output\n",
        "\n",
        "A numerical comparison of the two correction strategies and a clear determination of whether the frozen adjusted p-values follow the documented six-test family.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Completion Criteria\n",
        "\n",
        "The correction-family discrepancy must be identified and documented before the manuscript's inferential statistics are finalised.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "etyWb_-7Am7A"
      }
