            "    32: Friedman repeated-measures tests identified differences among the three illumination geometry groups for Euclidean displacement (χ²(2) = 76.0, p = 3.139e-17, Kendall's W = 1.0) and cosine distance (χ²(2) = 76.0, p = 3.139e-17, Kendall's W = 1.0). Each analysis included 38 identities measured across three groups.\n",
