            "Match 7 | Line 2174 | Terms: wilcoxon\n",
            "  2170: ### Methodology\n",
            "  2171: 1. Calculate median low-illumination displacement for each identity.\n",
            "  2172: 2. Calculate median high-illumination displacement for each identity.\n",
            "  2173: 3. Calculate the paired median displacement difference for each identity.\n",
            "  2174: 4. Apply a paired Wilcoxon signed-rank test across identities.\n",
            "  2175: 5. Report the number of identities showing greater displacement under high illumination.\n",
            "  2176: \n",
            "  2177: ### Research Purpose\n",
            "  2178: Reduce the risk of overstating statistical significance due to multiple correlated images belonging to the same identity.\n",
            "\n",
            "Match 8 | Line 2184 | Terms: wilcoxon\n",
            "  2180: ### Scientific Limitation\n",
            "  2181: The identity-level analysis contains only 13 independent identity groups, limiting statistical power.\n",
            "  2182: \n",
            "  2183: ### Status\n",
            "  2184: Successfully completed. Identity-level displacement statistics were calculated by aggregating paired image-level measurements using median displacement for each identity. The analysis included 13 evaluation identities. A paired Wilcoxon signed-rank test produced a statistic of 3.0 and a p-value of 0.001220703125. High-illumination median displacement was greater for 11 identities and lower for 2 identities. The median identity-level displacement difference was 0.079261. The result indicates a statistically significant identity-level difference, but the analysis remains limited by the small sample of 13 identities and the unequal number of images per identity.\n",
            "  2185: # CELL 60 (code)\n",
            "  2186: import numpy as np\n",
            "  2187: import pandas as pd\n",
            "  2188: from scipy.stats import wilcoxon\n",
