            "CELL 0 | TYPE: markdown | EXECUTION COUNT: None\n",
            "----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# Experiment 16: Cross-Condition Calibration Transfer for Embedding-Level Drift Detection\n",
            "\n",
            "## 1. Objective\n",
            "\n",
            "This experiment investigates whether embedding-level drift detection thresholds calibrated on one data distribution remain reliable when applied to a different target distribution.\n",
            "\n",
            "The study compares Euclidean distance and Ledoit–Wolf-regularized Mahalanobis distance under isotropic, anisotropic, and correlated synthetic embedding distributions.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 2. Research Questions\n",
            "\n",
            "1. How does transferring a frozen calibration threshold across distribution conditions affect the false-alarm rate?\n",
            "2. Does calibration transfer affect drift detection sensitivity?\n",
            "3. Do Euclidean and Mahalanobis detectors differ in their robustness to cross-condition calibration transfer?\n",
            "4. How do the results compare with condition-specific calibration thresholds?\n",
            "\n",
            "## 3. Experimental Methodology\n",
            "\n",
            "The experiment uses synthetic embeddings with a dimensionality of 64 and a window size of 20 embeddings. The evaluation is designed around 20 random seeds, with separate reference, calibration, control, and evaluation data.\n",
            "\n",
            "The principal stages are:\n",
            "\n",
            "- Generate synthetic embedding distributions with different covariance structures.\n",
            "- Calibrate detectors on a source condition and freeze the resulting thresholds.\n",
            "- Apply the frozen thresholds to independent control and drift-evaluation windows from target conditions.\n",
            "- Compare transferred-threshold performance against a condition-specific calibration benchmark.\n",
            "- Aggregate false-alarm rates and detection rates across random seeds.\n",
            "- Conduct statistical comparisons and numerical integrity checks.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 4. Detectors\n",
            "\n",
            "**Euclidean detector:** Measures the Euclidean distance between a window's mean embedding and the reference mean.\n",
            "\n",
            "**Mahalanobis detector:** Measures the distance using a regularized covariance estimate, accounting for variation and correlation among embedding dimensions.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 5. Evaluation Metrics\n",
            "\n",
            "- False-alarm rate on independent control windows.\n",
            "- Drift detection rate on evaluation windows with injected distribution shifts.\n",
            "- Difference in detection rates between detectors and calibration strategies.\n",
            "- Across-seed variability and confidence intervals.\n",
            "- Numerical stability and integrity audit results.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 6. Reproducibility\n",
            "\n",
            "The experiment records configuration parameters, software versions, random seeds, calibration thresholds, evaluation outputs, and validation checks. Results are saved under `results/experiment_16/`.\n",
            "\n",
            "## 7. Scope and Limitations\n",
            "\n",
            "This experiment uses synthetic embedding distributions. It evaluates statistical properties of the detectors and their calibration transfer; it does not establish real-world biometric recognition accuracy, fairness, or deployment readiness.\n",
            "\n",
            "All findings will be reported from the actual experiment outputs. No results are assumed in advance.\n",
            "\n",
            "====================================================================================================\n",
            "CELL 23 | TYPE: markdown | EXECUTION COUNT: None\n",
            "----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "# Experiment 16 — Step 12: Comparative Evaluation of Calibration Strategies\n",
            "\n",
            "## Objective\n",
            "\n",
            "This step evaluates the three calibration strategies using the shared independent control and drift evaluation datasets generated in Step 11.\n",
            "\n",
            "The purpose is to determine whether target-specific threshold recalibration and target-specific detector fitting improve calibration-transfer performance compared with the original frozen-source approach.\n",
            "\n",
            "## Evaluation Strategies\n",
            "\n",
            "**Method A — Frozen Source Calibration**\n",
            "\n",
            "Uses the source-condition reference mean, regularized covariance estimate, and frozen source-condition calibration threshold.\n",
            "\n",
            "**Method B — Target-Specific Threshold Recalibration**\n",
            "\n",
            "Retains the source-condition detector parameters but recalculates the threshold using target-condition calibration windows.\n",
            "\n",
            "**Method C — Full Target Adaptation**\n",
            "\n",
            "Uses target-condition detector parameters and target-condition calibration thresholds.\n",
            "\n",
            "## Evaluation Procedure\n",
            "\n",
            "For each random seed, source condition, target condition, and detector:\n",
            "\n",
            "1. Retrieve the corresponding detector parameters.\n",
            "2. Retrieve the threshold associated with each calibration strategy.\n",
            "3. Score the shared independent control windows.\n",
            "4. Calculate false alarms using the applicable threshold.\n",
            "5. Score the shared drift evaluation windows.\n",
            "6. Calculate detected drift windows using the same threshold.\n",
            "7. Record seed-level performance metrics for all three strategies.\n",
            "\n",
            "The same evaluation windows are used across all three methods to support paired comparisons.\n",
            "\n",
            "## Evaluation Metrics\n",
            "\n",
            "- False-alarm count and false-alarm rate.\n",
            "- Detected drift-window count and detection rate.\n",
            "- Across-seed variability.\n",
            "- Performance differences between calibration strategies.\n",
            "\n",
            "## Expected Output\n",
            "\n",
            "The experiment produces 1,080 seed-level evaluation records, representing:\n",
            "\n",
            "20 random seeds × 3 source conditions × 3 target conditions × 2 detectors × 3 methods.\n",
            "\n",
            "The results are saved separately for control evaluation, drift evaluation, and combined performance summaries.\n",
            "\n",
            "## Interpretation and Limitations\n",
            "\n",
            "A lower false-alarm rate does not necessarily imply improved drift detection sensitivity. Both metrics must be considered together.\n",
            "\n",
            "Method C represents a target-adapted benchmark and assumes access to target-condition reference and calibration data. It is not equivalent to zero-shot source-to-target transfer.\n",
            "\n",
            "All results remain limited to the specified synthetic multivariate Gaussian simulation conditions.\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "====================================================================================================\n",
            "CELL 25 | TYPE: markdown | EXECUTION COUNT: None\n",
            "----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "## Step 13: Paired Statistical Comparison of Calibration Methods\n",
            "\n",
            "This step performs paired statistical comparisons of the three calibration strategies:\n",
            "\n",
            "- Method A: Frozen source detector and frozen source threshold.\n",
            "- Method B: Source detector with target-specific threshold recalibration.\n",
            "- Method C: Target-fitted detector with target-specific threshold.\n",
            "\n",
            "The analysis uses the 20 independent random-seed replicates and compares methods under identical source-target scenarios and shared evaluation datasets.\n",
            "\n",
            "The evaluated metrics are:\n",
            "\n",
            "1. False-alarm rate.\n",
            "2. Detection rate.\n",
            "\n",
            "Pairwise comparisons are conducted using the Wilcoxon signed-rank test. Mean paired differences and 95% bootstrap confidence intervals are also calculated. Holm correction is applied to account for multiple comparisons.\n",
            "\n",
            "These comparisons assess statistical differences within the synthetic experimental setting and do not establish real-world biometric performance.\n",
            "\n",
            "====================================================================================================\n",
            "CELL 26 | TYPE: code | EXECUTION COUNT: 17\n",
            "----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# ============================================================\n",
            "# EXPERIMENT 16 — STEP 13:\n",
            "# PAIRED STATISTICAL COMPARISON OF METHODS A, B AND C\n",
            "# ============================================================\n",
            "\n",
            "import numpy as np\n",
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "from scipy.stats import wilcoxon\n",
            "\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# 1. Configuration\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "METHODS = [\n",
            "    \"A_frozen_source\",\n",
            "    \"B_source_detector_target_threshold\",\n",
            "    \"C_target_detector_target_threshold\"\n",
            "]\n",
            "\n",
            "METRICS = [\n",
            "    \"observed_false_alarm_rate\",\n",
            "    \"detection_rate\"\n",
            "]\n",
            "\n",
            "PAIRWISE_COMPARISONS = [\n",
            "    (\"A_frozen_source\", \"B_source_detector_target_threshold\"),\n",
            "    (\"A_frozen_source\", \"C_target_detector_target_threshold\"),\n",
            "    (\"B_source_detector_target_threshold\",\n",
            "     \"C_target_detector_target_threshold\")\n",
            "]\n",
            "\n",
            "N_BOOTSTRAP = 10000\n",
            "BOOTSTRAP_SEED = 202616\n",
            "\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# 2. Reconstruct seed-level paired evaluation dataset\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "merge_keys = [\n",
            "    \"seed\",\n",
            "    \"source_condition\",\n",
            "    \"target_condition\",\n",
            "    \"detector\",\n",
            "    \"method\"\n",
            "]\n",
            "\n",
            "seed_level_df = comparative_control_df.merge(\n",
            "    comparative_drift_df[\n",
            "        merge_keys + [\n",
            "            \"detection_rate\",\n",
            "            \"detected_windows\"\n",
            "        ]\n",
            "    ],\n",
            "    on=merge_keys,\n",
            "    how=\"inner\",\n",
            "    validate=\"one_to_one\"\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "expected_records = (\n",
            "    CONFIG[\"n_seeds\"]\n",
            "    * len(CONDITIONS)\n",
            "    * len(CONDITIONS)\n",
            "    * len(CONFIG[\"detectors\"])\n",
            "    * len(METHODS)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "assert len(seed_level_df) == expected_records, (\n",
            "    f\"Expected {expected_records} paired records, \"\n",
            "    f\"found {len(seed_level_df)}\"\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "assert seed_level_df[\"seed\"].nunique() == CONFIG[\"n_seeds\"]\n",
            "\n",
            "assert seed_level_df[METRICS].notna().all().all()\n",
            "\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# 3. Bootstrap confidence interval function\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "def paired_bootstrap_ci(\n",
            "    differences,\n",
            "    n_bootstrap=10000,\n",
            "    confidence_level=0.95,\n",
            "    random_seed=202616\n",
            "):\n",
            "    differences = np.asarray(differences, dtype=float)\n",
            "\n",
            "    rng = np.random.default_rng(random_seed)\n",
            "\n",
            "    n = len(differences)\n",
            "\n",
            "    bootstrap_means = np.empty(n_bootstrap)\n",
            "\n",
            "    for i in range(n_bootstrap):\n",
            "        sampled = rng.choice(\n",
            "            differences,\n",
            "            size=n,\n",
            "            replace=True\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "        bootstrap_means[i] = np.mean(sampled)\n",
            "\n",
            "    alpha = 1 - confidence_level\n",
            "\n",
            "    lower = np.quantile(\n",
            "        bootstrap_means,\n",
            "        alpha / 2\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    upper = np.quantile(\n",
            "        bootstrap_means,\n",
            "        1 - alpha / 2\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "    return lower, upper\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# 4. Holm multiple-testing correction\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "def holm_adjust(p_values):\n",
            "\n",
            "    p_values = np.asarray(p_values, dtype=float)\n",
            "\n",
            "    n = len(p_values)\n",
            "\n",
            "    order = np.argsort(p_values)\n",
            "\n",
            "    adjusted = np.empty(n)\n",
            "\n",
            "    running_max = 0.0\n",
            "\n",
            "    for rank, index in enumerate(order):\n",
            "\n",
            "        adjusted_value = (\n",
            "            (n - rank) * p_values[index]\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "        running_max = max(\n",
            "            running_max,\n",
            "            adjusted_value\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "        adjusted[index] = min(\n",
            "            running_max,\n",
            "            1.0\n",
            "        )\n",
            "\n",
            "    return adjusted\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# 5. Run paired comparisons\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "results = []\n",
            "\n",
            "scenario_columns = [\n",
            "    \"source_condition\",\n",
            "    \"target_condition\",\n",
            "    \"detector\"\n",
            "]\n",
            "\n",
            "rng_seed_offset = 0\n",
            "\n",
            "for metric in METRICS:\n",
            "\n",
            "    for source in CONDITIONS:\n",
            "\n",
            "        for target in CONDITIONS:\n",
            "\n",
            "            for detector in CONFIG[\"detectors\"]:\n",
            "\n",
            "                subset = seed_level_df[\n",
            "                    (seed_level_df[\"source_condition\"] == source)\n",
            "                    & (seed_level_df[\"target_condition\"] == target)\n",
            "                    & (seed_level_df[\"detector\"] == detector)\n",
            "                ]\n",
            "\n",
            "                pivot = subset.pivot(\n",
            "                    index=\"seed\",\n",
            "                    columns=\"method\",\n",
            "                    values=metric\n",
            "                )\n",
            "\n",
            "                pivot = pivot.reindex(columns=METHODS)\n",
            "\n",
            "                pivot = pivot.dropna()\n",
            "\n",
            "                if len(pivot) != CONFIG[\"n_seeds\"]:\n",
            "                    raise ValueError(\n",
            "                        f\"Incomplete paired data: \"\n",
            "                        f\"{source} -> {target}, \"\n",
            "                        f\"{detector}, {metric}\"\n",
            "                    )\n",
            "\n",
            "                for method_1, method_2 in PAIRWISE_COMPARISONS:\n",
            "\n",
            "                    # Positive difference means method_2\n",
            "                    # has a higher metric than method_1.\n",
            "                    differences = (\n",
            "                        pivot[method_2].to_numpy()\n",
            "                        - pivot[method_1].to_numpy()\n",
            "                    )\n",
            "\n",
            "                    mean_difference = np.mean(differences)\n",
            "\n",
            "                    median_difference = np.median(differences)\n",
            "\n",
            "                    if np.allclose(differences, 0):\n",
            "\n",
            "                        statistic = 0.0\n",
            "                        p_value = 1.0\n",
            "\n",
            "                    else:\n",
            "\n",
            "                        test = wilcoxon(\n",
            "                            pivot[method_1].to_numpy(),\n",
            "                            pivot[method_2].to_numpy(),\n",
            "                            alternative=\"two-sided\",\n",
            "                            zero_method=\"wilcox\",\n",
            "                            method=\"auto\"\n",
            "                        )\n",
            "\n",
            "                        statistic = float(test.statistic)\n",
            "                        p_value = float(test.pvalue)\n",
            "\n",
            "                    ci_lower, ci_upper = paired_bootstrap_ci(\n",
            "                        differences,\n",
            "                        n_bootstrap=N_BOOTSTRAP,\n",
            "                        random_seed=(\n",
            "                            BOOTSTRAP_SEED + rng_seed_offset\n",
            "                        )\n",
            "                    )\n",
            "\n",
            "                    rng_seed_offset += 1\n",
            "\n",
            "                    results.append({\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"metric\": metric,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"source_condition\": source,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"target_condition\": target,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"scenario_type\": (\n",
            "                            \"same_condition\"\n",
            "                            if source == target\n",
            "                            else \"cross_condition\"\n",
            "                        ),\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"detector\": detector,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"method_1\": method_1,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"method_2\": method_2,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"n_seed_pairs\": len(differences),\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"mean_method_1\": np.mean(\n",
            "                            pivot[method_1]\n",
            "                        ),\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"mean_method_2\": np.mean(\n",
            "                            pivot[method_2]\n",
            "                        ),\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"mean_paired_difference\": mean_difference,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"median_paired_difference\": median_difference,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"ci_95_lower\": ci_lower,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"ci_95_upper\": ci_upper,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"wilcoxon_statistic\": statistic,\n",
            "\n",
            "                        \"p_value\": p_value\n",
            "                    })\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# 6. Create statistical results DataFrame\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "paired_statistics_df = pd.DataFrame(results)\n",
            "\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# 7. Apply Holm correction separately for each metric\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "paired_statistics_df[\"holm_adjusted_p_value\"] = np.nan\n",
            "\n",
            "for metric in METRICS:\n",
            "\n",
            "    mask = paired_statistics_df[\"metric\"] == metric\n",
            "\n",
            "    paired_statistics_df.loc[\n",
            "        mask,\n",
            "        \"holm_adjusted_p_value\"\n",
            "    ] = holm_adjust(\n",
            "        paired_statistics_df.loc[\n",
            "            mask,\n",
            "            \"p_value\"\n",
            "        ].to_numpy()\n",
            "    )\n",
            "\n",
            "paired_statistics_df[\"significant_after_holm\"] = (\n",
            "    paired_statistics_df[\"holm_adjusted_p_value\"] < 0.05\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# 8. Validate statistical results\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "expected_comparisons = (\n",
            "    len(METRICS)\n",
            "    * len(CONDITIONS)\n",
            "    * len(CONDITIONS)\n",
            "    * len(CONFIG[\"detectors\"])\n",
            "    * len(PAIRWISE_COMPARISONS)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "assert len(paired_statistics_df) == expected_comparisons\n",
            "\n",
            "assert paired_statistics_df[\n",
            "    \"p_value\"\n",
            "].between(0, 1).all()\n",
            "\n",
            "assert paired_statistics_df[\n",
            "    \"holm_adjusted_p_value\"\n",
            "].between(0, 1).all()\n",
            "\n",
            "numeric_columns = [\n",
            "    \"mean_method_1\",\n",
            "    \"mean_method_2\",\n",
            "    \"mean_paired_difference\",\n",
            "    \"median_paired_difference\",\n",
            "    \"ci_95_lower\",\n",
            "    \"ci_95_upper\",\n",
            "    \"wilcoxon_statistic\",\n",
            "    \"p_value\",\n",
            "    \"holm_adjusted_p_value\"\n",
            "]\n",
            "\n",
            "assert np.isfinite(\n",
            "    paired_statistics_df[numeric_columns].to_numpy()\n",
            ").all()\n",
            "\n",
            "assert (\n",
            "    paired_statistics_df[\"n_seed_pairs\"]\n",
            "    == CONFIG[\"n_seeds\"]\n",
            ").all()\n",
            "\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# 9. Save statistical results\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "paired_statistics_df.to_csv(\n",
            "    RESULTS_DIR / \"paired_statistical_comparisons.csv\",\n",
            "    index=False\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "# 10. Display results\n",
            "# ------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
            "print(\"EXPERIMENT 16 — STEP 13: PAIRED STATISTICAL COMPARISON\")\n",
            "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Seed-level paired records:\", len(seed_level_df))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Statistical comparisons:\", len(paired_statistics_df))\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Expected comparisons:\", expected_comparisons)\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"Independent seed replicates:\", CONFIG[\"n_seeds\"])\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nSignificant comparisons after Holm correction:\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\n",
            "    paired_statistics_df[\n",
            "        \"significant_after_holm\"\n",
            "    ].sum()\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nFalse-alarm rate comparisons:\")\n",
            "\n",
            "display(\n",
            "    paired_statistics_df[\n",
            "        paired_statistics_df[\"metric\"]\n",
            "        == \"observed_false_alarm_rate\"\n",
            "    ].round(5)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nDetection rate comparisons:\")\n",
            "\n",
            "display(\n",
            "    paired_statistics_df[\n",
            "        paired_statistics_df[\"metric\"]\n",
            "        == \"detection_rate\"\n",
            "    ].round(5)\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nSaved:\")\n",
            "print(\"paired_statistical_comparisons.csv\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nValidation:\")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\n",
            "    \"Correct comparison count:\",\n",
            "    len(paired_statistics_df) == expected_comparisons\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\n",
            "    \"All p-values valid:\",\n",
            "    paired_statistics_df[\"p_value\"].between(0, 1).all()\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\n",
            "    \"All adjusted p-values valid:\",\n",
            "    paired_statistics_df[\n",
            "        \"holm_adjusted_p_value\"\n",
            "    ].between(0, 1).all()\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\n",
            "    \"All comparisons use 20 seed pairs:\",\n",
            "    (\n",
            "        paired_statistics_df[\"n_seed_pairs\"]\n",
            "        == CONFIG[\"n_seeds\"]\n",
            "    ).all()\n",
            ")\n",
            "\n",
            "print(\"\\nSTEP 13 COMPLETED.\")\n",
            "print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
            "\n",
            "SAVED CELL OUTPUTS\n",
            "\n",
            "Output 1:\n",
            "======================================================================\n",
            "EXPERIMENT 16 — STEP 13: PAIRED STATISTICAL COMPARISON\n",
            "======================================================================\n",
            "Seed-level paired records: 1080\n",
            "Statistical comparisons: 108\n",
            "Expected comparisons: 108\n",
            "Independent seed replicates: 20\n",
            "\n",
            "Significant comparisons after Holm correction:\n",
            "51\n",
            "\n",
            "False-alarm rate comparisons:\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "Output 2:\n",
            "                       metric source_condition target_condition  \\\n",
            "0   observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "1   observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "2   observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "3   observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "4   observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "5   observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "6   observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "7   observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "8   observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "9   observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "10  observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "11  observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "12  observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic       correlated   \n",
            "13  observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic       correlated   \n",
            "14  observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic       correlated   \n",
            "15  observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic       correlated   \n",
            "16  observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic       correlated   \n",
            "17  observed_false_alarm_rate        isotropic       correlated   \n",
            "18  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "19  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "20  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "21  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "22  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "23  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic        isotropic   \n",
            "24  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "25  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "26  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "27  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "28  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "29  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic      anisotropic   \n",
            "30  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic       correlated   \n",
            "31  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic       correlated   \n",
            "32  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic       correlated   \n",
            "33  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic       correlated   \n",
            "34  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic       correlated   \n",
            "35  observed_false_alarm_rate      anisotropic       correlated   \n",
            "36  observed_false_alarm_rate       correlated        isotropic   \n",
            "37  observed_false_alarm_rate       correlated        isotropic   \n",
            "38  observed_false_alarm_rate       correlated        isotropic   \n",
            "39  observed_false_alarm_rate       correlated        isotropic   \n",
            "40  observed_false_alarm_rate       correlated        isotropic   \n",
