      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "## Step 3.3.20 — Identity-Level Statistical Input Inspection\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "Locate and inspect the Experiment 20 CSV files that contain identity-level group measurements and paired comparison results.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Inspection Targets\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Identity-level group means.\n",
        "2. Existing paired comparison results.\n",
        "3. Any intermediate identity-level statistical input files.\n",
        "4. Column names, row counts, sample records, and SHA256 hashes.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Integrity Rules\n",
        "\n",
        "- Do not modify or overwrite any file.\n",
        "- Do not recalculate statistical results in this step.\n",
        "- Do not assume column names or data structure.\n",
        "- Do not treat the frozen comparison CSV as the original identity-level input.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Expected Outcome\n",
        "\n",
        "Identify the exact source data required to independently reproduce the six Wilcoxon tests and verify the combined six-test Holm correction.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hj_rRiiQB0sS"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import hashlib\n",
        "\n",
        "ROOT = Path(\n",
        "    \"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "if not ROOT.exists():\n",
        "    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Experiment 20 directory not found: {ROOT}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "keywords = (\n",
        "    \"identity\",\n",
        "    \"group_mean\",\n",
        "    \"paired\",\n",
        "    \"comparison\",\n",
        "    \"statistical\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "matches = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for path in ROOT.rglob(\"*.csv\"):\n",
        "    if any(term in path.name.lower() for term in keywords):\n",
        "        matches.append(path)\n",
        "\n",
        "matches = sorted(matches)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 100)\n",
        "print(\"EXPERIMENT 20 — STEP 3.3.20 IDENTITY-LEVEL INPUT INSPECTION\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 100)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n1. SEARCH SUMMARY\")\n",
        "print(\"-\" * 100)\n",
        "print(\"Search root:\", ROOT)\n",
        "print(\"Matching CSV files:\", len(matches))\n",
        "\n",
        "if not matches:\n",
        "    print(\"No matching CSV files found.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for index, path in enumerate(matches, start=1):\n",
        "    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 100)\n",
        "    print(f\"FILE {index}: {path}\")\n",
        "    print(\"-\" * 100)\n",
        "\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        raw = path.read_bytes()\n",
        "        digest = hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()\n",
        "\n",
        "        df = pd.read_csv(path)\n",
        "\n",
        "        print(\"SHA256:\", digest)\n",
        "        print(\"Rows:\", len(df))\n",
        "        print(\"Columns:\", len(df.columns))\n",
        "        print(\"Column names:\")\n",
        "        print(df.columns.tolist())\n",
        "\n",
        "        print(\"\\nFirst five rows:\")\n",
        "        print(df.head(5).to_string(index=False))\n",
        "\n",
        "        print(\"\\nData types:\")\n",
        "        print(df.dtypes.to_string())\n",
        "\n",
        "    except Exception as exc:\n",
        "        print(\"INSPECTION ERROR:\", repr(exc))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 100)\n",
        "print(\"2. INTEGRITY CONFIRMATION\")\n",
        "print(\"-\" * 100)\n",
        "print(\"Files modified: NO\")\n",
        "print(\"Statistical tests executed: NO\")\n",
        "print(\"Holm correction recalculated: NO\")\n",
        "print(\"Frozen results overwritten: NO\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nSTEP 3.3.20 COMPLETED\")\n",
        "print(\"Send the complete output.\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 100)\n"
      ],
