      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Section 3.3: Final Verification and Closure\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "Complete the final integrity verification of the Experiment 20 integrated manuscript and formally determine whether Section 3.3 is ready for closure.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Scope of Final Verification\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Manuscript integrity:** Confirm that the integrated manuscript (Version 2) remains unchanged from the verified version.\n",
        "2. **Table 1:** Verify all six descriptive-statistics rows against the frozen observation-level descriptive-statistics CSV, including observation counts, identity counts, condition counts, means, and standard deviations.\n",
        "3. **Table 2:** Verify all six raw p-values and all six combined six-test Holm-adjusted p-values using the corresponding manuscript columns.\n",
        "4. **Hemisphere analysis:** Verify both Euclidean and cosine comparison results, including group means, paired differences, and the separately corrected two-test Holm values.\n",
        "5. **Figures:** Confirm that all four embedded figures exist, retain their verified SHA256 hashes, and are referenced in the manuscript.\n",
        "6. **Audit records:** Confirm the presence of the required previous audit and verification reports.\n",
        "7. **Scientific interpretation:** Confirm that the manuscript retains the study's methodological limitations and does not overstate recognition accuracy, operational drift-detection capability, causal effects, or cross-architecture generalisation.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Scientific Interpretation Boundaries\n",
        "\n",
        "- Euclidean and cosine distances are mathematically related for L2-normalised embeddings and must not be presented as independent evidence.\n",
        "- The hemisphere comparison remains exploratory because hemisphere membership is associated with angular illumination geometry and unequal condition counts.\n",
        "- The findings characterise reference-relative embedding displacement within the evaluated dataset, preprocessing procedure, and fixed pretrained model.\n",
        "- The results do not establish recognition accuracy, operational drift-detection performance, deployment readiness, or generalisation across independent recognition architectures.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Integrity Restrictions\n",
        "\n",
        "- This is a read-only verification of existing research evidence.\n",
        "- Do not modify the integrated manuscript, frozen CSV files, figures, or previous audit records.\n",
        "- Preserve the documented historical Holm-correction discrepancy.\n",
        "- Save the final closure record as a new file without overwriting earlier evidence.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Completion Criterion\n",
        "\n",
        "Section 3.3 may be declared complete only if every required verification check passes. Any failed check must remain explicitly unresolved and must not be bypassed to force a completion status."
      ],
