      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Phase 3.4: Results and Statistical Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "Conduct a focused scientific review of the Results section in the integrated manuscript (Version 2), ensuring that the reported findings are statistically accurate, logically interpreted, and consistent with the frozen experimental evidence.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Review scope\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. Cohort and dataset reporting\n",
        "- Verify the evaluated dataset and image counts.\n",
        "- Verify identity and illumination-condition counts.\n",
        "- Confirm reference observations and evaluation observations are distinguished correctly.\n",
        "- Check the illumination geometry group definitions.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Descriptive results\n",
        "- Review Euclidean displacement and cosine distance statistics.\n",
        "- Confirm that means, medians, standard deviations, ranges, and group-level results are interpreted correctly.\n",
        "- Distinguish observation-level statistics from identity-level statistics.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. Inferential statistical results\n",
        "- Review the Friedman repeated-measures tests.\n",
        "- Verify the interpretation of Kendall's W.\n",
        "- Review the six pairwise Wilcoxon comparisons and combined six-test Holm correction.\n",
        "- Verify bootstrap confidence intervals and identity-level resampling descriptions.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Exploratory hemisphere analysis\n",
        "- Review frontal versus beyond-frontal comparisons.\n",
        "- Verify the reported differences, confidence intervals, and two-test Holm correction.\n",
        "- Preserve the exploratory nature of this analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5. Scientific interpretation\n",
        "- Distinguish statistical significance from practical significance.\n",
        "- Avoid treating Euclidean and cosine distances as independent evidence because they are mathematically related for L2-normalised embeddings.\n",
        "- Avoid causal interpretations of illumination geometry.\n",
        "- Avoid claims about recognition accuracy, operational drift detection, fairness, deployment readiness, or cross-architecture generalisation.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Integrity requirements\n",
        "- Use the integrated manuscript v2 and frozen experimental evidence.\n",
        "- Do not modify the manuscript or frozen evidence.\n",
        "- Do not invent missing statistics or interpretations.\n",
        "- Record unsupported, incomplete, or potentially misleading statements for review.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Expected output\n",
        "\n",
        "A structured Results and Statistical Interpretation Audit Report identifying:\n",
        "1. Verified findings.\n",
        "2. Statistical interpretation issues.\n",
        "3. Missing reporting elements.\n",
        "4. Potential overclaims.\n",
        "5. Required corrections, if any.\n",
        "\n",
        "The section is complete only after the audit findings have been reviewed and all material issues have been resolved or explicitly documented."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ZZ1pHcBWNuPz"
      }
