      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Experiment 20 — Phase 3.5: Discussion and Limitations Audit\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "Review the Discussion section of the integrated manuscript (Version 2) to ensure that the interpretation of the experimental findings is scientifically defensible, appropriately connected to the research objectives, and transparent about methodological limitations.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Review scope\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. Interpretation of findings\n",
        "- Examine the progressive increase in embedding displacement across near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular illumination groups.\n",
        "- Assess whether the discussion correctly interprets the identity-level statistical findings.\n",
        "- Distinguish observed associations from causal explanations.\n",
        "- Avoid presenting statistical significance as proof of practical recognition failure.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Research contribution\n",
        "- Assess whether the manuscript clearly identifies its empirical contribution.\n",
        "- Ensure that the contribution is limited to reference-relative embedding displacement under the evaluated illumination conditions.\n",
        "- Check that the manuscript does not claim a new recognition architecture or operational drift-detection system.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. Methodological limitations\n",
        "Review whether the manuscript adequately discusses:\n",
        "- The use of one pretrained FaceNet architecture.\n",
        "- The selected Extended Yale B cropped frontal-pose subset.\n",
        "- The exclusion of ambient images and incomplete subjects or conditions.\n",
        "- Direct image resizing instead of successful face detection and alignment.\n",
        "- The use of one reference illumination condition per identity.\n",
        "- The distinction between different illumination captures and transformations of identical source images.\n",
        "- The absence of recognition-performance evaluation and calibrated detection thresholds.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Statistical and interpretive limitations\n",
        "- Preserve the mathematical relationship between Euclidean and cosine distances for L2-normalised embeddings.\n",
        "- Explain that the hemisphere analysis is exploratory.\n",
        "- Avoid causal claims about illumination direction.\n",
        "- Avoid claims of fairness, deployment readiness, or cross-architecture generalisation.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5. Future research recommendations\n",
        "Assess whether proposed future work follows logically from the actual limitations and does not imply that unperformed experiments have already been completed.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Integrity requirements\n",
        "- Use the verified integrated manuscript v2.\n",
        "- Do not modify the manuscript or frozen evidence.\n",
        "- Do not invent contributions, citations, experiments, or limitations.\n",
        "- Identify unsupported claims and missing discussion elements explicitly.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Expected output\n",
        "\n",
        "A structured Discussion and Limitations Audit Report containing:\n",
        "1. Verified interpretations.\n",
        "2. Research contribution assessment.\n",
        "3. Methodological limitations assessment.\n",
        "4. Statistical and causal interpretation assessment.\n",
        "5. Future research alignment.\n",
        "6. Issues requiring correction, if any.\n",
        "\n",
        "Phase 3.5 is complete only after all material findings have been reviewed and resolved or explicitly documented."
      ],
