        "# Experiment 20 — Phase 3.6: Abstract and Conclusion Review\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "Evaluate the Abstract and concluding statements of the integrated manuscript (Version 2) to ensure that they accurately summarise the research objectives, methodology, principal findings, contributions, and limitations.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Review scope\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. Abstract\n",
        "- Verify that the research problem and objective are clearly stated.\n",
        "- Confirm that the dataset, model, embedding dimensions, and experimental scope are accurately described.\n",
        "- Check the reported sample size and principal numerical findings.\n",
        "- Verify that the statistical findings are represented accurately.\n",
        "- Ensure that Euclidean and cosine distances are not presented as independent evidence.\n",
        "- Check that the abstract does not claim recognition accuracy, operational drift detection, or deployment readiness.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Conclusion\n",
        "- Determine whether a standalone Conclusion section exists.\n",
        "- If no standalone section exists, evaluate the concluding subsection of the Discussion.\n",
        "- Confirm that the conclusion reflects the actual experimental findings.\n",
        "- Ensure that the research contribution is appropriately bounded.\n",
        "- Check that limitations and future research directions are consistent with the Discussion.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. Cross-section consistency\n",
        "- Compare the Abstract and conclusion with the verified Results and Discussion.\n",
        "- Check numerical consistency for the cohort, group means, and statistical findings.\n",
        "- Identify unsupported claims, missing qualifications, or contradictions.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Integrity requirements\n",
        "- Use the verified integrated manuscript v2 and frozen experimental evidence.\n",
        "- Do not modify the manuscript or frozen evidence.\n",
        "- Do not invent missing conclusions or research contributions.\n",
        "- Preserve the distinction between descriptive embedding displacement and recognition performance.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Expected output\n",
        "\n",
        "An Abstract and Conclusion Audit Report identifying:\n",
        "1. Abstract accuracy and completeness.\n",
        "2. Conclusion accuracy and completeness.\n",
        "3. Numerical consistency.\n",
        "4. Scientific overclaims or contradictions.\n",
        "5. Required corrections, if any.\n",
        "\n",
        "Phase 3.6 is complete only after all material issues have been reviewed and resolved or explicitly documented."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "liWpzSTXOoFa"
      }
