        "\n",
        "## Phase 3.7 — References and Citation Integrity Audit\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "This section audits the reference list and in-text citations of the Experiment 20 manuscript.\n",
        "\n",
        "The audit will examine:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Whether a references or bibliography section exists.\n",
        "2. Whether individual reference entries can be identified.\n",
        "3. Whether in-text citations are present and consistent with the manuscript's citation style.\n",
        "4. Whether cited author-year references can be matched against the reference list, where the formatting permits automated matching.\n",
        "5. Whether reference entries appear duplicated.\n",
        "6. Whether bibliographic information appears incomplete or inconsistent.\n",
        "7. Whether the reference list supports the study's methodological and scientific claims.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Audit boundaries\n",
        "\n",
        "- The existing manuscript will remain unchanged.\n",
        "- No references will be added, removed, or rewritten automatically.\n",
        "- No publication details will be invented.\n",
        "- Automated matching results will be treated as diagnostic findings, not definitive proof of citation validity.\n",
        "- Any ambiguous or unmatched references will be presented for manual verification.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Expected outcome\n",
        "\n",
        "A structured audit report containing the reference-section extraction, citation inventory, duplicate checks, potential inconsistencies, and items requiring manual review.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Completion criterion:** All references and citations must be reviewed, and unresolved issues must be documented before the manuscript proceeds to final submission preparation.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "tmfqgipPPrPh"
      }
