            "  \"created_utc\": \"2026-11-11T10:42:32.788904+00:00\",\n",
            "  \"draft_text\": \"Illumination conditions were grouped according to the angular deviation of the light source from the camera-facing direction. The angular deviation, denoted by θ, was calculated from the recorded illumination azimuth and elevation angles using θ = cos⁻¹(cos(elevation) × cos(azimuth)). The angular values were expressed in degrees for interpretation and grouping.\\n\\nThree study-specific illumination geometry groups were defined. Near-frontal conditions comprised observations with θ ≤ 30°. Oblique co...[truncated]\",\n",
