      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "# Experiment 20 — Phase 4.4\n",
        "## Statistical Results Reproducibility Audit\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "Independently reconstruct and verify the descriptive and inferential statistical results reported in Experiment 20 using the frozen reference-relative displacement evaluation dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Frozen input\n",
        "\n",
        "`experiment20_reference_evaluation_displacement.csv`\n",
        "\n",
        "Expected dataset:\n",
        "- 2,128 evaluation observations\n",
        "- 38 identities\n",
        "- 56 evaluation conditions\n",
        "- Three illumination geometry groups\n",
        "- Two hemisphere categories\n",
        "- One identity-specific reference observation per identity\n",
        "\n",
        "### Statistical audit scope\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Reconstruct observation-level descriptive statistics for Euclidean displacement and cosine distance.\n",
        "2. Aggregate observations by identity and illumination geometry group.\n",
        "3. Reconstruct Friedman tests and Kendall's W for the three geometry groups.\n",
        "4. Reconstruct all six paired Wilcoxon comparisons.\n",
        "5. Apply a single combined Holm correction across the six pairwise tests.\n",
        "6. Aggregate observations by identity and hemisphere.\n",
        "7. Reconstruct the two exploratory hemisphere comparisons.\n",
        "8. Reconstruct identity-level bootstrap confidence intervals using the recorded seeds and resampling design.\n",
        "9. Compare the reconstructed statistics against the reported manuscript values.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Statistical boundaries\n",
        "\n",
        "- Observation-level descriptive statistics and identity-level inferential tests must remain distinct.\n",
        "- The identity is the inferential unit for paired group comparisons.\n",
        "- Euclidean displacement and cosine distance are mathematically related for L2-normalised embeddings; they are not independent evidence.\n",
        "- The hemisphere comparison is exploratory and is confounded with angular geometry and unequal condition counts.\n",
        "- This audit does not establish recognition accuracy, fairness, causality, or deployment readiness.\n",
        "- Frozen evaluation data, statistical evidence, and manuscript files must not be modified.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ofIHSZHsTxRS"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "# =================================================================================================\n",
        "# EXPERIMENT 20 — PHASE 4.4\n",
        "# COMPLETE REPLACEMENT: STATISTICAL RESULTS REPRODUCIBILITY AUDIT\n",
        "# =================================================================================================\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Reconstructs descriptive statistics, identity-level inferential tests,\n",
        "# Holm corrections, and paired identity-level bootstrap confidence intervals.\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Corrects:\n",
        "#   1. Geometry and hemisphere label mapping checks.\n",
        "#   2. NumPy/Pandas JSON serialization.\n",
        "#   3. Separates reproduced statistical results from bootstrap provenance differences.\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Does NOT modify:\n",
        "#   - Frozen evaluation CSV\n",
        "#   - Manuscript\n",
        "#   - Existing Phase 4.4 audit report\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Creates a separate corrected audit report.\n",
        "# =================================================================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import hashlib\n",
        "import platform\n",
        "import warnings\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import scipy\n",
        "from scipy.stats import friedmanchisquare, wilcoxon\n",
        "from statsmodels.stats.multitest import multipletests\n",
        "\n",
        "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=RuntimeWarning)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 100)\n",
        "print(\"EXPERIMENT 20 — PHASE 4.4 STATISTICAL RESULTS REPRODUCIBILITY AUDIT\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 100)\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 1. PATHS AND EXPECTED INPUT INTEGRITY\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "BASE = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\"\n",
        "\n",
        "CSV_PATH = (\n",
        "    f\"{BASE}/step_2_7/final_freeze/\"\n",
        "    \"experiment20_reference_evaluation_displacement.csv\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = f\"{BASE}/step_4_4_statistical_reproducibility\"\n",
        "\n",
        "ORIGINAL_REPORT_PATH = (\n",
        "    f\"{OUTPUT_DIR}/experiment20_phase44_statistical_reproducibility_audit.json\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "CORRECTED_REPORT_PATH = (\n",
        "    f\"{OUTPUT_DIR}/experiment20_phase44_statistical_reproducibility_audit_corrected.json\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPECTED_CSV_SHA256 = (\n",
        "    \"d24a2a6d628eca608b8ab8e6c056fb50bc7b0e1c6c34e253dfae7c9354c9892f\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPECTED_ROWS = 2128\n",
        "EXPECTED_IDENTITIES = 38\n",
        "EXPECTED_CONDITIONS = 56\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPECTED_GROUP_COUNTS = {\n",
        "    \"near-frontal\": 646,\n",
        "    \"oblique\": 418,\n",
        "    \"large-angular\": 1064\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPECTED_HEMISPHERE_COUNTS = {\n",
        "    \"frontal\": 1710,\n",
        "    \"beyond-frontal\": 418\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "os.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "def sha256_file(path):\n",
        "    h = hashlib.sha256()\n",
        "    with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n",
        "        for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n",
        "            h.update(chunk)\n",
        "    return h.hexdigest()\n",
        "\n",
        "def json_safe(obj):\n",
        "    if isinstance(obj, np.generic):\n",
        "        return obj.item()\n",
        "    if isinstance(obj, np.ndarray):\n",
        "        return obj.tolist()\n",
        "    if isinstance(obj, (pd.Timestamp, datetime)):\n",
        "        return obj.isoformat()\n",
        "    if isinstance(obj, set):\n",
        "        return list(obj)\n",
        "    raise TypeError(f\"Unsupported JSON type: {type(obj).__name__}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "assert os.path.isfile(CSV_PATH), f\"Missing input CSV: {CSV_PATH}\"\n",
        "\n",
        "actual_csv_hash = sha256_file(CSV_PATH)\n",
        "csv_hash_match = actual_csv_hash == EXPECTED_CSV_SHA256\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n1. INPUT INTEGRITY\")\n",
        "print(\"CSV:\", CSV_PATH)\n",
        "print(\"Actual SHA256:\", actual_csv_hash)\n",
        "print(\"Expected SHA256:\", EXPECTED_CSV_SHA256)\n",
        "print(\"Hash match:\", csv_hash_match)\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 2. LOAD AND VALIDATE COHORT\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(CSV_PATH)\n",
        "\n",
        "required_columns = [\n",
        "    \"subject\",\n",
        "    \"illumination_group\",\n",
        "    \"hemisphere\",\n",
        "    \"euclidean_displacement\",\n",
        "    \"cosine_distance\",\n",
        "    \"evaluation_condition\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "missing_columns = [c for c in required_columns if c not in df.columns]\n",
        "assert not missing_columns, f\"Missing required columns: {missing_columns}\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Explicit mappings from the frozen CSV's original labels.\n",
        "GROUP_MAP = {\n",
        "    \"near_frontal\": \"near-frontal\",\n",
        "    \"oblique\": \"oblique\",\n",
        "    \"large_angular_deviation\": \"large-angular\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "HEMISPHERE_MAP = {\n",
        "    \"frontal_hemisphere\": \"frontal\",\n",
        "    \"beyond_frontal_hemisphere\": \"beyond-frontal\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "df[\"analysis_group\"] = df[\"illumination_group\"].map(GROUP_MAP)\n",
        "df[\"analysis_hemisphere\"] = df[\"hemisphere\"].map(HEMISPHERE_MAP)\n",
        "\n",
        "group_mapping_pass = (\n",
        "    df[\"analysis_group\"].notna().all()\n",
        "    and set(df[\"analysis_group\"].unique()) == set(GROUP_MAP.values())\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "hemisphere_mapping_pass = (\n",
        "    df[\"analysis_hemisphere\"].notna().all()\n",
        "    and set(df[\"analysis_hemisphere\"].unique()) == set(HEMISPHERE_MAP.values())\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "row_count = len(df)\n",
        "identity_count = df[\"subject\"].nunique()\n",
        "condition_count = df[\"evaluation_condition\"].nunique()\n",
        "\n",
        "group_counts = {\n",
        "    str(k): int(v)\n",
        "    for k, v in df[\"analysis_group\"].value_counts().items()\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "hemisphere_counts = {\n",
        "    str(k): int(v)\n",
        "    for k, v in df[\"analysis_hemisphere\"].value_counts().items()\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "metrics = [\"euclidean_displacement\", \"cosine_distance\"]\n",
        "groups = [\"near-frontal\", \"oblique\", \"large-angular\"]\n",
        "hemispheres = [\"frontal\", \"beyond-frontal\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "finite_metrics = all(\n",
        "    np.isfinite(df[m].to_numpy(dtype=float)).all()\n",
        "    for m in metrics\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n2. COHORT VALIDATION\")\n",
        "print(\"Rows:\", row_count)\n",
        "print(\"Identities:\", identity_count)\n",
        "print(\"Evaluation conditions:\", condition_count)\n",
        "print(\"Group mapping passed:\", group_mapping_pass)\n",
        "print(\"Hemisphere mapping passed:\", hemisphere_mapping_pass)\n",
        "print(\"Finite metric values:\", finite_metrics)\n",
        "print(\"Group counts:\", group_counts)\n",
        "print(\"Hemisphere counts:\", hemisphere_counts)\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 3. OBSERVATION-LEVEL DESCRIPTIVE STATISTICS\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "descriptive_results = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    grouped = df.groupby(\"analysis_group\")[metric].agg(\n",
        "        count=\"count\",\n",
        "        mean=\"mean\",\n",
        "        median=\"median\",\n",
        "        standard_deviation=\"std\"\n",
        "    ).reindex(groups)\n",
        "\n",
        "    descriptive_results[metric] = grouped.to_dict(orient=\"index\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n3. DESCRIPTIVE STATISTICS — {metric}\")\n",
        "    print(grouped.to_string())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Previously reported rounded values.\n",
        "expected_descriptive = {\n",
        "    \"euclidean_displacement\": {\n",
        "        \"near-frontal\": {\"mean\": 0.401897, \"median\": 0.391009},\n",
        "        \"oblique\": {\"mean\": 0.708976, \"median\": 0.711156},\n",
        "        \"large-angular\": {\"mean\": 1.118457, \"median\": 1.141883}\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"cosine_distance\": {\n",
        "        \"near-frontal\": {\"mean\": 0.086877, \"median\": 0.076444},\n",
        "        \"oblique\": {\"mean\": 0.262274, \"median\": 0.252871},\n",
        "        \"large-angular\": {\"mean\": 0.649095, \"median\": 0.651949}\n",
        "    }\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "descriptive_comparison = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    for group in groups:\n",
        "        for statistic in [\"mean\", \"median\"]:\n",
        "            reconstructed = descriptive_results[metric][group][statistic]\n",
        "            expected = expected_descriptive[metric][group][statistic]\n",
        "\n",
        "            key = f\"{metric}_{group}_{statistic}\"\n",
        "\n",
        "            descriptive_comparison[key] = {\n",
        "                \"reconstructed\": float(reconstructed),\n",
        "                \"previously_reported\": float(expected),\n",
        "                \"absolute_difference\": float(abs(reconstructed - expected)),\n",
        "                \"matches_rounded_report\": bool(\n",
        "                    abs(reconstructed - expected) <= 1e-6\n",
        "                )\n",
        "            }\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 4. IDENTITY-LEVEL AGGREGATION\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "identity_group = (\n",
        "    df.groupby([\"subject\", \"analysis_group\"])[metrics]\n",
        "    .mean()\n",
        "    .reset_index()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "identity_hemisphere = (\n",
        "    df.groupby([\"subject\", \"analysis_hemisphere\"])[metrics]\n",
        "    .mean()\n",
        "    .reset_index()\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "identity_group_matrices = {}\n",
        "identity_hemisphere_matrices = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    group_matrix = identity_group.pivot(\n",
        "        index=\"subject\",\n",
        "        columns=\"analysis_group\",\n",
        "        values=metric\n",
        "    ).reindex(columns=groups)\n",
        "\n",
        "    hemisphere_matrix = identity_hemisphere.pivot(\n",
        "        index=\"subject\",\n",
        "        columns=\"analysis_hemisphere\",\n",
        "        values=metric\n",
        "    ).reindex(columns=hemispheres)\n",
        "\n",
        "    identity_group_matrices[metric] = group_matrix\n",
        "    identity_hemisphere_matrices[metric] = hemisphere_matrix\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n4. IDENTITY-LEVEL GROUP MEANS — {metric}\")\n",
        "    print(group_matrix.describe().to_string())\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nIDENTITY-LEVEL HEMISPHERE MEANS — {metric}\")\n",
        "    print(hemisphere_matrix.describe().to_string())\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 5. FRIEDMAN TESTS AND KENDALL'S W\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "friedman_results = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    matrix = identity_group_matrices[metric]\n",
        "\n",
        "    assert matrix.shape == (EXPECTED_IDENTITIES, 3)\n",
        "    assert not matrix.isna().any().any()\n",
        "\n",
        "    statistic, p_value = friedmanchisquare(\n",
        "        matrix[\"near-frontal\"].to_numpy(),\n",
        "        matrix[\"oblique\"].to_numpy(),\n",
        "        matrix[\"large-angular\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    n = matrix.shape[0]\n",
        "    k = matrix.shape[1]\n",
        "    kendall_w = statistic / (n * (k - 1))\n",
        "\n",
        "    friedman_results[metric] = {\n",
        "        \"n_identities\": int(n),\n",
        "        \"groups\": groups,\n",
        "        \"chi_square\": float(statistic),\n",
        "        \"p_value\": float(p_value),\n",
        "        \"kendall_w\": float(kendall_w)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n5. FRIEDMAN TEST — {metric}\")\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(friedman_results[metric], indent=2))\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 6. SIX PAIRED WILCOXON TESTS AND COMBINED HOLM CORRECTION\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "comparisons = [\n",
        "    (\"near-frontal\", \"oblique\"),\n",
        "    (\"near-frontal\", \"large-angular\"),\n",
        "    (\"oblique\", \"large-angular\")\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "pairwise_raw = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    matrix = identity_group_matrices[metric]\n",
        "\n",
        "    for first, second in comparisons:\n",
        "        first_values = matrix[first].to_numpy()\n",
        "        second_values = matrix[second].to_numpy()\n",
        "\n",
        "        result = wilcoxon(\n",
        "            first_values,\n",
        "            second_values,\n",
        "            alternative=\"two-sided\",\n",
        "            zero_method=\"wilcox\",\n",
        "            method=\"auto\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        pairwise_raw.append({\n",
        "            \"metric\": metric,\n",
        "            \"comparison\": f\"{second} minus {first}\",\n",
        "            \"first_group\": first,\n",
        "            \"second_group\": second,\n",
        "            \"n_identities\": int(len(first_values)),\n",
        "            \"mean_paired_difference\": float(\n",
        "                np.mean(second_values - first_values)\n",
        "            ),\n",
        "            \"wilcoxon_statistic\": float(result.statistic),\n",
        "            \"raw_p_value\": float(result.pvalue)\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "raw_p_values = [x[\"raw_p_value\"] for x in pairwise_raw]\n",
        "\n",
        "holm_adjusted = multipletests(\n",
        "    raw_p_values,\n",
        "    alpha=0.05,\n",
        "    method=\"holm\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "pairwise_results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for i, item in enumerate(pairwise_raw):\n",
        "    item[\"combined_holm_p_value\"] = float(holm_adjusted[1][i])\n",
        "    item[\"reject_at_0_05_after_holm\"] = bool(holm_adjusted[0][i])\n",
        "    pairwise_results.append(item)\n",
        "\n",
        "pairwise_df = pd.DataFrame(pairwise_results)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n6. SIX PAIRED WILCOXON TESTS\")\n",
        "print(pairwise_df.to_string(index=False))\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 7. GROUP PAIRWISE PAIRED IDENTITY BOOTSTRAP\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "BOOTSTRAP_ITERATIONS = 20000\n",
        "GROUP_BOOTSTRAP_SEED = 2026274\n",
        "\n",
        "group_rng = np.random.default_rng(GROUP_BOOTSTRAP_SEED)\n",
        "group_bootstrap_results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    matrix = identity_group_matrices[metric]\n",
        "\n",
        "    for first, second in comparisons:\n",
        "        differences = (\n",
        "            matrix[second].to_numpy() - matrix[first].to_numpy()\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        n = len(differences)\n",
        "        bootstrap_means = np.empty(BOOTSTRAP_ITERATIONS)\n",
        "\n",
        "        for b in range(BOOTSTRAP_ITERATIONS):\n",
        "            indices = group_rng.integers(0, n, size=n)\n",
        "            bootstrap_means[b] = differences[indices].mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "        ci_lower, ci_upper = np.quantile(\n",
        "            bootstrap_means, [0.025, 0.975]\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        group_bootstrap_results.append({\n",
        "            \"metric\": metric,\n",
        "            \"comparison\": f\"{second} minus {first}\",\n",
        "            \"mean_difference\": float(differences.mean()),\n",
        "            \"ci_lower\": float(ci_lower),\n",
        "            \"ci_upper\": float(ci_upper),\n",
        "            \"iterations\": BOOTSTRAP_ITERATIONS,\n",
        "            \"seed\": GROUP_BOOTSTRAP_SEED,\n",
        "            \"resampling_unit\": \"identity\"\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "group_bootstrap_df = pd.DataFrame(group_bootstrap_results)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n7. GROUP PAIRWISE BOOTSTRAP CONFIDENCE INTERVALS\")\n",
        "print(group_bootstrap_df.to_string(index=False))\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 8. HEMISPHERE COMPARISONS AND BOOTSTRAP\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "HEMISPHERE_BOOTSTRAP_SEED = 2026275\n",
        "hemisphere_rng = np.random.default_rng(HEMISPHERE_BOOTSTRAP_SEED)\n",
        "\n",
        "hemisphere_raw_results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    matrix = identity_hemisphere_matrices[metric]\n",
        "\n",
        "    frontal = matrix[\"frontal\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "    beyond = matrix[\"beyond-frontal\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "\n",
        "    assert len(frontal) == EXPECTED_IDENTITIES\n",
        "    assert len(beyond) == EXPECTED_IDENTITIES\n",
        "\n",
        "    wilcoxon_result = wilcoxon(\n",
        "        beyond,\n",
        "        frontal,\n",
        "        alternative=\"two-sided\",\n",
        "        zero_method=\"wilcox\",\n",
        "        method=\"auto\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    differences = beyond - frontal\n",
        "    n = len(differences)\n",
        "\n",
        "    bootstrap_means = np.empty(BOOTSTRAP_ITERATIONS)\n",
        "\n",
        "    for b in range(BOOTSTRAP_ITERATIONS):\n",
        "        indices = hemisphere_rng.integers(0, n, size=n)\n",
        "        bootstrap_means[b] = differences[indices].mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "    ci_lower, ci_upper = np.quantile(\n",
        "        bootstrap_means, [0.025, 0.975]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    hemisphere_raw_results.append({\n",
        "        \"metric\": metric,\n",
        "        \"n_identities\": int(n),\n",
        "        \"frontal_mean\": float(frontal.mean()),\n",
        "        \"beyond_frontal_mean\": float(beyond.mean()),\n",
        "        \"beyond_minus_frontal_mean_difference\": float(differences.mean()),\n",
        "        \"wilcoxon_statistic\": float(wilcoxon_result.statistic),\n",
        "        \"raw_p_value\": float(wilcoxon_result.pvalue),\n",
        "        \"bootstrap\": {\n",
        "            \"mean_difference\": float(differences.mean()),\n",
        "            \"ci_lower\": float(ci_lower),\n",
        "            \"ci_upper\": float(ci_upper),\n",
        "            \"iterations\": BOOTSTRAP_ITERATIONS,\n",
        "            \"seed\": HEMISPHERE_BOOTSTRAP_SEED,\n",
        "            \"resampling_unit\": \"identity\",\n",
        "            \"method\": \"paired identity-level percentile bootstrap\"\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "hemisphere_holm = multipletests(\n",
        "    [x[\"raw_p_value\"] for x in hemisphere_raw_results],\n",
        "    alpha=0.05,\n",
        "    method=\"holm\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "hemisphere_results = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for i, item in enumerate(hemisphere_raw_results):\n",
        "    item[\"holm_p_value\"] = float(hemisphere_holm[1][i])\n",
        "    item[\"reject_after_holm\"] = bool(hemisphere_holm[0][i])\n",
        "    hemisphere_results[item[\"metric\"]] = item\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n8. HEMISPHERE COMPARISONS\")\n",
        "for metric, result in hemisphere_results.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n{metric}\")\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 9. REPORTED RESULT RECONCILIATION\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPECTED_FRIEDMAN = {\n",
        "    \"chi_square\": 76.0,\n",
        "    \"p_value\": 3.139132792048018e-17,\n",
        "    \"kendall_w\": 1.0\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPECTED_PAIRWISE_RAW_P = 7.275957614183426e-12\n",
        "EXPECTED_PAIRWISE_HOLM_P = 4.365574568508e-11\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPECTED_HEMISPHERE = {\n",
        "    \"euclidean_displacement\": {\n",
        "        \"frontal_mean\": 0.7062201499035649,\n",
        "        \"beyond_frontal_mean\": 1.2879898951855027,\n",
        "        \"difference\": 0.5817697452819375,\n",
        "        \"raw_p\": 7.275957614183426e-12,\n",
        "        \"holm_p\": 1.4551915228366852e-11,\n",
        "        \"ci_lower\": 0.5619855482971955,\n",
        "        \"ci_upper\": 0.6019542941366831\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"cosine_distance\": {\n",
        "        \"frontal_mean\": 0.29581613376952953,\n",
        "        \"beyond_frontal_mean\": 0.838623580414268,\n",
        "        \"difference\": 0.5428074466447383,\n",
        "        \"raw_p\": 7.275957614183426e-12,\n",
        "        \"holm_p\": 1.4551915228366852e-11,\n",
        "        \"ci_lower\": 0.5164192335,\n",
        "        \"ci_upper\": 0.5685162487\n",
        "    }\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "TOL = 1e-9\n",
        "CI_TOL = 1e-5\n",
        "\n",
        "reported_comparison = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    observed = friedman_results[metric]\n",
        "\n",
        "    for key in [\"chi_square\", \"p_value\", \"kendall_w\"]:\n",
        "        reported_comparison[f\"{metric}_friedman_{key}\"] = bool(\n",
        "            np.isclose(\n",
        "                observed[key],\n",
        "                EXPECTED_FRIEDMAN[key],\n",
        "                rtol=1e-7,\n",
        "                atol=TOL\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "for item in pairwise_results:\n",
        "    prefix = f\"{item['metric']}_{item['comparison']}\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    reported_comparison[f\"{prefix}_raw_p\"] = bool(\n",
        "        np.isclose(\n",
        "            item[\"raw_p_value\"],\n",
        "            EXPECTED_PAIRWISE_RAW_P,\n",
        "            rtol=1e-7,\n",
        "            atol=TOL\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    reported_comparison[f\"{prefix}_combined_holm\"] = bool(\n",
        "        np.isclose(\n",
        "            item[\"combined_holm_p_value\"],\n",
        "            EXPECTED_PAIRWISE_HOLM_P,\n",
        "            rtol=1e-7,\n",
        "            atol=TOL\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    observed = hemisphere_results[metric]\n",
        "    expected = EXPECTED_HEMISPHERE[metric]\n",
        "\n",
        "    fields = {\n",
        "        \"frontal_mean\": \"frontal_mean\",\n",
        "        \"beyond_frontal_mean\": \"beyond_frontal_mean\",\n",
        "        \"beyond_minus_frontal_mean_difference\": \"difference\",\n",
        "        \"raw_p_value\": \"raw_p\",\n",
        "        \"holm_p_value\": \"holm_p\"\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    for observed_key, expected_key in fields.items():\n",
        "        reported_comparison[\n",
        "            f\"{metric}_hemisphere_{observed_key}\"\n",
        "        ] = bool(\n",
        "            np.isclose(\n",
        "                observed[observed_key],\n",
        "                expected[expected_key],\n",
        "                rtol=1e-7,\n",
        "                atol=TOL\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "# Check the two hemisphere confidence intervals separately.\n",
        "# These are not allowed to silently determine whether the inferential\n",
        "# point estimates and significance tests reproduced.\n",
        "\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    observed_boot = hemisphere_results[metric][\"bootstrap\"]\n",
        "    expected = EXPECTED_HEMISPHERE[metric]\n",
        "\n",
        "    reported_comparison[\n",
        "        f\"{metric}_hemisphere_bootstrap_ci_lower\"\n",
        "    ] = bool(\n",
        "        np.isclose(\n",
        "            observed_boot[\"ci_lower\"],\n",
        "            expected[\"ci_lower\"],\n",
        "            rtol=0,\n",
        "            atol=CI_TOL\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    reported_comparison[\n",
        "        f\"{metric}_hemisphere_bootstrap_ci_upper\"\n",
        "    ] = bool(\n",
        "        np.isclose(\n",
        "            observed_boot[\"ci_upper\"],\n",
        "            expected[\"ci_upper\"],\n",
        "            rtol=0,\n",
        "            atol=CI_TOL\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "for key, result in descriptive_comparison.items():\n",
        "    reported_comparison[key] = result[\"matches_rounded_report\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 10. CHECKS AND STATUS\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "checks = {\n",
        "    \"input_csv_hash_valid\": bool(csv_hash_match),\n",
        "    \"evaluation_row_count_valid\": bool(row_count == EXPECTED_ROWS),\n",
        "    \"identity_count_valid\": bool(identity_count == EXPECTED_IDENTITIES),\n",
        "    \"evaluation_condition_count_valid\": bool(condition_count == EXPECTED_CONDITIONS),\n",
        "    \"all_geometry_labels_mapped\": bool(group_mapping_pass),\n",
        "    \"all_hemisphere_labels_mapped\": bool(hemisphere_mapping_pass),\n",
        "    \"geometry_group_counts_valid\": bool(group_counts == EXPECTED_GROUP_COUNTS),\n",
        "    \"hemisphere_counts_valid\": bool(hemisphere_counts == EXPECTED_HEMISPHERE_COUNTS),\n",
        "    \"all_metrics_finite\": bool(finite_metrics),\n",
        "    \"all_identity_group_matrices_complete\": bool(\n",
        "        all(\n",
        "            matrix.shape == (EXPECTED_IDENTITIES, 3)\n",
        "            and not matrix.isna().any().any()\n",
        "            for matrix in identity_group_matrices.values()\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"all_identity_hemisphere_matrices_complete\": bool(\n",
        "        all(\n",
        "            matrix.shape == (EXPECTED_IDENTITIES, 2)\n",
        "            and not matrix.isna().any().any()\n",
        "            for matrix in identity_hemisphere_matrices.values()\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"all_descriptive_results_match_rounded_report\": bool(\n",
        "        all(x[\"matches_rounded_report\"] for x in descriptive_comparison.values())\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"all_friedman_results_match\": bool(\n",
        "        all(\n",
        "            reported_comparison[f\"{m}_friedman_{k}\"]\n",
        "            for m in metrics\n",
        "            for k in [\"chi_square\", \"p_value\", \"kendall_w\"]\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"all_six_wilcoxon_raw_p_values_match\": bool(\n",
        "        all(\n",
        "            item[\"raw_p_value\"] is not None\n",
        "            and np.isclose(\n",
        "                item[\"raw_p_value\"],\n",
        "                EXPECTED_PAIRWISE_RAW_P,\n",
        "                rtol=1e-7,\n",
        "                atol=TOL\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            for item in pairwise_results\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"all_six_combined_holm_values_match\": bool(\n",
        "        all(\n",
        "            np.isclose(\n",
        "                item[\"combined_holm_p_value\"],\n",
        "                EXPECTED_PAIRWISE_HOLM_P,\n",
        "                rtol=1e-7,\n",
        "                atol=TOL\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            for item in pairwise_results\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    \"hemisphere_point_estimates_and_tests_match\": bool(\n",
        "        all(\n",
        "            reported_comparison.get(f\"{m}_hemisphere_{field}\", False)\n",
        "            for m in metrics\n",
        "            for field in [\n",
        "                \"frontal_mean\",\n",
        "                \"beyond_frontal_mean\",\n",
        "                \"beyond_minus_frontal_mean_difference\",\n",
        "                \"raw_p_value\",\n",
        "                \"holm_p_value\"\n",
        "            ]\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    )\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "core_checks = [\n",
        "    \"input_csv_hash_valid\",\n",
        "    \"evaluation_row_count_valid\",\n",
        "    \"identity_count_valid\",\n",
        "    \"evaluation_condition_count_valid\",\n",
        "    \"all_geometry_labels_mapped\",\n",
        "    \"all_hemisphere_labels_mapped\",\n",
        "    \"geometry_group_counts_valid\",\n",
        "    \"hemisphere_counts_valid\",\n",
        "    \"all_metrics_finite\",\n",
        "    \"all_identity_group_matrices_complete\",\n",
        "    \"all_identity_hemisphere_matrices_complete\",\n",
        "    \"all_descriptive_results_match_rounded_report\",\n",
        "    \"all_friedman_results_match\",\n",
        "    \"all_six_wilcoxon_raw_p_values_match\",\n",
        "    \"all_six_combined_holm_values_match\",\n",
        "    \"hemisphere_point_estimates_and_tests_match\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "core_pass = all(checks[x] for x in core_checks)\n",
        "\n",
        "cosine_ci_match = (\n",
        "    reported_comparison[\"cosine_distance_hemisphere_bootstrap_ci_lower\"]\n",
        "    and reported_comparison[\"cosine_distance_hemisphere_bootstrap_ci_upper\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "euclidean_ci_match = (\n",
        "    reported_comparison[\"euclidean_displacement_hemisphere_bootstrap_ci_lower\"]\n",
        "    and reported_comparison[\"euclidean_displacement_hemisphere_bootstrap_ci_upper\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "if core_pass and cosine_ci_match and euclidean_ci_match:\n",
        "    audit_status = \"PHASE_4_4_PASSED\"\n",
        "elif core_pass:\n",
        "    audit_status = (\n",
        "        \"PHASE_4_4_CORE_STATISTICS_REPRODUCED_\"\n",
        "        \"BOOTSTRAP_CI_PROVENANCE_DIFFERENCE_DOCUMENTED\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    audit_status = \"PHASE_4_4_REVIEW_REQUIRED\"\n",
        "\n",
        "failed_core_checks = [\n",
        "    name for name in core_checks if not checks[name]\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 11. REPORT\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "report = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": \"Experiment 20\",\n",
        "    \"phase\": \"4.4\",\n",
        "    \"audit_title\": \"Statistical Results Reproducibility Audit\",\n",
        "    \"created_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"audit_status\": audit_status,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"input\": {\n",
        "        \"csv_path\": CSV_PATH,\n",
        "        \"csv_sha256\": actual_csv_hash,\n",
        "        \"expected_csv_sha256\": EXPECTED_CSV_SHA256,\n",
        "        \"csv_hash_match\": bool(csv_hash_match)\n",
        "    },\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"environment\": {\n",
        "        \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n",
        "        \"numpy\": np.__version__,\n",
        "        \"pandas\": pd.__version__,\n",
        "        \"scipy\": scipy.__version__\n",
        "    },\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"cohort\": {\n",
        "        \"rows\": int(row_count),\n",
        "        \"identities\": int(identity_count),\n",
        "        \"evaluation_conditions\": int(condition_count),\n",
        "        \"group_counts\": group_counts,\n",
        "        \"hemisphere_counts\": hemisphere_counts\n",
        "    },\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"descriptive_results\": descriptive_results,\n",
        "    \"descriptive_comparison\": descriptive_comparison,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"identity_level_aggregation\": {\n",
        "        \"identity_group_records\": int(len(identity_group)),\n",
        "        \"identity_hemisphere_records\": int(len(identity_hemisphere)),\n",
        "        \"identities_per_group\": EXPECTED_IDENTITIES,\n",
        "        \"identities_per_hemisphere\": EXPECTED_IDENTITIES\n",
        "    },\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"friedman_results\": friedman_results,\n",
        "    \"pairwise_wilcoxon_results\": pairwise_results,\n",
        "    \"group_pairwise_bootstrap_results\": group_bootstrap_results,\n",
        "    \"hemisphere_comparisons\": hemisphere_results,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"reported_result_comparison\": reported_comparison,\n",
        "    \"checks\": checks,\n",
        "    \"failed_core_checks\": failed_core_checks,\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"bootstrap_reproducibility_note\": {\n",
        "        \"euclidean_hemisphere_ci_matches_previous_report\": bool(euclidean_ci_match),\n",
        "        \"cosine_hemisphere_ci_matches_previous_report\": bool(cosine_ci_match),\n",
        "        \"previous_cosine_ci\": [0.5164192335, 0.5685162487],\n",
        "        \"reconstructed_cosine_ci\": [\n",
        "            hemisphere_results[\"cosine_distance\"][\"bootstrap\"][\"ci_lower\"],\n",
        "            hemisphere_results[\"cosine_distance\"][\"bootstrap\"][\"ci_upper\"]\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"interpretation\": (\n",
        "            \"The cosine hemisphere point estimate, Wilcoxon test, and Holm-adjusted \"\n",
        "            \"p-value reproduce. The reconstructed bootstrap interval differs from \"\n",
        "            \"the previously reported interval. The original bootstrap implementation \"\n",
        "            \"has not been recovered, so this difference is documented rather than \"\n",
        "            \"treated as proof of an incorrect statistical result. The historical \"\n",
        "            \"interval must not be silently replaced.\"\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    },\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"scientific_scope\": {\n",
        "        \"resampling_unit\": \"identity\",\n",
        "        \"inferential_sample_size\": 38,\n",
        "        \"observation_level_descriptives_are_not_independent_identity_samples\": True,\n",
        "        \"euclidean_and_cosine_metrics_are_mathematically_related_for_l2_normalised_embeddings\": True,\n",
        "        \"kendall_w_one_is_rank_agreement_not_recognition_accuracy\": True,\n",
        "        \"hemisphere_analysis_is_exploratory\": True\n",
        "    },\n",
        "\n",
        "    \"preservation\": {\n",
        "        \"original_audit_overwritten\": False,\n",
        "        \"frozen_csv_modified\": False,\n",
        "        \"manuscript_modified\": False,\n",
        "        \"raw_embeddings_modified\": False\n",
        "    }\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 12. SAVE CORRECTED REPORT WITHOUT OVERWRITING ORIGINAL\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(CORRECTED_REPORT_PATH, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "    json.dump(\n",
        "        report,\n",
        "        f,\n",
        "        indent=2,\n",
        "        ensure_ascii=False,\n",
        "        default=json_safe,\n",
        "        allow_nan=False\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# Reload and verify JSON.\n",
        "with open(CORRECTED_REPORT_PATH, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "    verified_report = json.load(f)\n",
        "\n",
        "report_hash = sha256_file(CORRECTED_REPORT_PATH)\n",
        "final_csv_hash = sha256_file(CSV_PATH)\n",
        "\n",
        "assert isinstance(verified_report, dict)\n",
        "assert final_csv_hash == EXPECTED_CSV_SHA256\n",
        "\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# 13. FINAL OUTPUT\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 100)\n",
        "print(\"PHASE 4.4 — FINAL REPRODUCIBILITY AUDIT RESULTS\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 100)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nCHECKS\")\n",
        "for name, value in checks.items():\n",
        "    print((\"PASS\" if value else \"FAIL\") + \":\", name)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nFAILED CORE CHECKS\")\n",
        "print(failed_core_checks if failed_core_checks else \"None\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nFRIEDMAN RESULTS\")\n",
        "for metric, result in friedman_results.items():\n",
        "    print(metric, result)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nPAIRWISE HOLM RESULTS\")\n",
        "print(pairwise_df[\n",
        "    [\"metric\", \"comparison\", \"raw_p_value\", \"combined_holm_p_value\"]\n",
        "].to_string(index=False))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nHEMISPHERE BOOTSTRAP COMPARISON\")\n",
        "for metric in metrics:\n",
        "    current = hemisphere_results[metric][\"bootstrap\"]\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        metric,\n",
        "        \"reconstructed CI:\",\n",
        "        (current[\"ci_lower\"], current[\"ci_upper\"])\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nCOSINE CI MATCHES HISTORICAL REPORT:\", cosine_ci_match)\n",
        "print(\"EUCLIDEAN CI MATCHES HISTORICAL REPORT:\", euclidean_ci_match)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nFINAL AUDIT STATUS:\")\n",
        "print(audit_status)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nCORRECTED REPORT\")\n",
        "print(CORRECTED_REPORT_PATH)\n",
        "print(\"SHA256:\", report_hash)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nFROZEN CSV HASH RECHECK\")\n",
        "print(\"Hash unchanged:\", final_csv_hash == EXPECTED_CSV_SHA256)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nPRESERVATION\")\n",
        "print(\"Original audit overwritten: False\")\n",
        "print(\"Frozen CSV modified: False\")\n",
        "print(\"Manuscript modified: False\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 100)\n",
        "print(\"PHASE 4.4 REPLACEMENT AUDIT COMPLETED\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 100)\n"
