            "Line 159: The original resize operation did not explicitly specify interpolation or antialiasing arguments. The recorded torchvision version was 0.29.1+cpu, for which the applicable Resize defaults were bilinear interpolation and antialiasing enabled. These settings are therefore documented as library defaults rather than as manually specified experimental parameters.\n",
            "Line 169: The recorded software environment included Python 3.13.18, PyTorch 2.14.1+cpu, torchvision 0.29.1+cpu, and facenet-pytorch 2.6.0. The embedding-generation procedure used the pretrained InceptionResnetV1 model configured for VGGFace2 weights.\n",
            "Line 193: Across the 56 non-reference evaluation conditions, 17 conditions were classified as near-frontal, 11 as oblique, and 28 as large-angular. Across the 38 identities, these groups contained 646, 418, and 1,064 evaluation observations, respectively. All three groups therefore included observations from the same 38 identities, supporting the repeated-measures comparisons conducted at the identity level.\n",
