        "\n",
        "# Experiment 20 — Phase 4.6: Manuscript Integrity, Reporting Corrections and Final Verification\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "This phase completes the manuscript integrity and reporting review for Experiment 20. It addresses the outstanding issues identified during the Phase 4.6 audit and prepares a corrected manuscript copy without modifying previously frozen evidence or manuscript versions.\n",
        "\n",
        "The purpose is to ensure that the amended manuscript has functioning figure references, explicitly reports the retained methodological qualification concerning independence between identities, and preserves all previously verified numerical and statistical results.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Scope of Work\n",
        "\n",
        "The work in this phase is limited to the following corrections and verification activities.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. Figure Reference Corrections\n",
        "\n",
        "The four figure files have been located in the canonical directory:\n",
        "\n",
        "`/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results/step_3_3/step_3330/figures/`\n",
        "\n",
        "The current amended manuscript contains relative image references beginning with:\n",
        "\n",
        "`figures/`\n",
        "\n",
        "These references do not resolve correctly from the manuscript's current directory.\n",
        "\n",
        "Update the four figure references to use:\n",
        "\n",
        "`../step_3_3/step_3330/figures/`\n",
        "\n",
        "Preserve the original figure filenames and image content. Verify that all four corrected paths resolve to existing files.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Independence Between Identities Limitation\n",
        "\n",
        "The Phase 4.5 statistical methodology audit retained the qualification that statistical independence between the 38 identities cannot be independently established from the available dataset and acquisition records.\n",
        "\n",
        "This qualification must be explicitly included in Section 4.6 — Limitations.\n",
        "\n",
        "Insert the following paragraph as a separate limitation:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Independence between identities.** Identity served as the unit of inference for the repeated-measures analyses. However, the available dataset and acquisition records do not independently establish statistical independence between identities. The inferential results should therefore be interpreted with this limitation in mind.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not imply that the identities are necessarily dependent. The limitation concerns the absence of independent evidence establishing their statistical independence.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. Statistical Results Preservation\n",
        "\n",
        "The six pairwise comparisons in Table 2 have been reconciled against the Phase 4.4 statistical reproducibility report.\n",
        "\n",
        "All six comparisons match the verified evidence for:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Metric and comparison direction.\n",
        "- Mean paired differences.\n",
        "- 95% identity-level bootstrap confidence intervals.\n",
        "- Raw Wilcoxon signed-rank p-values.\n",
        "- Six-test Holm-adjusted p-values.\n",
        "\n",
        "The reported values are correct to the displayed precision.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not modify Table 2, its numerical values, statistical tests, confidence intervals, or p-values.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not substitute the sign-test results for the Wilcoxon results. They represent separate statistical analyses.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Manuscript Preservation\n",
        "\n",
        "The current Phase 4.5 final manuscript must remain unchanged:\n",
        "\n",
        "`experiment20_integrated_manuscript_v2_phase45_final.md`\n",
        "\n",
        "The original frozen manuscript V2 must also remain unchanged.\n",
        "\n",
        "Create a new corrected manuscript copy named:\n",
        "\n",
        "`experiment20_integrated_manuscript_v2_phase46_final.md`\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not overwrite either existing manuscript.\n",
        "\n",
        "Preserve all other manuscript sections, tables, figures, statistical results, references, and scientific qualifications unless a change is explicitly specified in this phase.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Verification Requirements\n",
        "\n",
        "The final verification must establish the following:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. The original Phase 4.5 manuscript remains unchanged.\n",
        "2. The new Phase 4.6 manuscript exists.\n",
        "3. All four figure references use the corrected relative paths.\n",
        "4. All four referenced figure files exist.\n",
        "5. Section 4.6 contains the complete independence limitation paragraph.\n",
        "6. Table 1 remains unchanged.\n",
        "7. Table 2 remains unchanged.\n",
        "8. All six Table 2 comparisons retain their verified numerical values.\n",
        "9. No previously documented methodological qualifications have been removed.\n",
        "10. The corrected manuscript has a recorded SHA256 hash.\n",
        "11. A separate Phase 4.6 manuscript correction and verification record is saved.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Scientific and Methodological Constraints\n",
        "\n",
        "The manuscript must continue to distinguish embedding displacement from face-recognition performance.\n",
        "\n",
        "The study remains a descriptive, identity-level empirical investigation of reference-relative face embedding displacement across illumination geometry conditions.\n",
        "\n",
        "The following limitations must remain explicit:\n",
        "\n",
        "- The dataset contains different captures under different illumination conditions, not controlled transformations of identical source images.\n",
        "- One common reference condition is used per identity.\n",
        "- The analysis uses one pretrained FaceNet/InceptionResnetV1 architecture.\n",
        "- The study does not establish face-recognition identification or verification accuracy.\n",
        "- No false acceptance rate or false rejection rate evaluation was conducted.\n",
        "- The study does not establish fairness or demographic performance.\n",
        "- The hemisphere comparison remains exploratory and is confounded with angular geometry.\n",
        "- Euclidean displacement and cosine distance are related measures, not independent evidence streams.\n",
        "- Statistical independence between identities cannot be independently established from the available evidence.\n",
        "- No operational real-time drift detection system was implemented or validated.\n",
        "\n",
        "No causal illumination claims, recognition-failure claims, fairness claims, or deployment-readiness claims may be introduced.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Execution Rules\n",
        "\n",
        "This phase must preserve the audit trail.\n",
        "\n",
        "- Do not overwrite frozen manuscripts.\n",
        "- Do not modify the frozen dataset, evaluation CSV, embedding archive, or statistical audit reports.\n",
        "- Do not recalculate or replace verified statistical results.\n",
        "- Do not silently change manuscript wording outside the approved corrections.\n",
        "- Save the corrected manuscript as a separate version.\n",
        "- Record all changes and verification results separately.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Expected Outcome\n",
        "\n",
        "A new manuscript version:\n",
        "\n",
        "`experiment20_integrated_manuscript_v2_phase46_final.md`\n",
        "\n",
        "A separate correction and verification record:\n",
        "\n",
        "`experiment20_phase46_manuscript_correction_verification.json`\n",
        "\n",
        "The phase may be marked complete only after all required verification checks pass and the preservation checks confirm that the earlier frozen files remain unchanged.\n"
      ],
