            "\n",
            "3. TABLE CONTEXT — LINES 245 TO 300\n",
            "245: \n",
            "246: ## 3.2 Overall reference-relative embedding displacement\n",
            "247: \n",
            "248: Across 2,128 evaluation observations, mean Euclidean displacement was 0.820496 (SD = 0.362940; median = 0.817311), with values ranging from 0.151681 to 1.522514. Mean cosine distance was 0.402439 (SD = 0.309758; median = 0.333999), ranging from 0.011504 to 1.159025.\n",
            "249: \n",
            "250: \n",
            "251: ## 3.3 Displacement across illumination geometry groups\n",
            "252: \n",
            "253: Both distance measures increased progressively across the illumination geometry groups. Mean Euclidean displacement increased from 0.401897 under near-frontal conditions to 0.708976 under oblique conditions and 1.118457 under large-angular deviation conditions. Mean cosine distance followed the same ordering, increasing from 0.086877 to 0.262274 and 0.649095, respectively. The identity-level patterns are shown in Figures 1 and 2.\n",
            "254: \n",
            "255: \n",
            "256: ### Table 1. Descriptive statistics by illumination geometry group\n",
            "257: \n",
            "258: | Illumination group | Observations | Identities | Conditions | Euclidean mean | Euclidean SD | Cosine mean | Cosine SD |\n",
            "259: |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n",
            "260: | Near-frontal | 646 | 38 | 17 | 0.4019 | 0.1107 | 0.0869 | 0.0479 |\n",
            "261: | Oblique | 418 | 38 | 11 | 0.7090 | 0.1482 | 0.2623 | 0.1062 |\n",
            "262: | Large-angular deviation | 1064 | 38 | 28 | 1.1185 | 0.2175 | 0.6491 | 0.2388 |\n",
            "263: \n",
            "264: \n",
            "265: ![Identity-level Euclidean displacement across near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular-deviation illumination groups.](figures/experiment20_figure1_euclidean_illumination_groups.png)\n",
            "266: \n",
            "267: *Figure 1. Identity-level Euclidean displacement across illumination geometry groups. Thin lines represent the mean displacement for each of the 38 identities within each group; the thick olive line represents the mean across identities.*\n",
            "268: \n",
            "269: ![Identity-level cosine distance across near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular-deviation illumination groups.](figures/experiment20_figure2_cosine_illumination_groups.png)\n",
            "270: \n",
            "271: *Figure 2. Identity-level cosine distance across illumination geometry groups. Thin lines represent the mean distance for each of the 38 identities within each group; the thick olive line represents the mean across identities.*\n",
            "272: \n",
            "273: \n",
            "274: ## 3.4 Identity-level repeated-measures analysis\n",
            "275: \n",
            "276: Friedman repeated-measures tests identified differences among the three illumination geometry groups for Euclidean displacement (χ²(2) = 76.0, p = 3.139e-17, Kendall's W = 1.0) and cosine distance (χ²(2) = 76.0, p = 3.139e-17, Kendall's W = 1.0). Each analysis included 38 identities measured across three groups.\n",
            "277: \n",
            "278: Pairwise identity-level comparisons used Wilcoxon signed-rank tests. Confidence intervals for mean paired differences were estimated using 20,000 identity-level bootstrap iterations with random seed 2026274. Holm correction was applied across one combined family of six comparisons covering both distance measures. All six comparisons remained statistically significant.\n",
            "279: \n",
            "280: In the sign-test sensitivity analysis, all 38 identities showed positive paired differences for each of the six primary comparisons, with no negative differences or ties. The exact two-sided sign-test p-value was 7.276 × 10⁻¹² for each comparison. Following Holm correction across the six-test family, all adjusted p-values were 4.366 × 10⁻¹¹. This consistent direction of differences provides sensitivity evidence supporting the ordering observed in the primary Wilcoxon analysis.\n",
            "281: \n",
            "282: \n",
            "283: ### Table 2. Identity-level pairwise comparisons\n",
            "284: \n",
            "285: | Metric | Comparison | Mean paired difference | 95% bootstrap CI | Raw p | Six-test Holm p |\n",
            "286: |---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n",
            "287: | Euclidean displacement | Near-frontal vs Oblique | 0.307079 | [0.285544, 0.328413] | 7.276e-12 | 4.366e-11 |\n",
            "288: | Euclidean displacement | Near-frontal vs Large-angular deviation | 0.716560 | [0.691110, 0.741689] | 7.276e-12 | 4.366e-11 |\n",
            "289: | Euclidean displacement | Oblique vs Large-angular deviation | 0.409481 | [0.387346, 0.431761] | 7.276e-12 | 4.366e-11 |\n",
            "290: | Cosine distance | Near-frontal vs Oblique | 0.175397 | [0.159082, 0.191703] | 7.276e-12 | 4.366e-11 |\n",
            "291: | Cosine distance | Near-frontal vs Large-angular deviation | 0.562219 | [0.536391, 0.588301] | 7.276e-12 | 4.366e-11 |\n",
            "292: | Cosine distance | Oblique vs Large-angular deviation | 0.386821 | [0.364906, 0.408321] | 7.276e-12 | 4.366e-11 |\n",
            "293: \n",
            "294: \n",
            "295: ## 3.5 Exploratory frontal and beyond-frontal comparison\n",
            "296: \n",
            "297: In the exploratory hemisphere analysis, mean Euclidean displacement was 0.706220 under frontal conditions and 1.287990 under beyond-frontal conditions. The mean paired difference (beyond-frontal minus frontal) was 0.581770 (95% bootstrap CI: [0.561986, 0.601954]; Holm-adjusted p = 1.455e-11). (Figure 3).\n",
            "298: \n",
            "299: For cosine distance, the corresponding means were 0.295816 and 0.838624. The mean paired difference was 0.542807 (95% bootstrap CI: [0.516419, 0.568516]; Holm-adjusted p = 1.455e-11). (Figure 4).\n",
            "300: \n",
            "\n",
            "4. FIGURE CAPTION AND REFERENCE CONTEXT\n",
            "Line 265: ![Identity-level Euclidean displacement across near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular-deviation illumination groups.](figures/experiment20_figure1_euclidean_illumination_groups.png)\n",
            "Line 267: *Figure 1. Identity-level Euclidean displacement across illumination geometry groups. Thin lines represent the mean displacement for each of the 38 identities within each group; the thick olive line represents the mean across identities.*\n",
