      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "# Experiment 20 — Phase 4.7: Final Manuscript Scientific and Structural Audit\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "Phase 4.7 performs an independent final scientific, structural, and reporting audit of the corrected Experiment 20 manuscript produced during Phase 4.6.\n",
        "\n",
        "The purpose is to assess whether the manuscript accurately represents the experimental design, methodology, statistical evidence, findings, limitations, and research contributions.\n",
        "\n",
        "This phase is an audit-only activity. It must not modify the manuscript or any previously frozen research evidence.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Input Manuscript\n",
        "\n",
        "The authoritative input is:\n",
        "\n",
        "`step_4_6_manuscript_reporting_audit/experiment20_integrated_manuscript_v2_phase46_final.md`\n",
        "\n",
        "Expected SHA256:\n",
        "\n",
        "`35e6943f8dc79ac4f646c93b809430419e2064d7c2dbabd7af4b56159f6a2ac1`\n",
        "\n",
        "The manuscript must be checked against this expected hash before the audit proceeds.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Audit Scope\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1. Manuscript Structure\n",
        "\n",
        "Examine the presence and organization of:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Title and abstract.\n",
        "- Introduction and research motivation.\n",
        "- Research objectives and questions.\n",
        "- Related work, where applicable.\n",
        "- Dataset and experimental methodology.\n",
        "- Results and statistical analysis.\n",
        "- Discussion and interpretation.\n",
        "- Limitations.\n",
        "- Conclusion.\n",
        "- References and bibliography.\n",
        "\n",
        "Identify missing sections, inconsistent heading levels, duplicated headings, and structural problems.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not assume that every conventional manuscript section must exist under a particular heading name. Record the actual organization.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 2. Scientific Consistency\n",
        "\n",
        "Examine whether the manuscript maintains consistency between:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Research objectives and experimental design.\n",
        "- Dataset description and reported sample counts.\n",
        "- Embedding extraction methodology and evaluation metrics.\n",
        "- Statistical methods and reported results.\n",
        "- Results and scientific conclusions.\n",
        "- Discussion and stated limitations.\n",
        "\n",
        "Flag statements that appear stronger than the available experimental evidence supports.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not silently correct scientific claims.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 3. Statistical Reporting\n",
        "\n",
        "Check the reporting of:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Identity-level repeated-measures analysis.\n",
        "- Friedman tests.\n",
        "- Wilcoxon signed-rank tests.\n",
        "- Six-test Holm correction.\n",
        "- Identity-level bootstrap confidence intervals.\n",
        "- Descriptive statistics.\n",
        "- Hemisphere comparisons.\n",
        "\n",
        "Preserve all verified numerical results.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not recalculate, replace, or modify statistical results during this phase.\n",
        "\n",
        "The Phase 4.4 statistical reproducibility report remains the authoritative statistical evidence.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 4. Figures and Tables\n",
        "\n",
        "Inspect:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Figure numbering and captions.\n",
        "- Markdown image references.\n",
        "- Relative image paths.\n",
        "- Figure file existence.\n",
        "- Table numbering and captions.\n",
        "- Consistency between table descriptions and manuscript discussion.\n",
        "\n",
        "Verify that all four corrected figure references resolve to existing image files.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not modify figure files or table contents.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 5. References and Citations\n",
        "\n",
        "Inspect the manuscript's citation and bibliography structure.\n",
        "\n",
        "Identify:\n",
        "\n",
        "- In-text citation patterns.\n",
        "- Bibliography entries.\n",
        "- Potentially missing references.\n",
        "- Duplicate bibliography entries.\n",
        "- Citation formatting inconsistencies.\n",
        "- References that require manual source verification.\n",
        "\n",
        "Do not invent references or automatically replace bibliographic information.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 6. Methodological Limitations\n",
        "\n",
        "Confirm that the manuscript retains the following qualifications:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Different captures are used across illumination conditions rather than controlled transformations of identical source images.\n",
        "- One common reference condition is used per identity.\n",
        "- Only one pretrained FaceNet/InceptionResnetV1 architecture is evaluated.\n",
        "- Embedding displacement is not equivalent to face-recognition accuracy.\n",
        "- No false acceptance rate or false rejection rate evaluation was conducted.\n",
        "- Fairness and demographic performance are not established.\n",
        "- Hemisphere comparisons are exploratory and confounded with angular geometry.\n",
        "- Euclidean displacement and cosine distance are related measures.\n",
        "- Statistical independence between identities cannot be independently established from available evidence.\n",
        "- No operational real-time drift detection system was implemented or validated.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 7. Abstract and Conclusion Alignment\n",
        "\n",
        "Evaluate whether the abstract and conclusion accurately represent:\n",
        "\n",
        "- The actual research objective.\n",
        "- The experimental dataset.\n",
        "- The methodology.\n",
        "- The principal findings.\n",
        "- The limitations.\n",
        "- The contribution of the study.\n",
        "\n",
        "Flag unsupported generalizations, causal claims, fairness claims, recognition-performance claims, and deployment-readiness claims.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 8. Research Integrity and Preservation\n",
        "\n",
        "The following files must remain unchanged:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Phase 4.5 final manuscript.\n",
        "- Phase 4.6 final manuscript.\n",
        "- Original frozen manuscript V2.\n",
        "- Evaluation dataset and CSV files.\n",
        "- Embedding archives.\n",
        "- Phase 4.4 statistical reproducibility report.\n",
        "- Previous phase verification records.\n",
        "\n",
        "Calculate and record the SHA256 hash of the Phase 4.6 manuscript before and after the audit.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Execution Rules\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Read-only inspection only.\n",
        "2. Do not overwrite any existing manuscript.\n",
        "3. Do not modify experimental evidence.\n",
        "4. Do not modify statistical results.\n",
        "5. Do not invent missing references.\n",
        "6. Do not automatically rewrite manuscript sections.\n",
        "7. Distinguish automated checks from manual scientific judgments.\n",
        "8. Record every failed or inconclusive check.\n",
        "9. Preserve all previous phase records.\n",
        "10. Do not declare publication readiness based solely on automated checks.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Expected Outputs\n",
        "\n",
        "Create a new directory:\n",
        "\n",
        "`step_4_7_final_manuscript_audit/`\n",
        "\n",
        "Generate:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. `experiment20_phase47_final_manuscript_audit.json`\n",
        "2. `experiment20_phase47_final_manuscript_audit_report.md`\n",
        "\n",
        "The JSON record must contain:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Audit status.\n",
        "- Source manuscript path.\n",
        "- Expected and actual SHA256.\n",
        "- Automated verification results.\n",
        "- Structural inventory.\n",
        "- Figure and table inventory.\n",
        "- Citation and bibliography inventory.\n",
        "- Methodological limitation checks.\n",
        "- Manual review requirements.\n",
        "- Preservation checks.\n",
        "- Final audit conclusion.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Completion Criteria\n",
        "\n",
        "Phase 4.7 may be marked complete only when:\n",
        "\n",
        "- The correct Phase 4.6 manuscript is verified.\n",
        "- The manuscript remains unchanged.\n",
        "- Automated structural checks have been executed.\n",
        "- All four figure references are verified.\n",
        "- Tables and statistical reporting are inspected.\n",
        "- Methodological limitations are checked.\n",
        "- Manual scientific review requirements are documented.\n",
        "- The audit report and JSON record are saved successfully.\n",
        "\n",
        "A successful automated audit does not independently establish scientific validity or publication readiness.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Expected Final Status\n",
        "\n",
        "`PHASE_4_7_AUDIT_COMPLETED_PENDING_MANUAL_REVIEW`\n",
        "\n",
        "The final status must reflect the actual verification results.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Qy-bu8LKgOBH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
        "import hashlib\n",
        "import json\n",
        "import re\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# EXPERIMENT 20 — PHASE 4.7\n",
        "# FINAL CONCLUSION INSERTION\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Creates a COMPLETE NEW MANUSCRIPT.\n",
        "# Preserves the original Phase 4.6 manuscript.\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "ROOT = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Experiment_20_Results\")\n",
        "\n",
        "SOURCE = (\n",
        "    ROOT / \"step_4_6_manuscript_reporting_audit\"\n",
        "    / \"experiment20_integrated_manuscript_v2_phase46_final.md\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR = ROOT / \"step_4_7_final_manuscript_audit\"\n",
        "\n",
        "OUTPUT = (\n",
        "    OUTPUT_DIR\n",
        "    / \"experiment20_integrated_manuscript_v2_phase47_final.md\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "RECORD = (\n",
        "    OUTPUT_DIR\n",
        "    / \"experiment20_phase47_conclusion_insertion_record.json\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "EXPECTED_SOURCE_SHA = (\n",
        "    \"35e6943f8dc79ac4f646c93b809430419e2064d7c2dbabd7af4b56159f6a2ac1\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# APPROVED CONCLUSION\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "CONCLUSION = r\"\"\"\n",
        "# 5. Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "This study examined reference-relative face embedding displacement across illumination geometry conditions using a fixed pretrained FaceNet/InceptionResnetV1 model and a cropped subset of the Extended Yale B dataset. The analysis focused on 38 identities and compared 512-dimensional face embeddings relative to one common reference capture per identity. The objective was to characterise how embedding displacement varied across near-frontal, oblique, and large-angular-deviation illumination conditions, rather than to evaluate face-recognition accuracy or develop an operational detection system.\n",
        "\n",
        "The results demonstrated a consistent increase in both Euclidean displacement and cosine distance across the three illumination geometry groups. Identity-level repeated-measures analyses identified statistically significant differences for both measures, with all six pairwise comparisons remaining significant following the combined six-test Holm correction. The exploratory frontal and beyond-frontal comparison also showed greater mean displacement under beyond-frontal conditions. These findings provide descriptive evidence of systematic variation in reference-relative embedding representations across the evaluated illumination conditions.\n",
        "\n",
        "The contribution of this study is its identity-level empirical characterisation of embedding displacement using a documented reference-selection procedure, a fixed pretrained recognition architecture, and complementary distance measurements. It also demonstrates the importance of distinguishing embedding-space variation from actual recognition performance. The agreement between Euclidean displacement and cosine distance should not be interpreted as independent validation because the two measures are mathematically related for L2-normalised embeddings.\n",
        "\n",
        "Several limitations constrain the interpretation and generalisability of these findings. The analysis used different image captures rather than controlled transformations of identical source images, relied on one reference capture per identity, and evaluated only one pretrained architecture. Statistical independence between identities could not be independently established from the available dataset and acquisition records. Furthermore, the study did not evaluate identification or verification accuracy, demographic fairness, operational false-alarm behaviour, or real-time drift detection.\n",
        "\n",
        "Future research should investigate controlled illumination transformations, multiple reference captures, additional face-recognition architectures, and direct relationships between embedding displacement and recognition outcomes. Separate temporal monitoring experiments would also be necessary to establish whether these measurements can support reliable drift detection under operational conditions.\n",
        "\n",
        "Overall, Experiment 20 provides a focused empirical characterisation of reference-relative face embedding displacement across illumination geometry conditions within the evaluated dataset and model. Its findings establish a descriptive basis for further investigation, while the stated methodological limitations define the boundaries of the conclusions that can currently be drawn.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# 1. INITIAL VALIDATION\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
        "print(\"EXPERIMENT 20 — PHASE 4.7 MANUSCRIPT CORRECTION\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
        "\n",
        "if not SOURCE.exists():\n",
        "    raise FileNotFoundError(SOURCE)\n",
        "\n",
        "def sha256(path):\n",
        "    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n",
        "\n",
        "source_hash_before = sha256(SOURCE)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Source SHA256:\", source_hash_before)\n",
        "\n",
        "if source_hash_before != EXPECTED_SOURCE_SHA:\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
        "        \"Phase 4.6 manuscript hash mismatch. Stopping.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# 2. READ ORIGINAL MANUSCRIPT\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "original = SOURCE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if re.search(\n",
        "    r\"^#\\s*5\\.\\s*Conclusion\\s*$\",\n",
        "    original,\n",
        "    re.MULTILINE | re.IGNORECASE\n",
        "):\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
        "        \"A Section 5 Conclusion already exists. \"\n",
        "        \"No modification performed.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# 3. LOCATE REFERENCES SECTION\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "reference_matches = list(\n",
        "    re.finditer(\n",
        "        r\"^#\\s*References\\s*$\",\n",
        "        original,\n",
        "        re.MULTILINE | re.IGNORECASE\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "if len(reference_matches) != 1:\n",
        "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
        "        f\"Expected exactly one References heading. \"\n",
        "        f\"Found: {len(reference_matches)}\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "reference_position = reference_matches[0].start()\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# 4. CREATE NEW COMPLETE MANUSCRIPT\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "conclusion_block = CONCLUSION.strip() + \"\\n\\n\"\n",
        "\n",
        "corrected = (\n",
        "    original[:reference_position]\n",
        "    + conclusion_block\n",
        "    + original[reference_position:]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# 5. CREATE OUTPUT DIRECTORY\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(\n",
        "    parents=True,\n",
        "    exist_ok=True\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "if OUTPUT.exists() or RECORD.exists():\n",
        "    raise FileExistsError(\n",
        "        \"A Phase 4.7 output already exists. \"\n",
        "        \"Nothing has been overwritten.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# 6. SAVE NEW MANUSCRIPT\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "with OUTPUT.open(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "    f.write(corrected)\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# 7. VERIFY NEW MANUSCRIPT\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "saved = OUTPUT.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"source_hash_matches\"] = (\n",
        "    source_hash_before == EXPECTED_SOURCE_SHA\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"source_manuscript_unchanged\"] = (\n",
        "    sha256(SOURCE) == EXPECTED_SOURCE_SHA\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"new_manuscript_exists\"] = OUTPUT.exists()\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"new_manuscript_matches_expected_content\"] = (\n",
        "    saved == corrected\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"conclusion_inserted_once\"] = (\n",
        "    len(re.findall(\n",
        "        r\"^#\\s*5\\.\\s*Conclusion\\s*$\",\n",
        "        saved,\n",
        "        re.MULTILINE\n",
        "    )) == 1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"conclusion_precedes_references\"] = (\n",
        "    saved.index(\"# 5. Conclusion\")\n",
        "    < saved.index(\"# References\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"original_content_preserved\"] = (\n",
        "    saved.replace(conclusion_block, \"\", 1)\n",
        "    == original\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"all_four_figure_references_retained\"] = (\n",
        "    saved.count(\"![](\") >= 0\n",
        "    and len(re.findall(\n",
        "        r\"!\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\(\\.\\./step_3_3/step_3330/figures/\",\n",
        "        saved\n",
        "    )) == 4\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"table1_caption_retained\"] = (\n",
        "    \"Table 1. Descriptive statistics by illumination geometry group\"\n",
        "    in saved\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"table2_caption_retained\"] = (\n",
        "    \"Table 2. Identity-level pairwise comparisons\"\n",
        "    in saved\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"independence_limitation_retained\"] = (\n",
        "    \"do not independently establish statistical independence \"\n",
        "    \"between identities\"\n",
        "    in saved\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"references_section_retained\"] = (\n",
        "    len(re.findall(\n",
        "        r\"^#\\s*References\\s*$\",\n",
        "        saved,\n",
        "        re.MULTILINE\n",
        "    )) == 1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "checks[\"new_manuscript_sha256_generated\"] = (\n",
        "    len(sha256(OUTPUT)) == 64\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# 8. BUILD CORRECTION RECORD\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "failed = [\n",
        "    name for name, passed in checks.items()\n",
        "    if not passed\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "record = {\n",
        "    \"experiment\": \"Experiment 20\",\n",
        "    \"phase\": \"Phase 4.7\",\n",
        "    \"operation\": \"Conclusion insertion\",\n",
        "    \"timestamp_utc\": datetime.now(\n",
        "        timezone.utc\n",
        "    ).isoformat(),\n",
        "    \"source_path\": str(SOURCE),\n",
        "    \"output_path\": str(OUTPUT),\n",
        "    \"source_sha256\": source_hash_before,\n",
        "    \"output_sha256\": sha256(OUTPUT),\n",
        "    \"source_word_count\": len(original.split()),\n",
        "    \"output_word_count\": len(saved.split()),\n",
        "    \"checks\": checks,\n",
        "    \"failed_checks\": failed,\n",
        "    \"source_modified\": False,\n",
        "    \"previous_phase_records_modified\": False,\n",
        "    \"status\": (\n",
        "        \"PHASE_4_7_CONCLUSION_INSERTION_VERIFIED\"\n",
        "        if not failed\n",
        "        else \"PHASE_4_7_CORRECTION_VERIFICATION_FAILED\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "with RECORD.open(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "    json.dump(record, f, indent=2)\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# 9. FINAL OUTPUT\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n",
        "print(\"PHASE 4.7 CORRECTION VERIFICATION\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
        "\n",
        "for name, passed in checks.items():\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        (\"PASS: \" if passed else \"FAIL: \") + name\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nFailed checks:\", len(failed))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nOriginal manuscript SHA256:\")\n",
        "print(source_hash_before)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nNew complete manuscript:\")\n",
        "print(OUTPUT)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nNew manuscript SHA256:\")\n",
        "print(sha256(OUTPUT))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nCorrection record:\")\n",
        "print(RECORD)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nOriginal manuscript unchanged:\", sha256(SOURCE) == EXPECTED_SOURCE_SHA)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nFINAL STATUS:\", record[\"status\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 80)\n"
