        "\n",
        "# EXPERIMENT 20 — PHASE 5.1\n",
        "# FINAL MANUSCRIPT CONSISTENCY REVIEW\n",
        "## Corrected Consolidated Audit — Version 2\n",
        "\n",
        "### Research project title\n",
        "\n",
        "Experiment 20: Paired Identity-Level Evaluation of Within-Identity Embedding Drift Detection Under Multiple Controlled Biometric Acquisition Changes\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "Perform a consolidated final consistency audit of the Phase 4.7 manuscript against the available frozen experimental evidence and Phase 4 audit records.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Corrections incorporated\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Distinguish the overall experiment title from the narrower manuscript publication title.\n",
        "2. Evaluate dataset and acquisition limitations using the actual manuscript sections.\n",
        "3. Compare Phase 4.6 and Phase 4.7 after excluding the newly inserted conclusion from an in-memory copy.\n",
        "4. Reconcile the historical Phase 4.7 conclusion-identification failure with the subsequent verified insertion record.\n",
        "5. Locate and inspect the actual corrected Phase 4.2, Phase 4.3 and Phase 4.4 audit records.\n",
        "6. Preserve all original manuscripts, statistical evidence, datasets and audit records.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Required checks\n",
        "\n",
        "- Manuscript integrity and SHA256.\n",
        "- Title and abstract consistency.\n",
        "- Methodology and experimental scope.\n",
        "- Statistical methods and numerical reporting.\n",
        "- Table and figure integrity.\n",
        "- Dataset and methodological limitations.\n",
        "- Discussion and conclusion structure.\n",
        "- Reference-section presence.\n",
        "- Phase 4 evidence reconciliation.\n",
        "- Cross-version manuscript preservation.\n",
        "- Historical audit-record reconciliation.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Preservation requirements\n",
        "\n",
        "- Read-only inspection of existing research artifacts.\n",
        "- No overwriting of frozen manuscripts.\n",
        "- No modification of existing statistical results.\n",
        "- No regeneration of embeddings or experimental outputs.\n",
        "- No deletion or replacement of historical audit records.\n",
        "- Only new Phase 5.1 reports may be created.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Audit classifications\n",
        "\n",
        "PASS: Verified requirement.\n",
        "\n",
        "REVIEW: A genuine issue or human verification requirement remains.\n",
        "\n",
        "FAIL: A demonstrated critical integrity failure.\n",
        "\n",
        "NOT VERIFIABLE: Available evidence is insufficient.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Completion condition\n",
        "\n",
        "Phase 5.1 can close only when critical integrity checks pass and remaining scientific or bibliographic review requirements are explicitly resolved or documented.\n",
        "\n",
        "A clean execution log must not be confused with proof of scientific validity.\n"
      ],
